[{"sha":"2407bca66bac5d199a923a0e58872c813eb006bc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDI0MDdiY2E2NmJhYzVkMTk5YTkyM2EwZTU4ODcyYzgxM2ViMDA2YmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T03:26:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T03:26:03Z"},"message":"fix(code): make non-incognito `!` shell output visible to the model (#3825)\n\n`!` shell commands in the TUI now add their command and output to the\nmodel's context as intended; `!!` remains local-only.\n\n---\n\nIn the `deepagents-code` TUI, `!command` (bang-shell) runs as a local\nsubprocess that bypasses the agent graph. Its command/output were only\nmounted into the UI message store, never written to the LangGraph\ncheckpoint the model reads on the next turn. As a result the documented\n`!` vs `!!` contract was unmet: `/help` says `!!` runs \"without adding\ncommand/output to model context\" (implying `!` *does*), but in practice\nboth were hidden from the model.\n\nThis adds `_record_shell_in_model_context`, which writes a\n`HumanMessage`/`AIMessage` pair into thread state via `aupdate_state`\n(wrapped in `tracing_context(enabled=False)`, matching the existing\ninterrupt-recovery pattern) for non-incognito `!` only. `!!` (incognito)\nstays local-only. The write is best-effort and no-ops when no\nagent/thread is active.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"20a6885ef10bd632303c7eeadfc616be9c11eb4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/20a6885ef10bd632303c7eeadfc616be9c11eb4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2407bca66bac5d199a923a0e58872c813eb006bc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKNlLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOc0QAAVYwXuS5AWdHVCc9OLZMaGb\ndWnEvsC+Ro6fXWGyBAvaGWPXklMvpaVmIDfZBYsFOjNXYJoDrj7o5zNF79Y6w8AY\nx3nSSCVEc3xAdSyEL61vnd7NMTLbDfE5/x8e22fslU2TvT3VNqLJIrxAeFtxwQUz\nPRJhelXQtedN4X7MkOZYeshRjXNvzW9jPDm38gFl7RYH7kLEQsLKrQ1bDyemu2Fd\nbFE/SoBLLSfWJ1HmewJLyd4ReyqMmBEdN2LTrq3t0Ed+N6oaGn5zYud1BiyFbdzY\nItCWIg5L2bI68BydhZh++sv46GsWK5rAY2bFFLW4ReKo7P4J8KIiaot7xxVZdD7y\ntW6FgEaF0NYh1FNS1Ciif4Cwu43pdtvyn4GhXS4IO/Od8Pt8Cab9T1qNkBuxR3pT\nSWLMDp5kMtawkOIygzyY38j8pwmta8SSWKiM49fIBQesyF/nH8uuxXdAq6+8K96E\nxwI4fYXq2XqzerN/liCDSwTooc2LLhz5OU+WXGfFWa9HzgO9uhwSvbn/sZv9P9mC\nol1X+TMRYPRwGzuurLdzxznKOhEU4KCeOA2GnEbahr2XjxrzwejWi/9Ey/zdGxDm\nc3WupHw6Y/aRfkt97HIv53P1QIDOgyGPIDHHX76CYiMSSJCcNe17CBnEWTncvuKI\nvXesob10e6jlbUEadxmv\n=DQj2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 20a6885ef10bd632303c7eeadfc616be9c11eb4c\nparent 51a29f4a0c28c122acae296a0df03bee20474455\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781061963 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781061963 -0400\n\nfix(code): make non-incognito `!` shell output visible to the model (#3825)\n\n`!` shell commands in the TUI now add their command and output to the\nmodel's context as intended; `!!` remains local-only.\n\n---\n\nIn the `deepagents-code` TUI, `!command` (bang-shell) runs as a local\nsubprocess that bypasses the agent graph. Its command/output were only\nmounted into the UI message store, never written to the LangGraph\ncheckpoint the model reads on the next turn. As a result the documented\n`!` vs `!!` contract was unmet: `/help` says `!!` runs \"without adding\ncommand/output to model context\" (implying `!` *does*), but in practice\nboth were hidden from the model.\n\nThis adds `_record_shell_in_model_context`, which writes a\n`HumanMessage`/`AIMessage` pair into thread state via `aupdate_state`\n(wrapped in `tracing_context(enabled=False)`, matching the existing\ninterrupt-recovery pattern) for non-incognito `!` only. `!!` (incognito)\nstays local-only. The write is best-effort and no-ops when no\nagent/thread is active.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T03:26:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2407bca66bac5d199a923a0e58872c813eb006bc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2407bca66bac5d199a923a0e58872c813eb006bc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2407bca66bac5d199a923a0e58872c813eb006bc/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"51a29f4a0c28c122acae296a0df03bee20474455","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/51a29f4a0c28c122acae296a0df03bee20474455","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/51a29f4a0c28c122acae296a0df03bee20474455"}]},{"sha":"51a29f4a0c28c122acae296a0df03bee20474455","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDUxYTI5ZjRhMGMyOGMxMjJhY2FlMjk2YTBkZjAzYmVlMjA0NzQ0NTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T03:04:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T03:04:36Z"},"message":"feat(code): persist `/threads` directory-scope preference (#3824)\n\n## Description\nThe `/threads` switcher reset its \"current directory / all directories\"\nscope on every open. This persists the scope to config (under\n`[threads].scope`), mirroring the existing `sort_order` and\n`relative_time` preferences, so the picker reopens with the user's last\nchoice.\n\n## Release Note\nThe `/threads` switcher now remembers your \"current directory / all\ndirectories\" filter across sessions.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Open `/threads`, switch to \"All directories\", close and reopen —\nit stays on \"All directories\".\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e32043f343de6639ae48c2d6db364bef5061e1f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e32043f343de6639ae48c2d6db364bef5061e1f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/51a29f4a0c28c122acae296a0df03bee20474455","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKNRECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2r0QABGgbqPkNeYspS0+R6gxe5Xh\n4OywxFumtR00o7KhRclx6CzDwW98stOy9IKroPeWOfH3RQM+3ZmsqpZdCr7/0cym\nDW3he42AZlcvuuROFsD945ueY1z/XoskjV9G7mqKln66mLwNKZrWdsFPw/5vDcPX\nfUWuHtRgrCfih/SH00/MpIr1nSS6h9r7Mbr8mDKg+AdH+5Xxs8i8CGGKpxEKTI4v\n7BvBAIOBHaBfVdZHWVZP5s5JIMYqxpNRRNj/Gv6Cd+aeoWyFM8SnKlep+zauBbOZ\nyuFaNJ4t+/GfiZiR0IPzjzt7s3tPWnCWccMU4TJWlSYzcFvbJMdPmFHmyODGSZWu\nHm6Qzgo5+ZDBL4s2pQRUauVf/pE/ia9V4WYJtRnp8o0kLqUJOIHcR6GEwzOiNqwV\nYOlCcjWmbUng2B/uCw4RqgrMbsJVXFre8gtWIXVjgn2JNhAst8JFJCz9DsOE5RnP\nybWId+YuXtzjUXiLif4PXY8pHkWsAp6aaN5T6GDvBHl16BXYkXV4nAvhurJe9F7B\nwgeoqYuDePVi7Z0+MkCkcqnM0BAsbTdfn0grfuSSMl5wjQ8P3BsvxBw49SL7bxJ1\nDoD5dujGfYoCb3v4X2BJYCkPrYRK5ixeVitj42ESXaxSl5T6DiGST4LCM7JWqbZp\nGA4UgdQd7SjbiLPUKPKP\n=h0kJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e32043f343de6639ae48c2d6db364bef5061e1f6\nparent 366cd81269e2d3891a477848b774cf51af0cefc0\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781060676 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781060676 -0400\n\nfeat(code): persist `/threads` directory-scope preference (#3824)\n\n## Description\nThe `/threads` switcher reset its \"current directory / all directories\"\nscope on every open. This persists the scope to config (under\n`[threads].scope`), mirroring the existing `sort_order` and\n`relative_time` preferences, so the picker reopens with the user's last\nchoice.\n\n## Release Note\nThe `/threads` switcher now remembers your \"current directory / all\ndirectories\" filter across sessions.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Open `/threads`, switch to \"All directories\", close and reopen —\nit stays on \"All directories\".\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T03:04:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/51a29f4a0c28c122acae296a0df03bee20474455","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/51a29f4a0c28c122acae296a0df03bee20474455","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/51a29f4a0c28c122acae296a0df03bee20474455/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"366cd81269e2d3891a477848b774cf51af0cefc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/366cd81269e2d3891a477848b774cf51af0cefc0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/366cd81269e2d3891a477848b774cf51af0cefc0"}]},{"sha":"366cd81269e2d3891a477848b774cf51af0cefc0","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM2NmNkODEyNjllMmQzODkxYTQ3Nzg0OGI3NzRjZjUxYWYwY2VmYzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T02:46:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T02:46:21Z"},"message":"fix(code): unblock TUI input during `/restart` (#3826)\n\n## Description\n`/restart` froze the TUI input field because `ServerProcess.restart()`\nran the synchronous `_stop_process` (which blocks up to\n`_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT` waiting on `process.wait`) directly on the Textual\nevent loop. Offloading the stop to a worker thread via\n`asyncio.to_thread` keeps the reactor responsive.\n\n## Release Note\nFixed `/restart` in dcode freezing the input field while the server\nsubprocess shut down.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Run `/restart` in dcode and confirm the input field stays\nresponsive while the server restarts.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f7aa4bc33b123c73764c51d7283d46f65b7add1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9f7aa4bc33b123c73764c51d7283d46f65b7add1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/366cd81269e2d3891a477848b774cf51af0cefc0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKM/9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWaoQAIS4bx3nOafXp5Vh0RTwD8iz\nM5rJwCgS+Eh7XxBAANd5ZhQdxF4nrdCItjbOvpPZgMb/mPnHDt5hGW89+Vad+ob2\nNFVeku3SYN4fPhWYhnYoR9tIn5Ja8EyP4VH6LmN+T+28z/mp85gJE7AbxhvJxX8V\nos1MUBYIys+Y144ny1TajsPQbNrOdZMYj43Jd1bab9h3t4DaMJwy5ozm2GxG65n+\npOXnJBcQ08z7ec0GAn+R3ZHzxnonylx6i72GNnDQwTBT5JxGFXF9TuyiwXPVmXDt\nS6jaFsPWLuHAQb1tBrtzRENlAVzMH3TQP1CDcuBBFPx+wVaTQdPpoJ0kT+6Vd3yd\nQLWKmnu0nirRA6hP008raXGr8aB3lJbrypshvdxaOhK8IX6Kk9DHyv+qRwqfgOd4\nyOxjHvcSNdFVui0/E/8umApk9SnL3n4Ptc0J0UubUJ0dy4NH6PDmbtkPNo3Xl4ER\n5/Iz3In+jgdEEe+Ve+JIUPke9xfFcsV748llm2Lg+KCuKZi67gTLwd1nDM0X4KuD\nAWJoKn0EwjtR22h6N7oLWqbDuOZOra3l2vkB60Md0Shzi55z5cy5k/FIF4/bWl1u\nLyr271bJI8pl8uZ9jFBrZ7wD9fVtlTwzADSRpT172/8X1JYgWfuoRlRPk0PPTDI+\ntIb7ZKW+BWq2/7iTdtFQ\n=wJrO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9f7aa4bc33b123c73764c51d7283d46f65b7add1\nparent 49ded9ef448dcd263bee07ac15f4904dd342bfa2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781059581 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781059581 -0400\n\nfix(code): unblock TUI input during `/restart` (#3826)\n\n## Description\n`/restart` froze the TUI input field because `ServerProcess.restart()`\nran the synchronous `_stop_process` (which blocks up to\n`_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT` waiting on `process.wait`) directly on the Textual\nevent loop. Offloading the stop to a worker thread via\n`asyncio.to_thread` keeps the reactor responsive.\n\n## Release Note\nFixed `/restart` in dcode freezing the input field while the server\nsubprocess shut down.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Run `/restart` in dcode and confirm the input field stays\nresponsive while the server restarts.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T02:46:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/366cd81269e2d3891a477848b774cf51af0cefc0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/366cd81269e2d3891a477848b774cf51af0cefc0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/366cd81269e2d3891a477848b774cf51af0cefc0/comments","author":