e7dc4b6d990d7490540dbbae0170fcfaac550ed\nparent 97a7052b3eef7ec80bc90a4c3b606deeaf13cb9b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781058875 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781058875 -0400\n\nfix(code): clarify `/restart` message during server startup (#3823)\n\n`/restart` during server startup now reports that the server is still\nstarting instead of falsely claiming a remote-server connection.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T02:34:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/49ded9ef448dcd263bee07ac15f4904dd342bfa2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/49ded9ef448dcd263bee07ac15f4904dd342bfa2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/49ded9ef448dcd263bee07ac15f4904dd342bfa2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"97a7052b3eef7ec80bc90a4c3b606deeaf13cb9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/97a7052b3eef7ec80bc90a4c3b606deeaf13cb9b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/97a7052b3eef7ec80bc90a4c3b606deeaf13cb9b"}]},{"sha":"97a7052b3eef7ec80bc90a4c3b606deeaf13cb9b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk3YTcwNTJiM2VlZjdlYzgwYmM5MGE0YzNiNjA2ZGVlYWYxM2NiOWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T02:16:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T02:16:22Z"},"message":"fix(code): handle MCP tool errors locally (#3830)\n\nUndo earlier `_ToolExceptionRecoveryMiddleware`.\n\nRecoverable MCP tool failures now stay inside the `StructuredTool` error\nhandler instead of relying on global agent middleware. This keeps MCP\n`isError` results, transient retry failures, and re-auth signals visible\nto the model as `ToolMessage(status=\"error\")` while avoiding broad\nagent-level `ToolException` recovery.\n\n## Changes\n- Removed `_ToolExceptionRecoveryMiddleware` from the main agent and\nimplicit subagent middleware stacks, so agent-level tool execution no\nlonger catches every `ToolException`.\n- Wired cached MCP tools to use adapter-owned `_handle_mcp_tool_error`\ndirectly through `_handle_cached_mcp_tool_error`, with warning logs and\nfallback text for recoverable wrapper failures the adapter does not\nformat.\n- Simplified cached MCP result conversion to call\n`_convert_call_tool_result`, leaving MCP `isError=True` handling in the\ntool-local `handle_tool_error` callback.\n- Updated MCP session failure behavior so repeated transient failures,\ngeneric wrapper failures, and re-auth signals return error-status\n`ToolMessage`s when invoked as tool calls.","tree":{"sha":"28eda51ce799b49a724b77dac26aa828fbd8fa8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/28eda51ce799b49a724b77dac26aa828fbd8fa8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/97a7052b3eef7ec80bc90a4c3b606deeaf13cb9b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKMj2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATHkQACG03x+eM0++A9iQNVdoEZP7\nwmdbBd50d70wuJTISu3B5xwvs3L+bR8lSP7XKvKtWAoh8PguF50YBN9iYFVt3aRV\n6TzRz4afaoe1pcUlKFVk/uA6Y9Pbh8Cjq9/4P+gZDPqOpOTgN44K1mgzaOkONNDW\nBFWVJdPR/FyXGgdH7Vb4uZ0C2TM18I1U22c/VmCG+AjRakGxzEG8NOE9zLXzyV8B\nPd0O538kxThbaPfkCuFFQYpbcu7n5RzJ5PljyulKrvUfN231amNLqU7P5oTWJXMM\nnxk9gUGBznB/gvKpTrJ2JSb4NmwXeFVZfXwevZrAkv/xtFodBW0vAJmQ9I9oZrL+\nVlTKCcHPVNVIAOxdj4gXBd1w0RWze2fMejoBNPJI8EppIme+W6vG8Z1sOeQ4p/Da\nQJ7hBx1jGGWOPZOgZnn7K4edu9UAXfXSClJ8T9bNRZfofxZRjdh+us0H8m63anQK\nnkxkbexFZlL/bGbi/fDBMA6tXRHG6UIDIjLI5/ll+PKB0HjWG5w3wLYI4fbXQA+J\nUl/39jCyWdy2evaIV6JejepKTR9xpgXMlcICxYGq9dLr2Hsdpbp4yXbMsrXkUE0q\n01Ukuh2FMXNxyzhG32tZRSL4/Ib35MzdHwo+J3ud67MAFHs3ufylHAPAb3hScAnk\nAQiaKE8cWIj9ghlmF9d/\n=6DPW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 28eda51ce799b49a724b77dac26aa828fbd8fa8d\nparent a3ef13314f36464ec6a02c7b56783795fb87e32b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781057782 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781057782 -0400\n\nfix(code): handle MCP tool errors locally (#3830)\n\nUndo earlier `_ToolExceptionRecoveryMiddleware`.\n\nRecoverable MCP tool failures now stay inside the `StructuredTool` error\nhandler instead of relying on global agent middleware. This keeps MCP\n`isError` results, transient retry failures, and re-auth signals visible\nto the model as `ToolMessage(status=\"error\")` while avoiding broad\nagent-level `ToolException` recovery.\n\n## Changes\n- Removed `_ToolExceptionRecoveryMiddleware` from the main agent and\nimplicit subagent middleware stacks, so agent-level tool execution no\nlonger catches every `ToolException`.\n- Wired cached MCP tools to use adapter-owned `_handle_mcp_tool_error`\ndirectly through `_handle_cached_mcp_tool_error`, with warning logs and\nfallback text for recoverable wrapper failures the adapter does not\nformat.\n- Simplified cached MCP result conversion to call\n`_convert_call_tool_result`, leaving MCP `isError=True` handling in the\ntool-local `handle_tool_error` callback.\n- Updated MCP session failure behavior so repeated transient failures,\ngeneric wrapper failures, and re-auth signals return error-status\n`ToolMessage`s when invoked as tool calls.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T02:16:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/97a7052b3eef7ec80bc90a4c3b606deeaf13cb9b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/97a7052b3eef7ec80bc90a4c3b606deeaf13cb9b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/97a7052b3eef7ec80bc90a4c3b606deeaf13cb9b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a3ef13314f36464ec6a02c7b56783795fb87e32b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a3ef13314f36464ec6a02c7b56783795fb87e32b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a3ef13314f36464ec6a02c7b56783795fb87e32b"}]},{"sha":"a3ef13314f36464ec6a02c7b56783795fb87e32b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGEzZWYxMzMxNGYzNjQ2NGVjNmEwMmM3YjU2NzgzNzk1ZmI4N2UzMmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T02:15:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T02:15:40Z"},"message":"docs(code): document local `dcode-dev` setup (#3831)\n\nAdded the local development install pattern for keeping the released\n`dcode` tool separate from an editable `dcode-dev` environment. The\nguide covers how to create the dedicated venv, wire the symlink, update\ndependencies when constraints change, and verify that the editable\nimport resolves to the checkout.","tree":{"sha":"5b4df9f0c6b2abc41e6f2b20f46b70715de359d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5b4df9f0c6b2abc41e6f2b20f46b70715de359d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a3ef13314f36464ec6a02c7b56783795fb87e32b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKMjMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWJUQAIZnRYJs0WVeFlCcVQJTXEvq\nK2O1Ur0gdUwaOaHMFhRrzkhtfG85DKkeEsjPQBSaT6nDEFA2RhVCqhI0+z4cAoez\nogQlcRe7vo9US5g7EEYm2BXuWhcHeKRpRQ1COGhLvvOkWT5+/FNlLAz7RXmOsoY+\nGvbXYy0WI8dfIm+eL7AkzW6qhQFZ3HbB3K+PesgHW/oRIjlbznC7FehbCKObQg4w\nUtVq80AdLe0k0OR+pq+wLSXWj1KZ2oBKfOwBnasf8HmyF7lxWYvIl8qrL4+pAlix\nYwJLmXGxu0MEdz1FIN2+tdoCqpYTMtUZmgXHt44P7/oUb7ICjTcCI5SuEyw4QU+a\nAsky6hh3VdMxPz5G5sjONhrotpVEJ1s0qF7Lv5j/e04hdRyV0/pIRgb080LDl4Ir\nMS7D68+hsm5flgSvoYG9u/3J54SZcurngv/zhJXMK+HfU65srL5UjgJrjusbv4OC\nD37utH3b1nIi005tm+icDqFMrz5Y7bvcm+pl8LDH2cIO4KRAZYMgF3Fv+j14y2jx\nJR5ztaXtLNtE2l0VJ4q2rW4erxc7fVGlBwQkiVFHoU8mhYVIqciRkbxwGzs8SO+h\nb7QdIITnpq8G6eH4nlPvoxTIC5jS67qZwnZe04rOlX9BqfnTAbrJpLfDfA5ZN28S\nSz8qSKwaRKWmYpS93nUs\n=tNZn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5b4df9f0c6b2abc41e6f2b20f46b70715de359d0\nparent d83b428f7f97bc40b9219c02846c2d8b4ccac434\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781057740 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781057740 -0400\n\ndocs(code): document local `dcode-dev` setup (#3831)\n\nAdded the local development install pattern for keeping the released\n`dcode` tool separate from an editable `dcode-dev` environment. The\nguide covers how to create the dedicated venv, wire the symlink, update\ndependencies when constraints change, and verify that the editable\nimport resolves to the checkout.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T02:15:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a3ef13314f36464ec6a02c7b56783795fb87e32b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a3ef13314f36464ec6a02c7b56783795fb87e32b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a3ef13314f36464ec6a02c7b56783795fb87e32b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d83b428f7f97bc40b9219c02846c2d8b4ccac434","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d83b428f7f97bc40b9219c02846c2d8b4ccac434","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d83b428f7f97bc40b9219c02846c2d8b4ccac434"}]},{"sha":"d83b428f7f97bc40b9219c02846c2d8b4ccac434","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ4M2I0MjhmN2Y5N2JjNDBiOTIxOWMwMjg0NmMyZDhiNGNjYWM0MzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T01:44:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T01:44:34Z"},"message":"fix(code): surface cached MCP errors as failed tool messages (#3829)\n\nCached-session MCP tools now match `langchain-mcp-adapters` 0.3 behavior\nfor MCP execution errors: `CallToolResult(isError=True)` is returned to\nthe model as a failed tool result instead of escaping as a raised\n`ToolException`. Transport, session, retry, and reauth failures keep\ntheir existing exception paths, while the generic recovery middleware\nremains documented as a compatibility fallback for\nnon-MCP/tool-originated `ToolException`s.","tree":{"sha":"1ad5014e97de4062fa3f579a83c97a3b59a5f07c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1ad5014e97de4062fa3f579a83c97a3b59a5f07c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d83b428f7f97bc40b9219c02846c2d8b4ccac434","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKMGCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjuQQAG17QeD3qvc/C4mipSCWCdiH\nwh4e/skjMJSfuSEtw07gmSdQIU2xdOEcbk1mkpYCNxGByQMThEFQn1JzScE+FfAE\n8mWt6VO+dUXjo/owFez+Ve45KMPYZ5Bg8C3YRl/tDQ0m4zp9BmDaQRYrr7SIj6Ac\nI9cfakzni/0GADgLk7l9m7/kQ2XALDFRKoXZYdChSCDt6Halua7bcPQgWjUcwfCq\nobv6SkxSySKC0DwLDfkhFwan30d/P8UWTrkoHhaRg849YFLxDxHbtPdPj71sfsT0\nLS/Q23UATDMTM+YgYKuwHPfxcqfA5K1SR/tE2zaU/MQVUu333chKY5s29Z8Y8mE1\nuOK2QmjCEyOcxUChKgxvbCQHD5mQgOQrMK+AplC74mwZc8Gbb3O5nQW0bSUoxFnO\nSxGlQIAPfKUzX37jpk5etn++fLCCnXHdEzaeVRZQkiMi+0QKlUdW8mWNPzF8Ocuz\nsvNA3uag/FtjmlLccH6iuyQVrTSksochgUacWGFT2MH7Z4WpE7nSoINEzgUVBb4S\nba3cTjvvGAdZckDeYbzm9N2OrfW7vUs7AyhAG4j+TddFLUPoqAHQiW8YfHtUO5y7\nOVi2nHlwbczLuyPTSHkIjrEaBUrEYdAVMKuYvAbUSTISzgnpkOMtjP5xKvmgt1ID\nThm5u8P6PSg9/BXj7y0p\n=FDb0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1ad5014e97de4062fa3f579a83c97a3b59a5f07c\nparent 7d887bd71fbf13076bdf8fed51b63232a6fd65a4\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781055874 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781055874 -0400\n\nfix(code): surface cached MCP errors as failed tool messages (#3829)\n\nCached-session MCP tools now match `langchain-mcp-adapters` 0.3 behavior\nfor MCP execution errors: `CallToolResult(isError=True)` is returned to\nthe model as a failed tool result instead of escaping as a raised\n`ToolException`. Transport, session, retry, and reauth failures keep\ntheir existing exception paths, while the generic recovery middleware\nremains documented as a compatibility fallback for\nnon-MCP/tool-originated `ToolException`s.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T01:44:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d83b428f7f97bc40b9219c02846c2d8b4ccac434","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d83b428f7f97bc40b9219c02846c2d8b4ccac434","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d83b428f7f97bc40b9219c02846c2d8b4ccac434/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7d887bd71fbf13076bdf8fed51b63232a6fd65a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d887bd71fbf13076bdf8fed51b63232a6fd65a4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7d887bd71fbf13076bdf8fed51b63232a6fd65a4"}]},{"sha":"7d887bd71fbf13076bdf8fed51b63232a6fd65a4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdkODg3YmQ3MWZiZjEzMDc2YmRmOGZlZDUxYjYzMjMyYTZmZDY1YTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T01:31:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T01:31:46Z"},"message":"chore(sdk): update summarization trigger compatibility (#3828)\n\nDeep Agents now pins to the LangChain release that owns the updated\nsummarization trigger representation used by the underlying\n`LCSummarizationMiddleware`. This is primarily a compatibility update\nfor the Deep Agents summarization wrapper and compact-tool eligibility,\nnot a broad new public configuration surface for `create_deep_agent`.\n\n## Changes\n- Raised the SDK's minimum `langchain` dependency to `>=1.3.6`, where\nLangChain stores and evaluates summarization triggers as dict clauses.\n- Kept `LCSummarizationMiddleware` as the source of truth for validating\n`trigger`/`keep`, storing `_trigger_clauses`, token counting setup, and\ndeciding when automatic summarization should run.\n- Passed `trigger` directly through `SummarizationMiddleware` so direct\nwrapper users can use LangChain's supported trigger shapes without Deep\nAgents mirroring that logic.\n- Removed the temporary SDK-side trigger normalization and evaluation\nshim that was only needed while the LangChain release was blocked on\nDeep Agents tests.","tree":{"sha":"29640482282f388729e934c91b83820d148f7574","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/29640482282f388729e934c91b83820d148f7574"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7d887bd71fbf13076bdf8fed51b63232a6fd65a4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKL6CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmJQQAEG86LB1Ys/ettV3a0KvSAnK\nkM/HpZU3D6hXKoP8MF7Q2Dp9eVamO3nlZ42Q+CegcnujWKhqe5pdBj20j6SNH0gB\nOfTCzfNxGTE5Y7UVyGyaNmvt9yH/+uPVrFH6M3Xj2N3w8YRuGn05ZWBUUo+rgXgp\nR/Xq2DYXzHCWIpW32a9BTi3vmc0G/+cAPCPJJaXdoF2fYheRqKudxei83nP7gPeX\n8MvhtFDCQ6OmpdbJqCDdmJkit9H0Jr6L79gCKT8AFgvM+9CKQ8RXPERsExKnVVe4\nW0Hrm44gZXOuixwlbXaFYfSHB609FWkp5lKm2g3wgkBUEBb4EBoBta5Cdcxukt15\nyIbizYuY6ule+8Xq7nOjWx+sFnRV6sJuT+oB1kexs4t8e5lyxzHBu+H8QoJAMrjp\nacTfXNBlJTmn+hzfTrjCV9VaRTDPnu3aJGqcfgF6nf7vcb+j963T7VFr644Fe5SJ\neam9/lNUQh4128j2toOLA0mNk4huKxph/CB+YZe2FqMQ+90aH0frWgqchsSfsb8T\ndY5/6A2Xhvhlym0d8DeG5RbVWCRuoxRGV6WYFg17010MPkgRm6qoLaZ301SrU7Tt\nln0y4Z6ViuZ91V46Zfxb+yEhjNHAIs3cgMN4E2M1DSgPmnV7HmHq0wQHiT3JDn+1\ncCdXrKiQ2WUmLjP1M12T\n=4dC8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 29640482282f388729e934c91b83820d148f7574\nparent dc0a51fc81d01b62dc8043148a9fd87099fc9123\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781055106 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781055106 -0400\n\nchore(sdk): update summarization trigger compatibility (#3828)\n\nDeep Agents now pins to the LangChain release that owns the updated\nsummarization trigger representation used by the underlying\n`LCSummarizationMiddleware`. This is primarily a compatibility update\nfor the Deep Agents summarization wrapper and compact-tool eligibility,\nnot a broad new public configuration surface for `create_deep_agent`.\n\n## Changes\n- Raised the SDK's minimum `langchain` dependency to `>=1.3.6`, where\nLangChain stores and evaluates summarization triggers as dict clauses.\n- Kept `LCSummarizationMiddleware` as the source of truth for validating\n`trigger`/`keep`, storing `_trigger_clauses`, token counting setup, and\ndeciding when automatic summarization should run.\n- Passed `trigger` directly through `SummarizationMiddleware` so direct\nwrapper users can use LangChain's supported trigger shapes without Deep\nAgents mirroring that logic.\n- Removed the temporary SDK-side trigger normalization and evaluation\nshim that was only needed while the LangChain release was blocked on\nDeep Agents tests.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T01:31:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d887bd71fbf13076bdf8fed51b63232a6fd65a4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7d887bd71fbf13076bdf8fed51b63232a6fd65a4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d887bd71fbf13076bdf8fed51b63232a6fd65a4/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dc0a51fc81d01b62dc8043148a9fd87099fc9123","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dc0a51fc81d01b62dc8043148a9fd87099fc9123","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/dc0a51fc81d01b62dc8043148a9fd87099fc9123"}]},{"sha":"dc0a51fc81d01b62dc8043148a9fd87099fc9123","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRjMGE1MWZjODFkMDFiNjJkYzgwNDMxNDhhOWZkODcwOTlmYzkxMjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T00:25:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T00:25:48Z"},"message":"feat(code): guard managed onboarding-name memory block from edits (#3822)\n\nProtect the machine-managed onboarding-name block in the user\n`AGENTS.md` from being overwritten by agent file edits.\n\n---\n\nThe onboarding flow writes the user's preferred name into the user\n`AGENTS.md` inside a block delimited by `deepagents:onboarding-name`\nHTML-comment markers. `MemoryMiddleware` strips HTML comments before\ninjecting memory, so the model never sees those markers — yet the same\nprompt tells it to `edit_file` that file to persist learnings, leaving\nnothing to stop it from rewriting the managed block.\n\nThis adds `ManagedMemoryGuardMiddleware`, a deterministic\n`wrap_tool_call` guard wired into the agent's memory stack. When\n`write_file`/`edit_file` targets the guarded user `AGENTS.md` and\nchanges (or drops) the managed block, the model's other edits are kept\nbut the block is restored to its prior content via the existing\n`_upsert_onboarding_name_memory`, and an error is returned so the model\nlearns the region is machine-managed. Edits that leave the block\nuntouched, reads, and writes to other files pass through unchanged.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Scenario where this applies</summary>\n\nA user has completed onboarding, so their preferred name is stored in\nthe machine-managed block inside their user `AGENTS.md`.\n\nLater, the agent tries to persist a new memory by calling `edit_file` on\nthat file. `ManagedMemoryGuardMiddleware` intercepts the tool call to\nensure the onboarding-name block is not changed. If the agent's edit\ntouches or removes that block, the middleware preserves the agent's\nother edits, restores the onboarding-name block to its previous content,\nand returns an error telling the agent not to modify the machine-managed\nregion.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"667a2e6a8250e2cf0c40956b1eba772271206805","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/667a2e6a8250e2cf0c40956b1eba772271206805"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/dc0a51fc81d01b62dc8043148a9fd87099fc9123","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKK8MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARrsQAD/cD1xu9KPf9EkW7YoanTuf\nPvcJNAib6Reff5RB/ENy7/edBbBHa+XCZVXXlqiJ92wa7fqPTyZnqBYFjTTTOLYj\nXKAJU/zkCD9sQPsybUNo5WKxeOAZpg954wWL4RvC6GYDJL8Jd1ttaW0GZAcpowDo\nRMCyTdurA4HhQ2+kk/cnetGg0+K+dk6eAA+p25dtE9k7vznCTBM0WkUsaIpqDxHZ\nlbCHjHUMNQ/Nvt475NscRfb8b934pTBWw876kwtp90ipW0NL+T1KerLaOjsIqSui\nUnRMY+P0vpCI8wuxfX56z1lH3IBS+3ApqCUynj5dpUw5xgZ62za48Zj6Ulp6gVMX\nRLU8MtBSQqwTYOqS5hAh2RhfoKVVPhPBPkM63esRja6e3yeXofZAuU9O8N9Dlrh0\nieMic/ppUxPpKa8EKAAMfrUj6U5tX9eMzHl5uPqHvxsdcUg7QsL3H8MPqhe7m2aC\nVxDS/baEipwG3ez+Ji5Rv31gYRaZ8NCFUxzcWxzFHBfFB41e6SDE3IAS48rtc0JH\nPFJKoVuM71NvpBty601ju/IRPOgv8s2+VVXP82/8G6tEJLcs+Sn5XhmKC2GCDGnA\nneDd1Qp/KwmqD3MEG8ZfinsyGFRAIltKC7rUSHONHcG6m0+liokQFyiIntBmyjCo\n5IYXIDChnBbnGZbivAGG\n=SEuZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 667a2e6a8250e2cf0c40956b1eba772271206805\nparent 16fee2adc69eaf4e70f61f3d67a55b4dc5af73dc\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781051148 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781051148 -0400\n\nfeat(code): guard managed onboarding-name memory block from edits (#3822)\n\nProtect the machine-managed onboarding-name block in the user\n`AGENTS.md` from being overwritten by agent file edits.\n\n---\n\nThe onboarding flow writes the user's preferred name into the user\n`AGENTS.md` inside a block delimited by `deepagents:onboarding-name`\nHTML-comment markers. `MemoryMiddleware` strips HTML comments before\ninjecting memory, so the model never sees those markers — yet the same\nprompt tells it to `edit_file` that file to persist learnings, leaving\nnothing to stop it from rewriting the managed block.\n\nThis adds `ManagedMemoryGuardMiddleware`, a deterministic\n`wrap_tool_call` guard wired into the agent's memory stack. When\n`write_file`/`edit_file` targets the guarded user `AGENTS.md` and\nchanges (or drops) the managed block, the model's other edits are kept\nbut the block is restored to its prior content via the existing\n`_upsert_onboarding_name_memory`, and an error is returned so the model\nlearns the region is machine-managed. Edits that leave the block\nuntouched, reads, and writes to other files pass through unchanged.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Scenario where this applies</summary>\n\nA user has completed onboarding, so their preferred name is stored in\nthe machine-managed block inside their user `AGENTS.md`.\n\nLater, the agent tries to persist a new memory by calling `edit_file` on\nthat file. `ManagedMemoryGuardMiddleware` intercepts the tool call to\nensure the onboarding-name block is not changed. If the agent's edit\ntouches or removes that block, the middleware preserves the agent's\nother edits, restores the onboarding-name block to its previous content,\nand returns an error telling the agent not to modify the machine-managed\nregion.\n\n</details>\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-10T00:25:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dc0a51fc81d01b62dc8043148a9fd87099fc9123","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/dc0a51fc81d01b62dc8043148a9fd87099fc9123","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dc0a51fc81d01b62dc8043148a9fd87099fc9123/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"16fee2adc69eaf4e70f61f3d67a55b4dc5af73dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/16fee2adc69eaf4e70f61f3d67a55b4dc5af73dc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/16fee2adc69eaf4e70f61f3d67a55b4dc5af73dc"}]},{"sha":"16fee2adc69eaf4e70f61f3d67a55b4dc5af73dc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE2ZmVlMmFkYzY5ZWFmNGU3MGY2MWYzZDY3YTU1YjRkYzVhZjczZGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-10T00:13:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T00:13:34Z"},"message":"hotfix(sdk): support upcoming `SummarizationMiddleware` trigger clauses (#3827)\n\nThis adds a temporary compatibility shim for the upcoming LangChain\n`SummarizationMiddleware` trigger-clause changes.\n\nLangChain is moving `_trigger_conditions` from tuple thresholds to dict\nclauses so triggers can support AND semantics within a clause and OR\nsemantics across clauses. Deep Agents already needs to handle that new\nshape for compact-tool eligibility, but the currently released LangChain\nwheel still rejects dict trigger inputs during middleware construction.\n\nThis keeps Deep Agents compatible with both versions by normalizing\ntriggers locally, passing old tuple-style triggers into older LangChain\nduring construction, and preserving the dict-clause shape for Deep\nAgents' own summarization and compact-tool checks.\n\nThis is intended to unblock the LangChain release. Once Deep Agents can\nraise its minimum LangChain version to a release that includes native\ntrigger-clause support, this shim can be simplified or removed.","tree":{"sha":"1cd0a2cbeb5675d1333d141dd1b590c29255b4ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1cd0a2cbeb5675d1333d141dd1b590c29255b4ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/16fee2adc69eaf4e70f61f3d67a55b4dc5af73dc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKKwuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACDwQAKrt03Si+zHK/FNQE4rrCakC\n/Z4q7P1FCpSCzDY9WjXhMae8ZS8PO6Xf4d/B3DVSJv0w2leK56LN84QD6p0hY+fo\np9TwzIrpKumPpNmlAQn1Vozr6e9Y+xzenU0tGnlvXFG/TJvG62S+3QT2yvBiUrr8\ns9AaDUHqQvZN1/NpMYIA+I53Yu8nfOqjUJ+4mYZfkX0v1U+ypsoQC7qlmYsLM7f4\nVwqvzlHqW+XbLJouK3ik5K8I6ohsK3S3AeXPDRUR3/D8ZdXvdPnJymLlGragre3a\nGw5+vtr0pDZEVKUf1JeiEVd3dHYnFbXx+GncNvGHfgmq4Rz1pd6bVx35MWxxM3Lj\njdHpb3ie65lU1GrhT5w6pGryEjUFTJiKSVereyaqjClx0EN5tP2PUqX3BaWTqGOn\nSajbzQbGkuO4A9QBJ96+H5+lMgEFpTOdXP82ZU32YBumkLkYfjrS0a6lsclUUWgE\ngPcODzlmKpa2/BUFAB8Poqj0DTEtlW9h0tjZsvGXfy3k0WU3kOfU1K+6elWm5grc\n6DDrFNCf8RoZysyG7ct+f4ZmRQ0XFHbHVkjESmRASgHu6VgZWgQwn858AeA1uiGw\n2Jea5wSl5TTyn2eO5Wvyszvbu+yMQGot4UzCi2zmyTm5kC5tyNwx2KDDu7B0ln40\nGuQLdakKg5eIeAtFudcw\n=LyMB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1cd0a2cbeb5675d1333d141dd1b590c29255b4ac\nparent e356efeff1c8bfb894119cebbb7d3c0853d327a2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781050414 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781050414 -0400\n\nhotfix(sdk): support upcoming `SummarizationMiddleware` trigger clauses (#3827)\n\nThis adds a temporary compatibility shim for the upcoming LangChain\n`SummarizationMiddleware` trigger-clause changes.\n\nLangChain is moving `_trigger_conditions` from tuple thresholds to dict\nclauses so triggers can support AND semantics within a clause and OR\nsemantics across clauses. Deep Agents already needs to handle that new\nshape for compact-tool eligibility, but the currently released LangChain\nwheel still rejects dict trigger inputs during middleware construction.\n\nThis keeps Deep Agents compatible with both versions by normalizing\ntriggers locally, passing old tuple-style triggers into older LangChain\nduring construction, and preserving the dict-clause shape for Deep\nAgents' own summarization and compact-tool checks.\n\nThis is intended to unblock the LangChain release. Once Deep Agents can\nraise its minimum LangChain version to a release that includes native\ntrigger-clause support, this shim can be simplified or removed.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T00:13:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/16fee2adc69eaf4e70f61f3d67a55b4dc5af73dc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/16fee2adc69eaf4e70f61f3d67a55b4dc5af73dc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/16fee2adc69eaf4e70f61f3d67a55b4dc5af73dc/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e356efeff1c8bfb894119cebbb7d3c0853d327a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e356efeff1c8bfb894119cebbb7d3c0853d327a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e356efeff1c8bfb894119cebbb7d3c0853d327a2"}]},{"sha":"e356efeff1c8bfb894119cebbb7d3c0853d327a2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGUzNTZlZmVmZjFjOGJmYjg5NDExOWNlYmJiN2QzYzA4NTNkMzI3YTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-09T23:00:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T23:00:12Z"},"message":"feat(code): offer restart after restart-capable install (#3821)\n\n`/install` now offers to restart the server immediately after installing\na provider/sandbox extra or package, instead of requiring a manual\n`/restart`.\n\n---\n\nAfter a successful provider/sandbox extra or `--package` install, the\nuser still has to type `/restart` to load it. Since dcode already owns\nthe server subprocess and knows whether it's idle, this offers a\none-keypress \"Restart now?\" prompt that runs the existing restart path.\nIt falls back to the current manual hint during an active run (a restart\ncancels it) and in remote-server mode (no subprocess to respawn).\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7ad221c078e98a5d700a7e1659d7dbf6fd5944ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7ad221c078e98a5d700a7e1659d7dbf6fd5944ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e356efeff1c8bfb894119cebbb7d3c0853d327a2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKJr9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQl8QAIiT43xcCf6AK1Ux5obKiUG8\nWzY6oF1VD6u6o/05/mgJ6XKuO/Vpt9Kdfz6z+LikI2XErL+6taVOxjCG0PCYumEN\nKRBtsZ+WWUoPeuN7msWwYG55jTRb8APtw24hROoXQB9sJAR32415PVx96N+8uZG/\nSAKAASYRQedgudgO5wi3vZNVIz3B+HqCbMfoaITZQJQK+CjFEV8HADFnhaaPFzVJ\nq8a7+yRDXFaDburebFB0IdxvM7/ec9xepjtwZiI4QTeT0pf8oPL4eoG9oGadYD+H\npx/9ItlhggVpVo83AOmjupglCMvLnpSdFHMs9OyuFXWPB7mY4eKAvAeJu0hED5Ik\n54e/1yfMoYdNjKYO3wjS4wMLxW7Vbb6lYHdzNnGmuQBWc7VhkNBD0bkUmBicX0ZB\nPclkA+6L1IRvSRMj40QuQE7S543cKki0Gk8b4/U0loI6xfygeyN2eRMDewCtRHZ0\nAO74uOQP0p3I2zuDth/fVI0xRITny9Rzq0EeVhOVmMLXTvbR0oAZLTqb5y6iVUVH\n9ov6mT+YiIfSD51EpfU4oYKz3Dpxn86KhyaatGxwIA4iupGT9kKY74v3Ly5hFLyd\nk4M8bZhNBvj2FUvNQ5v0BpBlhf9SCCz65RiM+YtbOxYsPH6DkAR5CH0cR1d/ZR45\nr4pAGsk6NMYgf2ZPyqM1\n=njmD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7ad221c078e98a5d700a7e1659d7dbf6fd5944ba\nparent 18ce094b7036796c7e23ce1338f4da56dc2ef126\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781046012 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781046012 -0400\n\nfeat(code): offer restart after restart-capable install (#3821)\n\n`/install` now offers to restart the server immediately after installing\na provider/sandbox extra or package, instead of requiring a manual\n`/restart`.\n\n---\n\nAfter a successful provider/sandbox extra or `--package` install, the\nuser still has to type `/restart` to load it. Since dcode already owns\nthe server subprocess and knows whether it's idle, this offers a\none-keypress \"Restart now?\" prompt that runs the existing restart path.\nIt falls back to the current manual hint during an active run (a restart\ncancels it) and in remote-server mode (no subprocess to respawn).\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-09T23:00:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e356efeff1c8bfb894119cebbb7d3c0853d327a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e356efeff1c8bfb894119cebbb7d3c0853d327a2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e356efeff1c8bfb894119cebbb7d3c0853d327a2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"18ce094b7036796c7e23ce1338f4da56dc2ef126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/18ce094b7036796c7e23ce1338f4da56dc2ef126","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/18ce094b7036796c7e23ce1338f4da56dc2ef126"}]},{"sha":"18ce094b7036796c7e23ce1338f4da56dc2ef126","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE4Y2UwOTRiNzAzNjc5NmM3ZTIzY2UxMzM4ZjRkYTU2ZGMyZWYxMjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-09T22:35:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T22:35:04Z"},"message":"feat(code): add `get_current_thread_id` tool (#3820)\n\nAdds a `get_current_thread_id` agent tool to `deepagents-code` so models\ncan retrieve the active LangGraph thread ID and pass it to thread-scoped\ntooling like the LangSmith CLI or an MCP server. The tool reads\n`configurable.thread_id` from the injected `RunnableConfig` (so it takes\nno model-visible arguments) and returns an explanatory message when no\nthread ID is available. It is wired into the tool lists for both ACP\nmode (`main.py`) and the server graph (`server_graph.py`).\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ddf185ae70bdb09ed06d73293479c766c790c7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6ddf185ae70bdb09ed06d73293479c766c790c7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/18ce094b7036796c7e23ce1338f4da56dc2ef126","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKJUYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfUoQAGTqOClOwAlRgQQGlr7IFMlY\nxvyZC79byk07j0nFNYbk2aIQ8ghbBY0neIlhIt18CfX4Ift3WidfvoBMsCJbYtfd\npOVbet7XcLF5UAtpdj36brQxldhMth/FhKigibwNUtOuWDGj1KS0gmoroTiVI0vJ\nlptM74Rzn52pCk+EoQVC2yQG4j+WwS9DUkJ8x1NLSHpIcznu9Jo5PmzYwjqc1tJl\nC08ZGi0FskkUpM4tC6Xpi6OLj345AWYSgoZW7Gg3NmB0N5TPLvOeRrCfsWhUMAlL\nyBTTauFdWSYZIbl8kXpnWhfGdTB3G14oMAqHWxkSx7WGARARmVNJIH2slxbIxh+U\nmc/vdq4ArZ6HvUW7v2hO6CuuSwpaLwLAoEqXXXG3yZnBqH6SNP/aOmVToFRvjbTR\neWT/IjnyPOUjmWbT9D88iKeols244UUKkTigfYYkX7QB9wU5nW55HSS2K1h0bnY0\n+4fAoSLnb681MtDGjJU7JFJuhCcJnpxLBAKojzolvcdSRRQBPQyqAIRyJRTDUelo\nPQiKgHuvUXTCv0J4Z0Hz0yqpDW4E/z/fANRw/xhIZXgQOVa/REpiNJ331CAhyl/4\n086izDyDMkFwP4qm3O7dhTLVO2TdZPth3c+1ReEllsqYEuVYDthTA/b0n/Ly6+Me\n/BkFWu0tyWmX0z2GFlyn\n=Ntze\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6ddf185ae70bdb09ed06d73293479c766c790c7d\nparent d417f530aafa8c77523487393dc3039cc822dc09\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781044504 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781044504 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add `get_current_thread_id` tool (#3820)\n\nAdds a `get_current_thread_id` agent tool to `deepagents-code` so models\ncan retrieve the active LangGraph thread ID and pass it to thread-scoped\ntooling like the LangSmith CLI or an MCP server. The tool reads\n`configurable.thread_id` from the injected `RunnableConfig` (so it takes\nno model-visible arguments) and returns an explanatory message when no\nthread ID is available. It is wired into the tool lists for both ACP\nmode (`main.py`) and the server graph (`server_graph.py`).\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-09T22:35:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/18ce094b7036796c7e23ce1338f4da56dc2ef126","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/18ce094b7036796c7e23ce1338f4da56dc2ef126","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/18ce094b7036796c7e23ce1338f4da56dc2ef126/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d417f530aafa8c77523487393dc3039cc822dc09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d417f530aafa8c77523487393dc3039cc822dc09","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d417f530aafa8c77523487393dc3039cc822dc09"}]},{"sha":"d417f530aafa8c77523487393dc3039cc822dc09","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ0MTdmNTMwYWFmYThjNzc1MjM0ODczOTNkYzMwMzljYzgyMmRjMDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-09T22:34:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T22:34:55Z"},"message":"fix(code): offer cwd switch on resume (#3810)\n\nPrompt users when resuming a thread whose stored cwd differs from the\ncurrent cwd, warning that staying can stale local context and tool\nbehavior. Accepting the switch updates cwd-aware UI state and, for\nin-app thread switches, replaces the app-owned server so the backend\nuses the resumed thread's cwd.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"44c793c8d5a35afb4f444cc80271c6e994012989","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/44c793c8d5a35afb4f444cc80271c6e994012989"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d417f530aafa8c77523487393dc3039cc822dc09","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKJUPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJM0QAHL38UjsHE+XnHyVkbAA+84W\n5YqolZwrxIkVlBp8iVY4HC/CqcWn/0/RhGSIcgApE6joONWjBHQZawY+CJbYGUyd\nF8GZlDxJxWU31zwvEIOEyKplbJ2BJmkN5OKpAOeevgYoiFO4G3nGVnEd5z7N8QtC\nd51XcZNAhEKIrFA+eMGxfGDpdkJgooJFzmEuLxKV2P5UdPvu3crkBsk86P/qnHcE\noppSTkJKvW2lExmWXFi/cNZAe4iBBVodKyRwXZnrTPnrSlmlqsS+iThe8eL/j3Pf\nYlRHcx0KvLcmxjuiEAbo/FolRrI5xLrNofBinhgFF6F3k+rqlLzKcNXbaKZrX90Z\nYcmzUuXu9eD2I9f95ycZOOj7z1BsrGa7uTwsxReRVGifQply1CP0l4/KzGQFpJrL\nsLuA464NelL88+Ej1gZK5Zk3lSFdh9IEuNllIzDLihjYDmuOmdYtn/UxHEtVL0tc\nJkAJx9mSyScMPMluvJtw5sWYmMo0bhf6g6ynmS+H19/3BhHVmyztmZ47QkAYl7gN\nUJi0sw9Zvd05VKIdjNxpN9nehQdPc3xJ5OcjBDB1tXga2fKYyBya5g9+NdKJsVlh\nWgtNHRhHBkmIV8e/LP1l8WUfbs9mCDv5Z15whIbAgZpOiMZc2935AMIkPw8Hssh6\nup545DEF274p+g0VpVbb\n=KChM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 44c793c8d5a35afb4f444cc80271c6e994012989\nparent 71a6d508b21b275c0c7c6bd2e0752adfba496ea9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781044495 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781044495 -0400\n\nfix(code): offer cwd switch on resume (#3810)\n\nPrompt users when resuming a thread whose stored cwd differs from the\ncurrent cwd, warning that staying can stale local context and tool\nbehavior. Accepting the switch updates cwd-aware UI state and, for\nin-app thread switches, replaces the app-owned server so the backend\nuses the resumed thread's cwd.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-09T22:34:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d417f530aafa8c77523487393dc3039cc822dc09","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d417f530aafa8c77523487393dc3039cc822dc09","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d417f530aafa8c77523487393dc3039cc822dc09/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starre