 SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8d673f4782189d523ef238fa279214e4cc583f27\nparent 5bd1ef8cb29db781ccbb37755db44ce0ab1d7bd2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781032224 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781032224 -0400\n\nfix(code): expose `/restart` slash command (#3809)\n\nMakes `/restart` a public `deepagents-code` slash command so users can\ndiscover it in autocomplete and `/help` while preserving its\nalways-immediate recovery behavior.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-09T19:10:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/64505b848868b80213b6da87113cd63890c3d520","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/64505b848868b80213b6da87113cd63890c3d520","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/64505b848868b80213b6da87113cd63890c3d520/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5bd1ef8cb29db781ccbb37755db44ce0ab1d7bd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5bd1ef8cb29db781ccbb37755db44ce0ab1d7bd2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5bd1ef8cb29db781ccbb37755db44ce0ab1d7bd2"}]},{"sha":"5bd1ef8cb29db781ccbb37755db44ce0ab1d7bd2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDViZDFlZjhjYjI5ZGI3ODFjY2JiMzc3NTVkYjQ0Y2UwYWIxZDdiZDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-09T19:02:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T19:02:30Z"},"message":"feat(code): surface gateway key mismatch on `PermissionDeniedError` (#3813)\n\n**TL;DR:** Deep Agents Code now surfaces a targeted error when a\nnon-LangSmith API key is routed through the LangSmith gateway, and links\ngateway/endpoint docs on other `PermissionDeniedError` cases.\n\n---\n\nA common cause of `PermissionDeniedError` is a provider API key that\ndoes not match the endpoint it is sent to — e.g. an `OPENAI_API_KEY`\nexported in the shell while the LangSmith gateway overrides the OpenAI\nbase URL, so the key is rejected. When this exact case is detected\n(gateway endpoint + a non-LangSmith key, identified by the absence of\nthe `lsv2_` prefix), the `ErrorMessage` now names the offending env var\nand the fix (unset it, or set `LANGCHAIN_DISABLE_GATEWAY=1`). Other\n`PermissionDeniedError` cases fall back to a generic message plus a docs\nlink. Detection only inspects the key prefix — the secret value is never\nlogged. Other error types render unchanged.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0794867b7541cb808b2190aead1373a83e795dac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0794867b7541cb808b2190aead1373a83e795dac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5bd1ef8cb29db781ccbb37755db44ce0ab1d7bd2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKGNGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACOgQAEHd7mhAv1gcOyTzIY9DbVhT\nxDx2aLCAtHTVV4Okzk0W+3esQ2QKdf0obOdtp3RJ9PWdqe/K+aqx7l8b74E68SwB\nBvjgyLn2KGD23SQX4P+5+jQG9f5SzkohrrYpUyxKgs1q8wesBsH2RTKYzfdJI7tP\nu086I1aPhyGPgJQ8c+hHqGdUov1EytWLqyeLtkl843Tjm59aF8ogKVgktGcVxNkv\nxPRccj/iuLwb+/ecZKT8ApDIlFCd87H3LScP1LHkZdztq37gz+L3R3vWmnwIV7H/\nQ4G1l5E2pqCrMzMAMnOe9ZkEr5j7M7ODTJ4uHp2iWAgv/jTGnFT9YpfYh32SUhOE\nyN6UclHEhGHd24ZBb9SwXN7NxyKBP9Q8r8tQfjogushgGO49oOL/AEqv6bQM7afX\nJhIHxA+2vckYoAy29WbDWp7uo0m6yKDinF4EHy8cb7KRRwwzlwScdB5fCAdsYC6d\n2WHBg5fCuW3ZOXW1qdQQ16iq+sP/Vb+dutWNM8x7xplSeIkGMbNcXHaeyscTdMeF\ngez5wLOEMagzfQvjKPz5zzjSij4yPT/NJiS2XlBsnoCmIgdhu0AWe8ktvNV8uXvI\nfP79CMDyJLgSogkV4dscmsNMyrvHgOTAN9fX5h/5hrLOlXBDf5mYcQnnIuvVm+lR\nqCCbgdOtNlyp68MD5C5P\n=HQrd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0794867b7541cb808b2190aead1373a83e795dac\nparent 68e64263f590b3244b689664715f354fb3a389cd\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781031750 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781031750 -0400\n\nfeat(code): surface gateway key mismatch on `PermissionDeniedError` (#3813)\n\n**TL;DR:** Deep Agents Code now surfaces a targeted error when a\nnon-LangSmith API key is routed through the LangSmith gateway, and links\ngateway/endpoint docs on other `PermissionDeniedError` cases.\n\n---\n\nA common cause of `PermissionDeniedError` is a provider API key that\ndoes not match the endpoint it is sent to — e.g. an `OPENAI_API_KEY`\nexported in the shell while the LangSmith gateway overrides the OpenAI\nbase URL, so the key is rejected. When this exact case is detected\n(gateway endpoint + a non-LangSmith key, identified by the absence of\nthe `lsv2_` prefix), the `ErrorMessage` now names the offending env var\nand the fix (unset it, or set `LANGCHAIN_DISABLE_GATEWAY=1`). Other\n`PermissionDeniedError` cases fall back to a generic message plus a docs\nlink. Detection only inspects the key prefix — the secret value is never\nlogged. Other error types render unchanged.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-09T19:02:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5bd1ef8cb29db781ccbb37755db44ce0ab1d7bd2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5bd1ef8cb29db781ccbb37755db44ce0ab1d7bd2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5bd1ef8cb29db781ccbb37755db44ce0ab1d7bd2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"68e64263f590b3244b689664715f354fb3a389cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/68e64263f590b3244b689664715f354fb3a389cd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/68e64263f590b3244b689664715f354fb3a389cd"}]},{"sha":"68e64263f590b3244b689664715f354fb3a389cd","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY4ZTY0MjYzZjU5MGIzMjQ0YjY4OTY2NDcxNWYzNTRmYjNhMzg5Y2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-09T18:29:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T18:29:46Z"},"message":"fix(code): don't show `\"No threads found\"` while threads load (#3815)\n\n## Description\nThe `/threads` switcher rendered \"No threads found\" whenever the cached\nsnapshot was empty — an empty startup cache, or a cwd filter that\nexcluded all cached rows — even though a background disk load always\nruns on mount. This gates the empty placeholder on a new\n`_disk_load_complete` flag so the picker shows \"Loading threads...\"\nuntil the disk query completes, then resolves to the real result.\n\n## Release Note\nFixed the `/threads` switcher incorrectly showing \"No threads found\"\nwhile threads were still loading from disk.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Open `/threads` with an empty startup cache (or in a directory\nwith no cached threads) and confirm it shows \"Loading threads...\" before\nresolving, instead of flashing \"No threads found\".\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cf770e44934ffc3c4ce3ebfbfcdb2ede50e43968","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/cf770e44934ffc3c4ce3ebfbfcdb2ede50e43968"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/68e64263f590b3244b689664715f354fb3a389cd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKFuaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMY0QAJji5YqP+D3SoOqVs/K6dbWm\n6CQArYOFV6ei9+YNjlpUYM4MhKsJxjsD5oV7hPL4/sHm7jNRM/eyVq4SnB+pH+wl\ntr3Emk6fzLKu0G/esdfNCRJc1KrbachK8JwzxyCk2CMP7neTsQCP3W3DCOVhKYmz\ngJisoQkbweepjGc8GaMB5pNgItsPw/c+UgxH6/+luIUm1GZ7xNZ1ekrrgjX2TFBg\nxHjNJ+2c8ZAfJO1409uZexmoHRnFq5YFfhVJ7n/+dc8LXTKo3hcPT8LBGqfPkR8y\nyyKN/b+EaNIljFIlXOR2SEQ6OvUWHTIYbJoUF/aKhJZkh8RT8y2st2hMKTdJbIpN\nQggP6hYvUsHpzTcwQMq3NutGR63c+WiSZkea/4tnncKoMxswWc6LmUAlZWB1X514\nStGDg2LY7OihF8ggNfvT8fPr3Y9qj17LoolcrEy5CG63V2aJRsyWp+EaaYyC4h3S\nYVHvCoPrDNSHOOlb3qZsNNgnEKqSWtKmMaOfV+vF1bMbbBMmpewfGR0/00F5ku3T\ncI8W9QqZ0j8TTXBm+DM/dy3kW0I0W/FE5opvtoOwvJF63m2+x/xPlwAyACGqf4oU\nl106TjsBDh+8wcJlUFczd6KO5I6xukzAv4JRK3NAMLMM37rhojjrwHK1VKR4Rapp\n2KpHPIyGMTptmKryzIxj\n=pBAP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cf770e44934ffc3c4ce3ebfbfcdb2ede50e43968\nparent b45eeebaf7e6ae6e07b8f9ca521525c66fe14f63\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781029786 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781029786 -0400\n\nfix(code): don't show `\"No threads found\"` while threads load (#3815)\n\n## Description\nThe `/threads` switcher rendered \"No threads found\" whenever the cached\nsnapshot was empty — an empty startup cache, or a cwd filter that\nexcluded all cached rows — even though a background disk load always\nruns on mount. This gates the empty placeholder on a new\n`_disk_load_complete` flag so the picker shows \"Loading threads...\"\nuntil the disk query completes, then resolves to the real result.\n\n## Release Note\nFixed the `/threads` switcher incorrectly showing \"No threads found\"\nwhile threads were still loading from disk.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Open `/threads` with an empty startup cache (or in a directory\nwith no cached threads) and confirm it shows \"Loading threads...\" before\nresolving, instead of flashing \"No threads found\".\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-09T18:29:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/68e64263f590b3244b689664715f354fb3a389cd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/68e64263f590b3244b689664715f354fb3a389cd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/68e64263f590b3244b689664715f354fb3a389cd/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b45eeebaf7e6ae6e07b8f9ca521525c66fe14f63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b45eeebaf7e6ae6e07b8f9ca521525c66fe14f63","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b45eeebaf7e6ae6e07b8f9ca521525c66fe14f63"}]},{"sha":"b45eeebaf7e6ae6e07b8f9ca521525c66fe14f63","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI0NWVlZWJhZjdlNmFlNmUwN2I4ZjljYTUyMTUyNWM2NmZlMTRmNjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-09T17:59:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T17:59:05Z"},"message":"fix(code): coalesce streamed markdown writes to keep input responsive (#3819)\n\nTyping in the chat input lagged while the model was actively streaming\ntokens. The streaming loop wrote every token straight to Textual's\n`MarkdownStream`, which woke its background task and\nre-parsed/re-rendered the markdown tail on essentially every chunk. That\nCPU-bound work runs on the same event loop that dispatches keypresses,\nso input stalled until streaming paused.\n\nThis buffers streamed tokens in `AssistantMessage` and flushes them to\nthe `MarkdownStream` on a throttled timer (`_STREAM_FLUSH_INTERVAL`), so\nthe event loop stays free to handle keyboard input. `stop_stream` and\n`set_content` drain the buffer and cancel the timer so finalized content\nis never dropped. Also gates the per-chunk `content_blocks` `repr()` in\nthe streaming adapter behind a debug-level check so it isn't built on\nevery token.\n\n## Release Note\nFix laggy keyboard input in the interactive REPL while the model is\nstreaming a response.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Stream a long response and confirm typing in the input stays\nsmooth.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a23cb3a2aa9f679e63635173727292d0932678a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a23cb3a2aa9f679e63635173727292d0932678a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b45eeebaf7e6ae6e07b8f9ca521525c66fe14f63","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKFRpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALO4QAKrQe3aK5lhmM60HLRRbTdqj\n3X2smMki+VrTQAemM/jR9rHdT3DIe1xL8Ib6WzjuyYA9EdCbYG+CgOntZsIlnfRH\nOVo0ROhphreE3500E5etjRPAH/THexW2iK3+ZKy86eu9BYW5YQsGLmtzElPQuSz+\n44F0ufiufpZSR+324xohBMuhhOaTnGPM3mr2KyzFylQbCvk6eVWxpeaQNR3q5ELy\nwFDpVC+VYMnwhs/sqocQc0grlv9FKML4t+xl0l3zbzWaRmMKuYa2n2Z3DX8P6Jgu\ntKUm8MLCej3ZEb/OSLyKRjrfWEN5gVIqHQO7OXlVgFIFQNzEfV/sqqOaQpPBJvdz\nvpad6ilPovEO57PQIuoa2CxHsrzkehCyISpHiurPc5sVIQSw+Ta+wtn32sOK2tIW\nC4isZ82/TqADW1V9pQ/v5F+1kXv3Yxg3AYgSRwVTHj/DK2cGsnOJyosWXslDwkST\n761iWk93E4oyjlfKb094junuaJl9MdvBh14OogEhC8pD1RwOVUFWbvpApGMXtsbS\n9w1OkKXCoC26IycEt6H3dyjh8n9QZRUHMWSXZnmK60xq+W4Mb/kua6KuLiiGnxm+\nUJWCTVVBNGkRvqiXVV9hBIUKc0Z8lGbR2lkutFaH0SxAWrYrneHlrUw5Va8osGXZ\noF78A41V9idW4cgKpreP\n=TEku\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a23cb3a2aa9f679e63635173727292d0932678a7\nparent 73952b308e1329187675d49aa7b8babb8e05cbd0\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781027945 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781027945 -0400\n\nfix(code): coalesce streamed markdown writes to keep input responsive (#3819)\n\nTyping in the chat input lagged while the model was actively streaming\ntokens. The streaming loop wrote every token straight to Textual's\n`MarkdownStream`, which woke its background task and\nre-parsed/re-rendered the markdown tail on essentially every chunk. That\nCPU-bound work runs on the same event loop that dispatches keypresses,\nso input stalled until streaming paused.\n\nThis buffers streamed tokens in `AssistantMessage` and flushes them to\nthe `MarkdownStream` on a throttled timer (`_STREAM_FLUSH_INTERVAL`), so\nthe event loop stays free to handle keyboard input. `stop_stream` and\n`set_content` drain the buffer and cancel the timer so finalized content\nis never dropped. Also gates the per-chunk `content_blocks` `repr()` in\nthe streaming adapter behind a debug-level check so it isn't built on\nevery token.\n\n## Release Note\nFix laggy keyboard input in the interactive REPL while the model is\nstreaming a response.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Stream a long response and confirm typing in the input stays\nsmooth.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-09T17:59:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b45eeebaf7e6ae6e07b8f9ca521525c66fe14f63","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b45eeebaf7e6ae6e07b8f9ca521525c66fe14f63","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b45eeebaf7e6ae6e07b8f9ca521525c66fe14f63/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"73952b308e1329187675d49aa7b8babb8e05cbd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/73952b308e1329187675d49aa7b8babb8e05cbd0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/73952b308e1329187675d49aa7b8babb8e05cbd0"}]},{"sha":"73952b308e1329187675d49aa7b8babb8e05cbd0","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDczOTUyYjMwOGUxMzI5MTg3Njc1ZDQ5YWE3YjhiYWJiOGUwNWNiZDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-09T17:58:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T17:58:43Z"},"message":"test(code): stop unit tests from recoloring the real terminal (#3817)\n\n## Description\nRunning `libs/code` unit tests from inside a real terminal (e.g. an\neditable install via the bash tool, or VSCode's zsh) visibly changed the\nterminal's theme. `DeepAgentsApp.__init__` calls\n`sync_terminal_background()` and the spinner path calls\n`set_terminal_progress()`, which emit `OSC 11` (background color) and\n`OSC 9;4` (taskbar progress) sequences through\n`terminal_escape.write_terminal_escape`. That writer targets `/dev/tty`,\nwhich pytest does not capture, so the escapes leaked to the developer's\nlive session. An autouse fixture sets\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_NO_TERMINAL_ESCAPE=1` for the whole unit run;\n`test_terminal_escape.py` still clears it in its own fixture so the real\nwrite path stays covered.\n\n## Release Note\nnone\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Run `libs/code` unit tests from inside an interactive terminal and\nconfirm the terminal background/theme no longer changes.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d837affda59498fe9e593a69f4836a270149b89d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d837affda59498fe9e593a69f4836a270149b89d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/73952b308e1329187675d49aa7b8babb8e05cbd0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKFRTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlUIQAEV7oZk4e51Ak5e3ynLJQlPJ\n7ys6gWcFda4qpraxP3mbGVQ35ij6yFPM6TrCWg/17OsIKVHdc+BMzfeMjQbT1Tyn\n+bCyPZxpC6KlgkvpE/+hm3nrsVbucyreHYeZpoNGZf2bmnev1W5vgjB62I5P3iNr\nyb0V0CJnCLb4r5R9iJ42q9uHRvedHTnpmB5ZKhR+5ChK56FP/2W0Fh+3O9ehFK2E\nmpX0H7etn0GHKwg9gqlpv8Sk59Zvp+ecL5rUljC0cEv/Fa6SJnrtAGQGE/WeWOSE\na89oMGuqXYSR53NiR25xCM9oW4bTulhuai5oOitP0InUtNAOD0MJougvbO5c+fni\n+KCUpmzkcKJvr+fOYvG9W6DLdzbOu06ETyiZ4dCOcuHqt74Mx4ZcwHTTi00lwVaH\nC8nE9z9DopXuwVdGvFs7Rs/rpjMIcA2af7qLxJ1ThQ2K0tuQzZPmPkVJon2p9HSo\nq+8+5Sf4+uZeLzgfMscgWPLBRVr0mkL0xfSaZFze8PpeBmFbEAy823UBOqO4ms4y\nJuLEFVDiq5UhFtj6UDZxWWiTTOAmwAEwCfgILgWfQTbXM9abOEPYqw7djeIs6HtL\nUk21tpfZkFRRbXaMtqmOCv7axJuB0XVOLBFufxe0+lXyOvGmIbkLP7nxQIvvbma2\nrAZkL66cJYLTY5+yl6HJ\n=7sPS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d837affda59498fe9e593a69f4836a270149b89d\nparent 969cbe8709110eed334b25e50530510317954cfd\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781027923 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781027923 -0400\n\ntest(code): stop unit tests from recoloring the real terminal (#3817)\n\n## Description\nRunning `libs/code` unit tests from inside a real terminal (e.g. an\neditable install via the bash tool, or VSCode's zsh) visibly changed the\nterminal's theme. `DeepAgentsApp.__init__` calls\n`sync_terminal_background()` and the spinner path calls\n`set_terminal_progress()`, which emit `OSC 11` (background color) and\n`OSC 9;4` (taskbar progress) sequences through\n`terminal_escape.write_terminal_escape`. That writer targets `/dev/tty`,\nwhich pytest does not capture, so the escapes leaked to the developer's\nlive session. An autouse fixture sets\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_NO_TERMINAL_ESCAPE=1` for the whole unit run;\n`test_terminal_escape.py` still clears it in its own fixture so the real\nwrite path stays covered.\n\n## Release Note\nnone\n\n## Test Plan\n- [ ] Run `libs/code` unit tests from inside an interactive terminal and\nconfirm the terminal background/theme no longer changes.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-09T17:58:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/73952b308e1329187675d49aa7b8babb8e05cbd0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/73952b308e1329187675d49aa7b8babb8e05cbd0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/73952b308e1329187675d49aa7b8babb8e05cbd0/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"969cbe8709110eed334b25e50530510317954cfd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/969cbe8709110eed334b25e50530510317954cfd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/969cbe8709110eed334b25e50530510317954cfd"}]},{"sha":"969cbe8709110eed334b25e50530510317954cfd","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk2OWNiZTg3MDkxMTBlZWQzMzRiMjVlNTA1MzA1MTAzMTc5NTRjZmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-09T17:25:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T17:25:21Z"},"message":"chore(deps): update lint and typing dependency floors (#3818)\n\nDependency floors are refreshed across the monorepo for newer\nLangChain/LangSmith releases, provider integrations, pytest tooling,\n`ruff`, and `ty`. The code changes are the compatibility work needed for\nthose newer lint and type checks, with small structural cleanups where\nthe tools needed clearer narrowing or less complex functions.\n\n## Changes\n- Raised runtime and test dependency minimums across SDK, CLI, Code,\nACP, evals, examples, and partner packages, including updated\nLangChain/LangSmith/provider pins and current lint/test tooling\nbaselines.\n- Reworked backend factory typing around `BACKEND_TYPES` with\n`_resolve_backend`, widened file transfer error fields to support\nbackend-specific strings, and updated filesystem/summarization\nmiddleware to use the shared resolver.\n- Tightened `deepagents-code` typing for middleware stacks, MCP tool\nfiltering, update checks, and Textual compatibility patches, replacing\nstale suppressions with `ty`-specific ignores where runtime behavior is\nintentionally narrower than static types.\n- Split large CLI command handlers into focused helpers such as\n`_dispatch_command`, `_execute_agents_command`, and the MCP server\nsubcommand helpers while preserving existing command behavior.\n- Updated Harbor LangSmith sandbox handling to rely on explicit\n`NetworkPolicy` and `capabilities` instead of legacy property overrides,\nwith tests adjusted around the new capability checks.\n- Applied lint/format/type-check cleanups across tests and examples so\nthe staged code passes the refreshed tooling expectations.","tree":{"sha":"7bddcb2b8fde9193c5d8ee3f1c0ea949567074d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7bddcb2b8fde9193c5d8ee3f1c0ea949567074d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/969cbe8709110eed334b25e50530510317954cfd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKEyBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+UwQAA9kBw/YuhT6eQgEf+K+dRbJ\nvSdab5BrBUXgJAblBfw+U0dgiLm2d+r9zcX7nANOMKJV5PO6lCo5sJ/4lgsiXiPh\nzQngPQ08S3qeS0bpFPHwgc/aHXH0QLtt8XagxteBzdQjrXCxPXpIdqyMEDTSck2c\nhz60ihfyBhCC8llKUmqh6aNorHQykL7ofSURb4LK4dG7tIJF0SsjkD7WYLuSJCdP\nWtwgZVlURVDEv5e2V0WUcgj3u1vHr0drtXbjcfZYU2zYvZqR1o5Mgccvfg0KMrzn\nMYEjBJfS6VSe+hvMZyfGGoDPb6WLrNLTaB0lrHX4bzEgpcUhr8ZNLMbA09GnY3W3\nUjAaOlZj26FVO6prnDcs7INobdY3WOIrqYgampEHmCqbYhLiwzg2QUVbIPie+om9\n0AB52BI8mCWUf7uyaPggunv5qEBy9OCeN4FrPBT2CgdPQ41wYGqbAFFevNpGxxHH\ntcypc03LvEpci6VEXzTNCgZVBnwuL+q0wA7nfvOGPenwZXv1qypVWjU6bPefKTGy\ng2QsPv3AMnBsc7XLj3oPXFfzqd6HoSYqCyDAG0CVlQ7e+HAzDFFUFjEBI33uNe+q\nlvMnPyhc5KIrdvl0pRKF65plEPk4WL/jt+7NqbYWxbW5avw9jfQ9EyE7jaWProUN\nARJ4kBlC5wJUCb1u9Ay9\n=WOKk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7bddcb2b8fde9193c5d8ee3f1c0ea949567074d2\nparent 7358a6663b1b2cda42392616eb04d39d01f42b2b\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781025921 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781025921 -0400\n\nchore(deps): update lint and typing dependency floors (#3818)\n\nDependency floors are refreshed across the monorepo for newer\nLangChain/LangSmith releases, provider integrations, pytest tooling,\n`ruff`, and `ty`. The code changes are the compatibility work needed for\nthose newer lint and type checks, with small structural cleanups where\nthe tools needed clearer narrowing or less complex functions.\n\n## Changes\n- Raised runtime and test dependency minimums across SDK, CLI, Code,\nACP, evals, examples, and partner packages, including updated\nLangChain/LangSmith/provider pins and current lint/test tooling\nbaselines.\n- Reworked backend factory typing around `BACKEND_TYPES` with\n`_resolve_backend`, widened file transfer error fields to support\nbackend-specific strings, and updated filesystem/summarization\nmiddleware to use the shared resolver.\n- Tightened `deepagents-code` typing for middleware stacks, MCP tool\nfiltering, update checks, and Textual compatibility patches, replacing\nstale suppressions with `ty`-specific ignores where runtime behavior is\nintentionally narrower than static types.\n- Split large CLI command handlers into focused helpers such as\n`_dispatch_command`, `_execute_agents_command`, and the MCP server\nsubcommand helpers while preserving existing command behavior.\n- Updated Harbor LangSmith sandbox handling to rely on explicit\n`NetworkPolicy` and `capabilities` instead of legacy property overrides,\nwith tests adjusted around the new capability checks.\n- Applied lint/format/type-check cleanups across tests and examples so\nthe staged code passes the refreshed tooling expectations.","verified_at":"2026-06-09T17:25:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/969cbe8709110eed334b25e50530510317954cfd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/969cbe8709110eed334b25e50530510317954cfd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/969cbe8709110eed334b25e50530510317954cfd/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7358a6663b1b2cda42392616eb04d39d01f42b2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7358a6663b1b2cda42392616eb04d39d01f42b2b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7358a6663b1b2cda42392616eb04d39d01f42b2b"}]},{"sha":"7358a6663b1b2cda42392616eb04d39d01f42b2b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDczNThhNjY2M2IxYjJjZGE0MjM5MjYxNmViMDRkMzlkMDFmNDJiMmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"John Kennedy","email":"65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-09T15:01:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T15:01:31Z"},"message":"feat(talon): add local runtime host (#3759)\n\nAdd `deepagents-talon`, a local single-operator runtime host for\nlong-running Deep Agents over channels and scheduled jobs. The package\nwires a Deep Agents runtime to channel adapters, cron tools, MCP\nloading, optional voice transcription, LangSmith trace context, and a\nrunnable WhatsApp Docker Compose example.\n\nThis first PR focused is on the local host, WhatsApp adapter, scheduler,\nand CI/release plumbing while reusing existing `deepagents-code` web and\nMCP utilities (where practical).\n\nAreas that need careful review:\n\n- Whether the generic channel abstractions should stay in the first PR\nor be narrowed to WhatsApp-only.\n- WhatsApp exposure defaults, session storage, downloaded media\nretention, and open-mode acknowledgement.\n- The dependency boundary with `deepagents-code`, especially MCP helpers\nand web tools.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"b48b7cbc6776c000b89f7ee2d12c89a5fdeac9ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b48b7cbc6776c000b89f7ee2d12c89a5fdeac9ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7358a6663b1b2cda42392616eb04d39d01f42b2b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKCrLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAG1EQAF4elcy8YzYkGwauFwpBrQ/y\nbZsVBn2jPJuO6SEY39lZ6ZaMa/hKMjD5eHpxIk8ooGVAyefUv5dtUthikuLpegUk\nRmOcls+q4auB5b7KXMe4ohPclIYsZVdt4zOr95twQAR1VFP1INp1TiHxASZyp5hJ\nxD4Lo1lbRutY2zku7+0jplYTuJ0ZagQAyCwxu4aqM40QXvhgJZWRXXowSE1vBdp0\n2R+LB81g8MJFb6bwxdnOs4t7DfDgQaOYmjHdcm+y4oLv6NLTc0KaA/NqxsMlcxyL\nwS/FT30jJd6I8SEaX73HhYU9SXwlKMeFhFL5lRyjLVxOJCTjKnrZAAdrquXg7heC\nhtvBLbBOG9clbwGuDxNGhevG3MZYNNUYwsovUeujKaZ5Z5Z2NXhVWwzp5dVM1Hr7\n5FwA3pd5aK+PsItQ3xl7BZJCE2PB7wwrVbt0jDaTnYrqsS0lscVUf0EV0qTxQIY9\nS4hsNbjPwC0CR3OB2iHx7wHOZjYRMcB4izJpowXTbOkyHCgB7/EDjgLwnQ/xivUW\nyQpxPGF9ffMhw7oeLKxW6O+IuDkvauj5SVy+erGhN0MMmZ74Y5P05+dbiegTqigk\ntJW1n7AMXMFipPGORWhb7hRjYFMfDjFDCaNkeotQEVRSZTQLg1PRlZIjmTAGqBkV\nLODvT3+g8HiQsZ/LYpLm\n=/NeA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b48b7cbc6776c000b89f7ee2d12c89a5fdeac9ce\nparent 45691c556105e171c7210c7c10388dc73202a025\nauthor John Kennedy <65985482+jkennedyvz@users.noreply.github.com> 1781017291 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781017291 -0400\n\nfeat(talon): add local runtime host (#3759)\n\nAdd `deepagents-talon`, a local single-operator runtime host for\nlong-running Deep Agents over channels and scheduled jobs. The package\nwires a Deep Agents runtime to channel adapters, cron tools, MCP\nloading, optional voice transcription, LangSmith trace context, and a\nrunnable WhatsApp Docker Compose example.\n\nThis first PR focused is on the local host, WhatsApp adapter, scheduler,\nand CI/release plumbing while reusing existing `deepagents-code` web and\nMCP utilities (where practical).\n\nAreas that need careful review:\n\n- Whether the generic channel abstractions should stay in the first PR\nor be narrowed to WhatsApp-only.\n- WhatsApp exposure defaults, session storage, downloaded media\nretention, and open-mode acknowledgement.\n- The dependency boundary with `deepagents-code`, especially MCP helpers\nand web tools.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Deep Agent <agent@deepagents.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-09T15:01:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7358a6663b1b2cda42392616eb04d39d01f42b2b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7358a6663b1b2cda42392616eb04d39d01f42b2b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7358a6663b1b2cda42392616eb04d39d01f42b2b/comments","author":{"login":"jkennedyvz","id":65985482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTg1NDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65985482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz","html_url":"https://github.com/jkennedyvz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jkennedyvz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"45691c556105e171c7210c7c10388dc73202a025","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/45691c556105e171c7210c7c10388dc73202a025","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/45691c556105e171c7210c7c10388dc73202a025"}]},{"sha":"45691c556105e171c7210c7c10388dc73202a025","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ1NjkxYzU1NjEwNWUxNzFjNzIxMGM3YzEwMzg4ZGM3MzIwMmEwMjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-08T17:05:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T17:05:35Z"},"message":"fix(code): recover from tool errors instead of aborting run (#3804)\n\nWhen an MCP tool returns an error, `langchain-mcp-adapters` raises a\n`ToolException`, and LangGraph's default tool-error handling re-raises\nplain `ToolException` rather than converting it — so a recoverable\ntool-level failure (e.g. `langsmith_fetch_runs` reporting `no project\nfound`) would crash the entire agent run. A new middleware catches these\nand hands the model an error message it can work around.\n\n## Changes\n- Add `_ToolExceptionRecoveryMiddleware`, which catches `ToolException`\nfrom tool execution and returns an error `ToolMessage`\n(`status=\"error\"`) so the run continues. Only `ToolException` is caught\n— every other exception propagates so genuine bugs still surface.\n- Wire the middleware onto both the main agent and CLI subagents, placed\ninnermost in each stack so it wraps tool execution as tightly as\npossible and only intercepts the tool's own failures, not sibling\nmiddleware (which return error messages rather than raise).\n- Log recovered failures at `WARNING` with `exc_info=True` so the\ntraceback is preserved for debugging.\n- Fall back to a tool-named message (`\"<tool> failed with no error\ndetail\"`) when the exception carries no text, instead of an opaque\nexception class name.","tree":{"sha":"169e8c30c7af578249c349c4f6f22ad7c051d432","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/169e8c30c7af578249c349c4f6f22ad7c051d432"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/45691c556105e171c7210c7c10388dc73202a025","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJvZfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAgIQAGU7X0TfdlPezeisKuW2FNJ5\nIylJc42fg0C+AdxxKmXoIy47LxO8u8fZLy0eKvhPJoi3Gdmymrc95YL4albtmD3k\nX/T2lx2Pkr4yy7tcW86vO772VWVg4sWuotlOn6N34S+geYlniwrMmaM0UOfzc3nf\nrTZdOMMGEK076Bgm2Fm27oy8MmRLwYRGMqXY3VIlt+5SB9k1nX1PxDl3HGP3lUYQ\nGu3Q4Rj8n+eYWktUrSFoNO487tPXiVrrxdH2PzWood7oG6/IueFcOk3OMfnov+DQ\nwsjqDe7dcCAi/ITMBx4CiHQl/YdszqIV3qMcMyqoNtK7K48Nf03tjJIeRzhAJ090\n+PiWDCOudL8Y0Pbwppqi2D0f4KOFB6HCQnOTmrJG0hwXOKlHLzuOVNJgWStaJ9nl\nlBRkD9GIBVfsK5NUI5DGRd/vQreTFZZnoa11JlURO1dwKX0+aGg+uWFsNK8t968f\n5RocUeCNDobzLNNC9u8m+8Ri0ltWfuwzauLz8Wi2YfM/tD+M+SKFjLpw0tMKTpBB\n37BoJSqVNBJ1ST2Vd7OrLuqa5MKQ/7gVowapz3MAVRybaKfeAZWjdocHD2YzVpSA\nE4JcWyI1VtsufQ/tmRCUidJXn6dI06W19C5QwmIH8YaNJdhFj4/bx/gi269lYeLt\nvVWJxQIimXAlQ/j5Ju+G\n=KJik\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 169e8c30c7af578249c349c4f6f22ad7c051d432\nparent 0b683a9435b95bce79d10451868eae54c6a3e88c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1780938335 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780938335 -0400\n\nfix(code): recover from tool errors instead of aborting run (#3804)\n\nWhen an MCP tool returns an error, `langchain-mcp-adapters` raises a\n`ToolException`, and LangGraph's default tool-error handling re-raises\nplain `ToolException` rather than converting it — so a recoverable\ntool-level failure (e.g. `langsmith_fetch_runs` reporting `no project\nfound`) would crash the entire agent run. A new middleware catches these\nand hands the model an error message it can work around.\n\n## Changes\n- Add `_ToolExceptionRecoveryMiddleware`, which catches `ToolException`\nfrom tool execution and returns an error `ToolMessage`\n(`status=\"error\"`) so the run continues. Only `ToolException` is caught\n— every other exception propagates so genuine bugs still surface.\n- Wire the middleware onto both the main agent and CLI subagents, placed\ninnermost in each stack so it wraps tool execution as tightly as\npossible and only intercepts the tool's own failures, not sibling\nmiddleware (which return error messages rather than raise).\n- Log recovered failures at `WARNING` with `exc_info=True` so the\ntraceback is preserved for debugging.\n- Fall back to a tool-named message (`\"<tool> failed with no error\ndetail\"`) when the exception carries no text, instead of an opaque\nexception class name.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T17:05:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/45691c556105e171c7210c7c10388dc73202a025","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/45691c556105e171c7210c7c10388dc73202a025","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/45691c556105e171c7210c7c10388dc73202a025/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0b683a9435b95bce79d10451868eae54c6a3e88c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0b683a9435b95bce79d10451868eae54c6a3e88c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0b683a9435b95bce79d10451868eae54c6a3e88c"}]},{"sha":"0b683a9435b95bce79d10451868eae54c6a3e88c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDBiNjgzYTk0MzViOTViY2U3OWQxMDQ1MTg2OGVhZTU0YzZhM2U4OGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"langsmith-engine[bot]","email":"270983758+langsmith-engine[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-08T17:05:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T17:05:25Z"},"message":"fix(code): agent retries `gh search` with invalid `mergedAt` field (#3802)\n\nWhen summarizing GitHub activity, the agent calls `gh search prs ...\n--json ...,mergedAt,...` across multiple user-role queries\n(author/reviewed-by/commenter) in parallel; `gh search` does not support\nthe `mergedAt` field and all calls fail identically with `Unknown JSON\nfield: \"mergedAt\"`. The agent doesn't probe the field schema before\nfanning out and only drops `mergedAt` on the next turn after seeing\nrepeated identical errors — wasting ~3 tool calls and a model turn\nbefore recovery.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: LangSmith Issues Agent <issues-agent@langsmith.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"bfa6fe945ddf8bfce2c6bdbf2e7ae4af3357affb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/bfa6fe945ddf8bfce2c6bdbf2e7ae4af3357affb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0b683a9435b95bce79d10451868eae54c6a3e88c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJvZVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAENAQADtM26D/AcvyNOwZV9Z/gcRQ\nmY+fMrNphQGAz7X4RtUX+z3BLePHHBW1SkimOdBkkaSS1NWYORidZbPcNM20M/ce\nCblrl30xrB86gnyKJuWVEDwTSWYzb0n01a8dD7W/ud6mllpWwN/ami+MOYdC3L1B\nPTmlAp/Yv1sbg1aEq3qg3iPzShXaTXsROw+OmOIECOknhzeBdmOt3mYtv1y+5TDy\njRqnbo0Bpoo/HInRAN+wmCtWmxRDSUxNyBybyoAQxY0xNec1nNwzTWnkQWF3iorv\nZBLyHZBlYZfegtgtey05gVVNOlyIWAPdEk9tAn/P+UALnF+l9nTjQqsAjQPtnl+f\n44enJanKCnlcSah4SiNFONRbxTIWqglIhiCZ3y+7qRVXeyo3/3bG3Srm5YouEvTn\nQbgwZMBJhQeDaHtcAfu2P14PnSZ7zWwWvFj+DKy7hOwBAWpPDtz7p6a6sCehJJXs\nWbMCvvPXRFuVtud3JKZYm0m5zzNQrEduQJfTLdyLvG2OYVD86pyzdpS6AJyENGH4\ndH/uI2pzcppQrTtZtvfIn2Dbn0XwUU7MnlRjvn4t6H4Va+RE6I1LxF0iKczIoTc7\nhiHnW1QRvzDampK8zJXFlYRMGyKjDtnTpzVXBYb9Gts9aMQnFGnNzihDpk4MLdOO\nxVRM4JgaKWwhwgw86jIn\n=O1sY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bfa6fe945ddf8bfce2c6bdbf2e7ae4af3357affb\nparent db252411d8ca945aca86429acb644540ec970bdb\nauthor langsmith-engine[bot] <270983758+langsmith-engine[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1780938325 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780938325 -0400\n\nfix(code): agent retries `gh search` with invalid `mergedAt` field (#3802)\n\nWhen summarizing GitHub activity, the agent calls `gh search prs ...\n--json ...,mergedAt,...` across multiple user-role queries\n(author/reviewed-by/commenter) in parallel; `gh search` does not support\nthe `mergedAt` field and all calls fail identically with `Unknown JSON\nfield: \"mergedAt\"`. The agent doesn't probe the field schema before\nfanning out and only drops `mergedAt` on the next turn after seeing\nrepeated identical errors — wasting ~3 tool calls and a model turn\nbefore recovery.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: LangSmith Issues Agent <issues-agent@langsmith.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T17:05:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0b683a9435b95bce79d10451868eae54c6a3e88c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0b683a9435b95bce79d10451868eae54c6a3e88c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0b683a9435b95bce79d10451868eae54c6a3e88c/comments","author":{"login":"langsmith-engine[bot]","id":270983758,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOECbiTg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/3183926?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/langsmith-engine%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/langsmith-engine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langsmith-engine%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langsmith-engine%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/us