f8efa192501b8993d37f94a7\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1780674397 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780674397 -0400\n\nfix(code): skip update prompts for editable installs (#3781)\n\nEditable installs can be intentionally behind the latest PyPI release,\nso startup update prompts should not appear for local checkout sessions.\nThe update check now exits before contacting PyPI or registering the\nupdate modal when `deepagents-code` is installed editable.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T15:46:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ae2874e8ece96c04233c1a88a9da1bd7b9ee2bb2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ae2874e8ece96c04233c1a88a9da1bd7b9ee2bb2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ae2874e8ece96c04233c1a88a9da1bd7b9ee2bb2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8e743ac895c4e38df8efa192501b8993d37f94a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e743ac895c4e38df8efa192501b8993d37f94a7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8e743ac895c4e38df8efa192501b8993d37f94a7"}]},{"sha":"8e743ac895c4e38df8efa192501b8993d37f94a7","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhlNzQzYWM4OTVjNGUzOGRmOGVmYTE5MjUwMWI4OTkzZDM3Zjk0YTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-05T15:42:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T15:42:08Z"},"message":"fix(code): unify auth status labels (#3773)\n\n## Description\nUnifies provider auth status labels through one helper so `/auth` and\n`/model` interpret `CONFIGURED`, `MISSING`, `NOT_REQUIRED`, `IMPLICIT`,\n`MANAGED`, and `UNKNOWN` consistently. This fixes implicit auth\nproviders such as Vertex AI rendering as missing in `/auth`.\n\n## Release Note\nFix `/auth` provider labels for implicit, local/no-auth, managed, and\nunknown credential states.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] Added unit coverage for both auth-label styles and the Vertex\nimplicit ADC regression.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f3b2e4f07aba21f1358beba2c4a4e32ff327ccee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f3b2e4f07aba21f1358beba2c4a4e32ff327ccee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8e743ac895c4e38df8efa192501b8993d37f94a7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIu5QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg10QAIsaqW9bbK9BBJ6FMUYUKpTT\n9EUclUU++7yO26cFB4H2GYzKi4gIpHKtH3YQMVCsxe36pmX2//3/v1iiFigZx4EB\n89JuvB2OUv6djehz3to04z/mzb4P+nNNl0MYWwgwPZZgL6AFf/5fDJwwsFyPBmXP\n4ST0aS25WQw1dASTVorOSW/VpXxeXUMa/R22tfXoA6amRcBIEAfPThw7wcdArvXe\nRCVvUv75KwDIoSPeyew/I9F/hV8lQnKB8jMFRkrxo6zIeMafEjxg4EiOBy9NZ+8g\nB6BRLKEP1lQdjjvlB32BW4o946L22jr1nEiL9LU8JSxRUMKFOAmxYVBCDSXaMCTr\nySeiriFRap2lnyessTQbrXTaUtF6ju98mJAn4BR21i1z3J6plejTGTBElPsn3v6n\nY7yt1BoI8a1F9yJH5xAYHjx2HIKUi37Ca/vH2NMQVOMZU0R04dIRJlL8W3hqH4wb\nQABnEBOpI1WTw6wOQ5f+0XoNyuXkZuwRQf2xagi99GWvUb8j0w0d4hOpHmi2mZsW\nDx4HQMicJTVfcBsk78zt91XTV1h6s0QYfEPLiYsM0kbEFD6fY5OltrBf+Wo7Ub1a\ndwYMB64BYiDG8oqR/ukobsTAseP9fINcvNXpONl4OQEFNYi4UT2/+R/a0XepG+d6\nDfTiHGFo8M2GbUt1C3Dd\n=FzEe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f3b2e4f07aba21f1358beba2c4a4e32ff327ccee\nparent 5694486b24e90f60f5f283f64b74c23509cfc5fc\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1780674128 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780674128 -0400\n\nfix(code): unify auth status labels (#3773)\n\n## Description\nUnifies provider auth status labels through one helper so `/auth` and\n`/model` interpret `CONFIGURED`, `MISSING`, `NOT_REQUIRED`, `IMPLICIT`,\n`MANAGED`, and `UNKNOWN` consistently. This fixes implicit auth\nproviders such as Vertex AI rendering as missing in `/auth`.\n\n## Release Note\nFix `/auth` provider labels for implicit, local/no-auth, managed, and\nunknown credential states.\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] Added unit coverage for both auth-label styles and the Vertex\nimplicit ADC regression.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-05T15:42:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e743ac895c4e38df8efa192501b8993d37f94a7","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8e743ac895c4e38df8efa192501b8993d37f94a7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8e743ac895c4e38df8efa192501b8993d37f94a7/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5694486b24e90f60f5f283f64b74c23509cfc5fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5694486b24e90f60f5f283f64b74c23509cfc5fc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5694486b24e90f60f5f283f64b74c23509cfc5fc"}]},{"sha":"5694486b24e90f60f5f283f64b74c23509cfc5fc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDU2OTQ0ODZiMjRlOTBmNjBmNWYyODNmNjRiNzRjMjM1MDljZmM1ZmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-05T04:30:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T04:30:17Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.10 (#3741)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.10](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.9...deepagents-code==0.1.10)\n(2026-06-05)\n\n### Features\n\n* Pair model API keys with their endpoints\n([#3770](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3770))\n([cf98030](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cf9803072dc0fdc1d5850c9fd2fc4eb6893ed8c9))\n* Word-level double-click selection\n([#3740](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3740))\n([4bb4286](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4bb4286a26c9c9bc69a36f2714d9eb0e3e5e4d40))\n* Blueprint bootstrapping for Runloop sandboxes\n([#3556](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3556))\n([13dafd8](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/13dafd8823c4b530c8e096012733ad74cd501b59))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Propagate runtime model switches to subagents\n([#3771](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3771))\n([f577182](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f577182c84746e625b65c3c2fda95f8ca21164cf))\n* Guard pasted-path probes against `OSError`\n([#3745](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3745))\n([c9617d3](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c9617d3594ab1448c4f3ee2212cdc66cbf138b77))\n* Keep startup import prewarm from crashing the TUI mid-upgrade\n([#3756](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3756))\n([867a2e5](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/867a2e5c341bd9dfa70b47c7fafc194ac51d7469))\n* Move MCP trust state out of user config\n([#3742](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3742))\n([a97f2fd](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a97f2fd394e6b0b943225a0195b0901188bd368c))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"be06ad7ed124e2856f6596adf7609354c7ad7621","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/be06ad7ed124e2856f6596adf7609354c7ad7621"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5694486b24e90f60f5f283f64b74c23509cfc5fc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIlDZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACEQQAJSIVm7+3gStMn4ub8d2plzG\nuAlUE66QE9/WFjDlNhA7E6qfmm/Fnjq/cmxPhGID0bp6RyQ3TW3ZdHRssZtn42Mz\nJYRAPZn8kEYzH8KRYgIpInBecXOZcq1Xv3GlFkPrAW/bXNv34+fZLpuPK5dPmBZd\nkaNfEoQWmHSHq/M0t/Nb5CgsN7Mgg/xnD2c1KM7AtexHDe3/wvkmYTVLaOnX0fIp\n9cc1U8wFwtpMs3/kWiTm1WMvvpL4CcZEWp9mwGnKALM/RfdYzf+gPMbPNwWDTqzW\ncT3LN9JXJ4tzFqKjeomOgSmakYeyg7Ma5GA1KqxPndJ4heUogI4pTc2P+zgIEnFq\nBA3oTAZVvk8/YCpXEVRRbk+09diTtPgML3XDTksTpz0UFo0qoTfoYyZkN9mjmS/T\nO54Udlwiq1TwMh46cydHDPNYGOri4QCfhjolnMRJGRzr5RVXyht9xO7JVBpq9psp\nhXIsotEqKkWLTl4UnryXPAgdIsnKARQKcmok6V/6yjEU1W7cZQX5zZENtiG7qRSx\nX97QdBOPRJU6u67SSJZdtUIo38frRL0FRNESuSp/4MIk2Nu+kcDm4hH8CuVrNnGE\nP6Gs8RsDFR3gWLP6piFD1rZAzf77RCHmMnxs/8UrYpmUZ5iraOqiNz5h+3HcYY4G\nHSOWoKjMvNneOxS8osp/\n=pjtJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree be06ad7ed124e2856f6596adf7609354c7ad7621\nparent f577182c84746e625b65c3c2fda95f8ca21164cf\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1780633817 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780633817 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.10 (#3741)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.10](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.9...deepagents-code==0.1.10)\n(2026-06-05)\n\n### Features\n\n* Pair model API keys with their endpoints\n([#3770](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3770))\n([cf98030](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cf9803072dc0fdc1d5850c9fd2fc4eb6893ed8c9))\n* Word-level double-click selection\n([#3740](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3740))\n([4bb4286](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4bb4286a26c9c9bc69a36f2714d9eb0e3e5e4d40))\n* Blueprint bootstrapping for Runloop sandboxes\n([#3556](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3556))\n([13dafd8](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/13dafd8823c4b530c8e096012733ad74cd501b59))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Propagate runtime model switches to subagents\n([#3771](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3771))\n([f577182](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f577182c84746e625b65c3c2fda95f8ca21164cf))\n* Guard pasted-path probes against `OSError`\n([#3745](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3745))\n([c9617d3](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c9617d3594ab1448c4f3ee2212cdc66cbf138b77))\n* Keep startup import prewarm from crashing the TUI mid-upgrade\n([#3756](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3756))\n([867a2e5](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/867a2e5c341bd9dfa70b47c7fafc194ac51d7469))\n* Move MCP trust state out of user config\n([#3742](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3742))\n([a97f2fd](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a97f2fd394e6b0b943225a0195b0901188bd368c))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-05T04:30:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5694486b24e90f60f5f283f64b74c23509cfc5fc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5694486b24e90f60f5f283f64b74c23509cfc5fc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5694486b24e90f60f5f283f64b74c23509cfc5fc/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f577182c84746e625b65c3c2fda95f8ca21164cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f577182c84746e625b65c3c2fda95f8ca21164cf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f577182c84746e625b65c3c2fda95f8ca21164cf"}]},{"sha":"f577182c84746e625b65c3c2fda95f8ca21164cf","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY1NzcxODJjODQ3NDZlNjI1YjY1YzNjMmZkYTk1ZjhjYTIxMTY0Y2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-05T04:20:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T04:20:14Z"},"message":"fix(code): propagate runtime model switches to subagents (#3771)\n\nFixes #2316\n\n---\n\nRuntime `/model` overrides should apply to subagents that inherit the\nCLI-selected model, but not to subagents that intentionally pin their\nown model. This adds `ConfigurableModelMiddleware` only to subagents\nwhose `AGENTS.md` omits `model:`, including the default\n`general-purpose` subagent.\n\nExamples:\n- No `model:` in a subagent config: after `/model\nanthropic:claude-opus-4-6`, that subagent follows the main session and\nuses Opus.\n- `model: anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5` in a subagent config: after the\nsame `/model` switch, that subagent keeps using Haiku because the model\nwas explicitly pinned.\n\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b22f120639e2024ea6f0821e09f7d791586f69da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b22f120639e2024ea6f0821e09f7d791586f69da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f577182c84746e625b65c3c2fda95f8ca21164cf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIk5+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXB0QAJduDfmO+nPukW5WOL1WEUa4\nI3ymJb4YLadDD+2bo9WoZXMsShVh4vcHnExxvUqxeUytJggqiBhjaL4bWrNYeIjt\nAciY/DaBP+mkG7NEhjzbyTuR03Ko8XN642pqHm757HSDdEgL+arKqwgEInEJT7Ra\nEp58UeA2wtIXt7cMYzl/dp035kzMq3Ka1JcmCplkpatU8Wj6s+EMvf3nNjsnlL4f\nEWEfCLdtPtxAlTLI458GiTBnPpeCtDvoRFdiqqEh09KBw/Cc1xo0if/xylznT8Z0\nAbR3TEkMd+wk+BVYx69PyflZLdkJ9EjYQbRQ3WzNhvLY7SBqFo+lwUBmN+lo10MN\nyGe2B1w0A1ej8O32TDoDeus4mGvbWnV+vACm+e5q0/kKewEdZIlqXawMdUVYcM2b\njv2gW4g57d9hp8lqObQhZmBOFCMn5j7WcbCXjvuDr1cZ4iLSgTd+dOOWq9whnEdZ\nCCWfh1ng8/+7nvqHrXM70WN2Bfe0p2HOMiwDuSK6FfUDhLQAiI/K3ucoVhZyXacP\nv0tPkgARC3BGR4davHtw6Ob6XHHdJbscOY9Nkk/cQ5i8QXiuXnvz3oH9g4zxHHcA\nVLYIShNSLr6D3Q7TJFbDQF9uabG4c5bLNHtRNyNU0f1cunTQUFiaYsv02dYrUF9x\n+jUULlsYeSbzbHhOxQu+\n=qbSu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b22f120639e2024ea6f0821e09f7d791586f69da\nparent cf9803072dc0fdc1d5850c9fd2fc4eb6893ed8c9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1780633214 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780633214 -0400\n\nfix(code): propagate runtime model switches to subagents (#3771)\n\nFixes #2316\n\n---\n\nRuntime `/model` overrides should apply to subagents that inherit the\nCLI-selected model, but not to subagents that intentionally pin their\nown model. This adds `ConfigurableModelMiddleware` only to subagents\nwhose `AGENTS.md` omits `model:`, including the default\n`general-purpose` subagent.\n\nExamples:\n- No `model:` in a subagent config: after `/model\nanthropic:claude-opus-4-6`, that subagent follows the main session and\nuses Opus.\n- `model: anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5` in a subagent config: after the\nsame `/model` switch, that subagent keeps using Haiku because the model\nwas explicitly pinned.\n\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-05T04:20:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f577182c84746e625b65c3c2fda95f8ca21164cf","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f577182c84746e625b65c3c2fda95f8ca21164cf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f577182c84746e625b65c3c2fda95f8ca21164cf/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cf9803072dc0fdc1d5850c9fd2fc4eb6893ed8c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cf9803072dc0fdc1d5850c9fd2fc4eb6893ed8c9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cf9803072dc0fdc1d5850c9fd2fc4eb6893ed8c9"}]},{"sha":"cf9803072dc0fdc1d5850c9fd2fc4eb6893ed8c9","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGNmOTgwMzA3MmRjMGZkYzFkNTg1MGM5ZmQyZmM0ZWI2ODkzZWQ4Yzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-05T04:09:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T04:09:18Z"},"message":"feat(code): pair model API keys with their endpoints (#3770)\n\nA provider's API key and its endpoint (`base_url`) are a coupled pair: a\ngateway's API key typically only authenticates against that specific\ngateway. A provider-native key only against the provider's own API.\n\nPreviously the two resolved through independent paths — keys honored\n`/auth`, the `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_` prefix, and env vars, while `base_url`\ncame only from `config.toml` or whatever the provider SDK happened to\nread from the environment. Overriding just the key (e.g. entering a\npersonal key in `/auth` on a machine provisioned with a model gateway)\nleft the gateway `base_url` in place, so the key shipped to the wrong\nendpoint and could fail with an opaque error message.\n\nThis makes the key and endpoint resolve and apply together. It also adds\n`/install <pkg> --package`, an escape hatch for providers whose package\nisn't a bundled extra.\n\n## Changes\n- `/auth` now stores an optional `base_url` alongside the key.\n`set_stored_key` takes a `base_url` param and `get_stored_base_url`\nreads it back; `ApiKeyCredential.base_url` is a new (non-secret,\nbackward-compatible) field, and legacy entries written before it read\ncleanly as `base_url=None`.\n- `apply_stored_credentials` applies the key and endpoint atomically via\n`_apply_stored_base_url`, which writes the canonical base-URL env var\nand **clears every alternate name** a provider's SDK might read (e.g.\nboth `OPENAI_API_BASE` and `OPENAI_BASE_URL`). A stored key with a blank\nURL clears any inherited gateway endpoint so it falls back to the\nprovider default rather than a leftover value.\n- `PROVIDER_BASE_URL_ENV` registers base-URL env vars (canonical name\nfirst) for ~16 providers — `anthropic`, `openai`, `google_genai`,\n`azure_openai`, `cohere`, `groq`, `mistralai`, `xai`, etc.\nOpenAI-compatible providers deliberately omit the shared\n`OPENAI_BASE_URL`. A `base_url_env` `ProviderConfig` field (parallel to\n`api_key_env`) lets an out-of-registry provider declare its own endpoint\nvariable.\n- `ModelConfig.get_base_url` resolution order is now: (1) `config.toml`\nliteral `base_url`; (2) the provider's base-URL env var via\n`resolve_env_var`, so a `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_*` override beats the plain\nname and the gateway-provisioned URL is honored in the default case; (3)\nthe stored `/auth` endpoint, for providers with no base-URL env var. A\ncorrupt credential store resolves to \"no endpoint\" rather than raising.\n- The `/auth` modal gains an optional base-URL `Input` with a three-tier\nhint (surviving `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_*` var → provider's endpoint var →\ngeneric default), and `on_input_submitted` saves the key/URL pair from\nEnter in either field. `action_cursor_up` lets Shift+Tab cycle back from\nthe new field.\n- Add `/install <pkg> --package` (TUI, via `_handle_install_package`)\nand `dcode --install <pkg> --package` (headless), running `uv tool\ninstall -U deepagents-code --with <pkg>` for providers outside the\ncurated extras. Package names are validated against a PEP 508 pattern\nand `shlex.quote`-d as defense in depth; editable, Homebrew, and uv-less\ninstalls are refused with actionable hints; `--force`/`--yes` is\nrequired since arbitrary packages have no allowlist.","tree":{"sha":"61ded47ee0fea2083130876afc29a26a80f62561","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/61ded47ee0fea2083130876afc29a26a80f62561"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/cf9803072dc0fdc1d5850c9fd2fc4eb6893ed8c9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIkvuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArqIQACkuKhfVBi76t2CdNwvhSFXT\nmpS+ZBQkfuCjz+MbXXwikUHI/KJfc1H4y0UanGvZKai3mBv8n/zug8AmwrS+GEsa\nTBPEFx9LZxb28TEo9J7B/iWZtcNSDJEJfpT9HJ/mKtdtG8hONUlagRUdEIUk1mqb\ndauuVr5cJNsoALPkNvgXsWqQj/GU4DDRqehURrGEPFbvIkS780jqgqtbbxQLAKaI\nawBv62zFTR9IavRylGK2DRMG1GJ46EaGzsCvp7pRu6a6VeUAwte9ZmpaOc68wZ/E\nawRUKs21FDPALCoz9qNO1LhWXRsv5zw2OBf11ovEhz7nVBej9HbQd53JmYxfuQ1n\npczeWQ9nb/ZzHt5psVSb4JXgcN5ybBFaJAnwfDTZg/IJfZSPcKKtozyPfYtX9i2c\nBuTNNjSRfXc2dQk2bxv2rgL18FerTfYxnQXhm2rACq3amXLTPt40fttbXNFVtt5Z\n7MfvsDmgTIJAUNbX1dcLCspDBDwTrEZSiZsfAmwRJdr8iH3HDjpH/tyxIsWHuupB\n7K5CbUPhczr3m10r+fZs2vcfJaQgal1fMlx+2wPCopF5gXBo1S8SAB0sSmtPHdRQ\nZ9nHy/uJF6mF4qxAA/qvjFD1WZPHInssLL/K8v1EemktnAguH0tZKiLr/ND56jmS\nemMhnP2HCiHx3IKnJ6ji\n=xuEb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 61ded47ee0fea2083130876afc29a26a80f62561\nparent 802ecc4a2246ba6a0ae56d4deca4c5eec06aafd2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1780632558 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780632558 -0400\n\nfeat(code): pair model API keys with their endpoints (#3770)\n\nA provider's API key and its endpoint (`base_url`) are a coupled pair: a\ngateway's API key typically only authenticates against that specific\ngateway. A provider-native key only against the provider's own API.\n\nPreviously the two resolved through independent paths — keys honored\n`/auth`, the `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_` prefix, and env vars, while `base_url`\ncame only from `config.toml` or whatever the provider SDK happened to\nread from the environment. Overriding just the key (e.g. entering a\npersonal key in `/auth` on a machine provisioned with a model gateway)\nleft the gateway `base_url` in place, so the key shipped to the wrong\nendpoint and could fail with an opaque error message.\n\nThis makes the key and endpoint resolve and apply together. It also adds\n`/install <pkg> --package`, an escape hatch for providers whose package\nisn't a bundled extra.\n\n## Changes\n- `/auth` now stores an optional `base_url` alongside the key.\n`set_stored_key` takes a `base_url` param and `get_stored_base_url`\nreads it back; `ApiKeyCredential.base_url` is a new (non-secret,\nbackward-compatible) field, and legacy entries written before it read\ncleanly as `base_url=None`.\n- `apply_stored_credentials` applies the key and endpoint atomically via\n`_apply_stored_base_url`, which writes the canonical base-URL env var\nand **clears every alternate name** a provider's SDK might read (e.g.\nboth `OPENAI_API_BASE` and `OPENAI_BASE_URL`). A stored key with a blank\nURL clears any inherited gateway endpoint so it falls back to the\nprovider default rather than a leftover value.\n- `PROVIDER_BASE_URL_ENV` registers base-URL env vars (canonical name\nfirst) for ~16 providers — `anthropic`, `openai`, `google_genai`,\n`azure_openai`, `cohere`, `groq`, `mistralai`, `xai`, etc.\nOpenAI-compatible providers deliberately omit the shared\n`OPENAI_BASE_URL`. A `base_url_env` `ProviderConfig` field (parallel to\n`api_key_env`) lets an out-of-registry provider declare its own endpoint\nvariable.\n- `ModelConfig.get_base_url` resolution order is now: (1) `config.toml`\nliteral `base_url`; (2) the provider's base-URL env var via\n`resolve_env_var`, so a `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_*` override beats the plain\nname and the gateway-provisioned URL is honored in the default case; (3)\nthe stored `/auth` endpoint, for providers with no base-URL env var. A\ncorrupt credential store resolves to \"no endpoint\" rather than raising.\n- The `/auth` modal gains an optional base-URL `Input` with a three-tier\nhint (surviving `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_*` var → provider's endpoint var →\ngeneric default), and `on_input_submitted` saves the key/URL pair from\nEnter in either field. `action_cursor_up` lets Shift+Tab cycle back from\nthe new field.\n- Add `/install <pkg> --package` (TUI, via `_handle_install_package`)\nand `dcode --install <pkg> --package` (headless), running `uv tool\ninstall -U deepagents-code --with <pkg>` for providers outside the\ncurated extras. Package names are validated against a PEP 508 pattern\nand `shlex.quote`-d as defense in depth; editable, Homebrew, and uv-less\ninstalls are refused with actionable hints; `--force`/`--yes` is\nrequired since arbitrary packages have no allowlist.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T04:09:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cf9803072dc0fdc1d5850c9fd2fc4eb6893ed8c9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/cf9803072dc0fdc1d5850c9fd2fc4eb6893ed8c9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/cf9803072dc0fdc1d5850c9fd2fc4eb6893ed8c9/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"802ecc4a2246ba6a0ae56d4deca4c5eec06aafd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/802ecc4a2246ba6a0ae56d4deca4c5eec06aafd2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/802ecc4a2246ba6a0ae56d4deca4c5eec06aafd2"}]},{"sha":"802ecc4a2246ba6a0ae56d4deca4c5eec06aafd2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgwMmVjYzRhMjI0NmJhNmEwYWU1NmQ0ZGVjYTRjNWVlYzA2YWFmZDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-05T03:04:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T03:04:35Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump starlette from 0.52.1 to 1.0.1 in /libs/code (#3767)\n\nBumps [starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette) from 0.52.1 to\n1.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/releases\">starlette's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 1.0.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3279\">Kludex/starlette#3279</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here! 🎉</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a>,\nand <a href=\"https://github.com/uSpike\"><code>@​uSpike</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years! ❤️</p>\n<p>Read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0\">https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0rc1</h2>\n<p>We're ready! 🚀</p>\n<p>The first release candidate for Starlette 1.0 is here! After years on\nZeroVer, we're finally making the jump.</p>\n<p>This release removes all deprecated features marked for 1.0.0, along\nwith some last-minute bug fixes.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years!</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/blob/main/docs/release-notes.md\">starlette's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.0.1 (May 21, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3279\">#3279</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0 (March 22, 2026)</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here!</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.\nThank you to everyone who tested the release candidate and reported\nissues.</p>\n<p>You can read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Track session access and modification in\n<code>SessionMiddleware</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3166\">#3166</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Handle websocket denial responses in <code>StreamingResponse</code>\nand <code>FileResponse</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3189\">#3189</a>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>bytearray</code> for field accumulation in\n<code>FormParser</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3179\">#3179</a>.</li>\n<li>Move <code>parser.finalize()</code> inside try/except in\n<code>MultiPartParser.parse()</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3153\">#3153</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0rc1 (February 23, 2026)</h2>\n<p>We're ready! I'm thrilled to announce the first release candidate for\nStarlette 1.0.</p>\n<p>Starlette was created in June 2018 by Tom Christie, and has been on\nZeroVer for years. Today, it's downloaded\nalmost <a href=\"https://pypistats.org/packages/starlette\">10 million\ntimes a day</a>, serves as the foundation for FastAPI,\nand has inspired many other frameworks. In the age of AI, Starlette\ncontinues to play an important role as a\ndependency of the Python MCP SDK.</p>\n<p>This release focuses on removing deprecated features that were marked\nfor removal in 1.0.0, along with some\nlast minute bug fixes. It's a release candidate, so we can gather\nfeedback from the community before the final\n1.0.0 release soon.</p>\n<p>A huge thank you to all the contributors who have helped make\nStarlette what it is today.\nIn particular, I'd like to recognize:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\">Kim Christie</a> - The\noriginal creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, and MkDocs, and the\ncurrent maintainer of HTTPX. Kim's work helped lay the foundation for\nthe modern async Python ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/adriangb\">Adrian Garcia Badaracco</a> -\nOne of the smartest people I know, whom I have the pleasure of working\nwith at Pydantic.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/graingert\">Thomas Grainger</a> - My\nasync teacher, always ready to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/agronholm\">Alex Grönholm</a> - Another\nasync mentor, always prompt to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\">Florimond Manca</a> -\nAlways present in the early days of both Starlette and Uvicorn, and\nhelped a lot in the ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\">Amin Alaee</a> - Contributed\na lot with file-related PRs.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\">Sebastián Ramírez</a> -\nMaintains FastAPI upstream, and always in contact to help with upstream\nissues.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\">Alex Oleshkevich</a> -\nHelped a lot on templates and many discussions.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/48f8e331b23ca692f4713ac1f370bff1b5cd034c\"><code>48f8e33</code></a>\nVersion 1.0.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3281\">#3281</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/f078832be1aa27ab0e7ec3153479a347749e967a\"><code>f078832</code></a>\nRemove Hugging Face sponsor block from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3280\">#3280</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/472951eba8f6e35be845fd1b91625a1b5488294b\"><code>472951e</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3277\">#3277</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/764dab0dcfb9033d75442d7a359645c9f94648c6\"><code>764dab0</code></a>\nIgnore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3279\">#3279</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/19d08115ce56da8d4da2838ecdd9c5882cb2b365\"><code>19d0811</code></a>\nHarden GitHub Actions workflows and Dependabot config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3276\">#3276</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/01f46378120fe2c6312074ed7e997e3b5f7d8c20\"><code>01f4637</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump idna from 3.10 to 3.15 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3274\">#3274</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/b8fa5140d2ef9f22483d777e936ab4c2df897179\"><code>b8fa514</code></a>\ndocs: fix typos in TestClient docs and test_requests comment (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3266\">#3266</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/e935b6b5d4616c2317bbdadfb4cf07a8e7637955\"><code>e935b6b</code></a>\nfix uvicorn domain (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3269\">#3269</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/96af9521a7e46bc0d00b5227186f03b70b6d242f\"><code>96af952</code></a>\nAdd 7-day cooldown for dependency resolution via uv exclude-newer (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3265\">#3265</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/61e385bd6dc438a90493c50f65ed232430f873fb\"><code>61e385b</code></a>\nAdd zizmor GitHub Actions security analysis workflow (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3264\">#3264</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2fa42e2db0948ab7098bfe2ecb8852c677d493f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2fa42e2db0948ab7098bfe2ecb8852c677d493f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/802ecc4a2246ba6a0ae56d4deca4c5eec06aafd2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIjzDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7CUQAAlugXiydI0gBtWle0cD/+aR\nTiKPv3Ei8Qgb9Bb7rUwHRANNeVFa89jtJ0cBjHBXlPaYMNps/PEFbOMGwUuDOwLa\nhITubydDfZZBz7A7X2NxyY8O6KnQxgNQP0Y6cFl9mny4eHXqJx/BLGqFpJhAdLnl\nB/yYl0rIwOKIcV2EizZowZm47s4WVocHrsXgy5paljB2YQ0MOMnpS2X8xc1ggFlC\nc5VWCRYku0zfwZcWM0CYYX/nO0CJ0YkTG2sA1WK4J6II75zp/HVza6ScZ0z4zDvb\ntWk/CNv0RX6wInluG2bbLtOqGDRf82KJX1pjSkbIllVIG+SsaltsjTRN9kyJiy7U\nW5IbXZyQDubGibgfxT8TyKanRmhqYgyuS7bddnnEngAIMFddLGCx3Suk80gjSt2v\nJ8iQ+KYMcoNypyQ2r5QqtRrY15nUdRQ5EQtl95UA1Lhbw1Dqh4XJF/0l75yhuwzP\nD9yCvGcyCvud1H1z8Y4WrVnDrJoo44wuRy8gRKhuywsDUtylB+rTyizqqn8r12Q5\n47xV4Z8JiI9eVRadXCDt15XIveEqrRMGu0xyN2UUdpmwagH4eZknswC9EfYNFGjJ\nbLY2gRLNcxOO5r7nwVPYKKpLzPe0Vz491ky4YkOzAB2K24vve38ZSakpX95uAi+t\nPVKZW+tD6El6RyH5PtDn\n=Z878\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2fa42e2db0948ab7098bfe2ecb8852c677d493f0\nparent 997121b8f2ee0c49260de07444003c0045724106\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1780628675 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780628675 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump starlette from 0.52.1 to 1.0.1 in /libs/code (#3767)\n\nBumps [starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette) from 0.52.1 to\n1.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/releases\">starlette's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 1.0.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3279\">Kludex/starlette#3279</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here! 🎉</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a>,\nand <a href=\"https://github.com/uSpike\"><code>@​uSpike</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years! ❤️</p>\n<p>Read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0\">https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0rc1</h2>\n<p>We're ready! 🚀</p>\n<p>The first release candidate for Starlette 1.0 is here! After years on\nZeroVer, we're finally making the jump.</p>\n<p>This release removes all deprecated features marked for 1.0.0, along\nwith some last-minute bug fixes.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years!</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/blob/main/docs/release-notes.md\">starlette's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.0.1 (May 21, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3279\">#3279</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0 (March 22, 2026)</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here!</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.\nThank you to everyone who tested the release candidate and reported\nissues.</p>\n<p>You can read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Track session access and modification in\n<code>SessionMiddleware</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3166\">#3166</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Handle websocket denial responses in <code>StreamingResponse</code>\nand <code>FileResponse</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3189\">#3189</a>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>bytearray</code> for field accumulation in\n<code>FormParser</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3179\">#3179</a>.</li>\n<li>Move <code>parser.finalize()</code> inside try/except in\n<code>MultiPartParser.parse()</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3153\">#3153</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0rc1 (February 23, 2026)</h2>\n<p>We're ready! I'm thrilled to announce the first release candidate for\nStarlette 1.0.</p>\n<p>Starlette was created in June 2018 by Tom Christie, and has been on\nZeroVer for years. Today, it's downloaded\nalmost <a href=\"https://pypistats.org/packages/starlette\">10 million\ntimes a day</a>, serves as the foundation for FastAPI,\nand has inspired many other frameworks. In the age of AI, Starlette\ncontinues to play an important role as a\ndependency of the Python MCP SDK.</p>\n<p>This release focuses on removing deprecated features that were marked\nfor removal in 1.0.0, along with some\nlast minute bug fixes. It's a release candidate, so we can gather\nfeedback from the community before the final\n1.0.0 release soon.</p>\n<p>A huge thank you to all the contributors who have helped make\nStarlette what it is today.\nIn particular, I'd like to recognize:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\">Kim Christie</a> - The\noriginal creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, and MkDocs, and the\ncurrent maintainer of HTTPX. Kim's work helped lay the foundation for\nthe modern async Python ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/adriangb\">Adrian Garcia Badaracco</a> -\nOne of the smartest people I know, whom I have the pleasure of working\nwith at Pydantic.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/graingert\">Thomas Grainger</a> - My\nasync teacher, always ready to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/agronholm\">Alex Grönholm</a> - Another\nasync mentor, always prompt to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\">Florimond Manca</a> -\nAlways present in the early days of both Starlette and Uvicorn, and\nhelped a lot in the ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\">Amin Alaee</a> - Contributed\na lot with file-related PRs.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\">Sebastián Ramírez</a> -\nMaintains FastAPI upstream, and always in contact to help with upstream\nissues.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\">Alex Oleshkevich</a> -\nHelped a lot on templates and many discussions.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/48f8e331b23ca692f4713ac1f370bff1b5cd034c\"><code>48f8e33</code></a>\nVersion 1.0.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3281\">#3281</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/f078832be1aa27ab0e7ec3153479a347749e967a\"><code>f078832</code></a>\nRemove Hugging Face sponsor block from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3280\">#3280</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/472951eba8f6e35be845fd1b91625a1b5488294b\"><code>472951e</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3277\">#3277</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/764dab0dcfb9033d75442d7a359645c9f94648c6\"><code>764dab0</code></a>\nIgnore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3279\">#3279</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/19d08115ce56da8d4da2838ecdd9c5882cb2b365\"><code>19d0811</code></a>\nHarden GitHub Actions workflows and Dependabot config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3276\">#3276</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/01f46378120fe2c6312074ed7e997e3b5f7d8c20\"><code>01f4637</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump idna from 3.10 to 3.15 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3274\">#3274</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/b8fa5140d2ef9f22483d777e936ab4c2df897179\"><code>b8fa514</code></a>\ndocs: fix typos in TestClient docs and test_requests comment (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3266\">#3266</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/e935b6b5d4616c2317bbdadfb4cf07a8e7637955\"><code>e935b6b</code></a>\nfix uvicorn domain (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3269\">#3269</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/96af9521a7e46bc0d00b5227186f03b70b6d242f\"><code>96af952</code></a>\nAdd 7-day cooldown for dependency resolution via uv exclude-newer (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3265\">#3265</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/61e385bd6dc438a90493c50f65ed232430f873fb\"><code>61e385b</code></a>\nAdd zizmor GitHub Actions security analysis workflow (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3264\">#3264</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-05T03:04:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/802ecc4a2246ba6a0ae56d4deca4c5eec06aafd2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/802ecc4a2246ba6a0ae56d4deca4c5eec06aafd2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/802ecc4a2246ba6a0ae56d4deca4c5eec06aafd2/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"997121b8f2ee0c49260de07444003c0045724106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/997121b8f2ee0c49260de07444003c0045724106","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/997121b8f2ee0c49260de07444003c0045724106"}]},{"sha":"997121b8f2ee0c49260de07444003c0045724106","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk5NzEyMWI4ZjJlZTBjNDkyNjBkZTA3NDQ0MDAzYzAwNDU3MjQxMDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-05T03:04:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T03:04:29Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump starlette from 0.52.1 to 1.0.1 in /examples/nvidia_deep_agent (#3769)\n\nBumps [starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette) from 0.52.1 to\n1.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/releases\">starlette's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 1.0.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3279\">Kludex/starlette#3279</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here! 🎉</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a>,\nand <a href=\"https://github.com/uSpike\"><code>@​uSpike</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years! ❤️</p>\n<p>Read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0\">https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0rc1</h2>\n<p>We're ready! 🚀</p>\n<p>The first release candidate for Starlette 1.0 is here! After years on\nZeroVer, we're finally making the jump.</p>\n<p>This release removes all deprecated features marked for 1.0.0, along\nwith some last-minute bug fixes.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years!</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/blob/main/docs/release-notes.md\">starlette's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.0.1 (May 21, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3279\">#3279</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0 (March 22, 2026)</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here!</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.\nThank you to everyone who tested the release candidate and reported\nissues.</p>\n<p>You can read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Track session access and modification in\n<code>SessionMiddleware</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3166\">#3166</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Handle websocket denial responses in <code>StreamingResponse</code>\nand <code>FileResponse</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3189\">#3189</a>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>bytearray</code> for field accumulation in\n<code>FormParser</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3179\">#3179</a>.</li>\n<li>Move <code>parser.finalize()</code> inside try/except in\n<code>MultiPartParser.parse()</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3153\">#3153</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0rc1 (February 23, 2026)</h2>\n<p>We're ready! I'm thrilled to announce the first release candidate for\nStarlette 1.0.</p>\n<p>Starlette was created in June 2018 by Tom Christie, and has been on\nZeroVer for years. Today, it's downloaded\nalmost <a href=\"https://pypistats.org/packages/starlette\">10 million\ntimes a day</a>, serves as the foundation for FastAPI,\nand has inspired many other frameworks. In the age of AI, Starlette\ncontinues to play an important role as a\ndependency of the Python MCP SDK.</p>\n<p>This release focuses on removing deprecated features that were marked\nfor removal in 1.0.0, along with some\nlast minute bug fixes. It's a release candidate, so we can gather\nfeedback from the community before the final\n1.0.0 release soon.</p>\n<p>A huge thank you to all the contributors who have helped make\nStarlette what it is today.\nIn particular, I'd like to recognize:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\">Kim Christie</a> - The\noriginal creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, and MkDocs, and the\ncurrent maintainer of HTTPX. Kim's work helped lay the foundation for\nthe modern async Python ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/adriangb\">Adrian Garcia Badaracco</a> -\nOne of the smartest people I know, whom I have the pleasure of working\nwith at Pydantic.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/graingert\">Thomas Grainger</a> - My\nasync teacher, always ready to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/agronholm\">Alex Grönholm</a> - Another\nasync mentor, always prompt to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\">Florimond Manca</a> -\nAlways present in the early days of both Starlette and Uvicorn, and\nhelped a lot in the ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\">Amin Alaee</a> - Contributed\na lot with file-related PRs.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\">Sebastián Ramírez</a> -\nMaintains FastAPI upstream, and always in contact to help with upstream\nissues.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\">Alex Oleshkevich</a> -\nHelped a lot on templates and many discussions.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/48f8e331b23ca692f4713ac1f370bff1b5cd034c\"><code>48f8e33</code></a>\nVersion 1.0.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3281\">#3281</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/f078832be1aa27ab0e7ec3153479a347749e967a\"><code>f078832</code></a>\nRemove Hugging Face sponsor block from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3280\">#3280</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/472951eba8f6e35be845fd1b91625a1b5488294b\"><code>472951e</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3277\">#3277</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/764dab0dcfb9033d75442d7a359645c9f94648c6\"><code>764dab0</code></a>\nIgnore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3279\">#3279</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/19d08115ce56da8d4da2838ecdd9c5882cb2b365\"><code>19d0811</code></a>\nHarden GitHub Actions workflows and Dependabot config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3276\">#3276</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/01f46378120fe2c6312074ed7e997e3b5f7d8c20\"><code>01f4637</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump idna from 3.10 to 3.15 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3274\">#3274</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/b8fa5140d2ef9f22483d777e936ab4c2df897179\"><code>b8fa514</code></a>\ndocs: fix typos in TestClient docs and test_requests comment (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3266\">#3266</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/e935b6b5d4616c2317bbdadfb4cf07a8e7637955\"><code>e935b6b</code></a>\nfix uvicorn domain (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3269\">#3269</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/96af9521a7e46bc0d00b5227186f03b70b6d242f\"><code>96af952</code></a>\nAdd 7-day cooldown for dependency resolution via uv exclude-newer (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3265\">#3265</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/61e385bd6dc438a90493c50f65ed232430f873fb\"><code>61e385b</code></a>\nAdd zizmor GitHub Actions security analysis workflow (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3264\">#3264</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ce199293baa564093177b3c1418badc44eba0744","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ce199293baa564093177b3c1418badc44eba0744"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/997121b8f2ee0c49260de07444003c0045724106","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIjy9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4xoQACM8a430xHS6N6RYVddK0s2P\np+/gFetGvXNKA2YglePoQDWIbkzn9/fLYOWsDFACNnklShKuDJzV0hiJi3QdM1Yn\nB7ZyIJzOl7cTk8cMHCnR3Fr8M62ZXnhbyXa2QWq0Bqf9YnnG0GHPXoxpo1cATYF5\nNZ2bg3q+tHDGtlOXPr52m0XwDoSnyLv8ksr7nrjck/oDJQTNvab70IbeTaIohd/r\nxKbNVDdEZS/dwbsdKD8TChS1yhu/Fp80X/pix8zquqQekNbHeYYvqObe38Uufi2c\nGTX2BSyfUJwIXOoQL47zCisrpqCRcmhxW8TaE6UqEwibMmT65wLyO77tYfg6XWB+\nJIlj1LsW8ta6kuii/jGPu/z9Ov3Nf3R0CazHm95YLGikD/V67dXutEp3EXEOEAgw\nBmTxWZ3OmYG00audrbxCLVuQGtyiOLcVq8CTfPd71aemLDLC+vHp2vwKhRLugsEi\nhAP+dlptmlXFmh72Bd1LeqURmNNHTCFSo6SK5G5FGsZAHnMYFyZ3f+o0NlJCLvig\nGbwPRXanqZth0m9r1W2lHuV4PP4zRrcr+MzAkNauin+KBQVpoII1xy79tYqsjCev\nf+5SBDwYmaGuDF+ryFYuO2wGSghdSl7q8+mHOlZclR1KAm4QnDM9+LaFlbzAvybz\nIaL7nUDhlBRPr6DHgA2o\n=9N1U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ce199293baa564093177b3c1418badc44eba0744\nparent 5ff807cc773bc983ee3e696672b685e3e3e54596\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1780628669 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780628669 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump starlette from 0.52.1 to 1.0.1 in /examples/nvidia_deep_agent (#3769)\n\nBumps [starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette) from 0.52.1 to\n1.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/releases\">starlette's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 1.0.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3279\">Kludex/starlette#3279</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here! 🎉</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a>,\nand <a href=\"https://github.com/uSpike\"><code>@​uSpike</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years! ❤️</p>\n<p>Read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0\">https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0rc1</h2>\n<p>We're ready! 🚀</p>\n<p>The first release candidate for Starlette 1.0 is here! After years on\nZeroVer, we're finally making the jump.</p>\n<p>This release removes all deprecated features marked for 1.0.0, along\nwith some last-minute bug fixes.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years!</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/blob/main/docs/release-notes.md\">starlette's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.0.1 (May 21, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3279\">#3279</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0 (March 22, 2026)</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here!</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.\nThank you to everyone who tested the release candidate and reported\nissues.</p>\n<p>You can read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Track session access and modification in\n<code>SessionMiddleware</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3166\">#3166</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Handle websocket denial responses in <code>StreamingResponse</code>\nand <code>FileResponse</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3189\">#3189</a>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>bytearray</code> for field accumulation in\n<code>FormParser</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3179\">#3179</a>.</li>\n<li>Move <code>parser.finalize()</code> inside try/except in\n<code>MultiPartParser.parse()</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3153\">#3153</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0rc1 (February 23, 2026)</h2>\n<p>We're ready! I'm thrilled to announce the first release candidate for\nStarlette 1.0.</p>\n<p>Starlette was created in June 2018 by Tom Christie, and has been on\nZeroVer for years. Today, it's downloaded\nalmost <a href=\"https://pypistats.org/packages/starlette\">10 million\ntimes a day</a>, serves as the foundation for FastAPI,\nand has inspired many other frameworks. In the age of AI, Starlette\ncontinues to play an important role as a\ndependency of the Python MCP SDK.</p>\n<p>This release focuses on removing deprecated features that were marked\nfor removal in 1.0.0, along with some\nlast minute bug fixes. It's a release candidate, so we can gather\nfeedback from the community before the final\n1.0.0 release soon.</p>\n<p>A huge thank you to all the contributors who have helped make\nStarlette what it is today.\nIn particular, I'd like to recognize:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\">Kim Christie</a> - The\noriginal creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, and MkDocs, and the\ncurrent maintainer of HTTPX. Kim's work helped lay the foundation for\nthe modern async Python ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/adriangb\">Adrian Garcia Badaracco</a> -\nOne of the smartest people I know, whom I have the pleasure of working\nwith at Pydantic.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/graingert\">Thomas Grainger</a> - My\nasync teacher, always ready to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/agronholm\">Alex Grönholm</a> - Another\nasync mentor, always prompt to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\">Florimond Manca</a> -\nAlways present in the early days of both Starlette and Uvicorn, and\nhelped a lot in the ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\">Amin Alaee</a> - Contributed\na lot with file-related PRs.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\">Sebastián Ramírez</a> -\nMaintains FastAPI upstream, and always in contact to help with upstream\nissues.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\">Alex Oleshkevich</a> -\nHelped a lot on templates and many discussions.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/48f8e331b23ca692f4713ac1f370bff1b5cd034c\"><code>48f8e33</code></a>\nVersion 1.0.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3281\">#3281</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/f078832be1aa27ab0e7ec3153479a347749e967a\"><code>f078832</code></a>\nRemove Hugging Face sponsor block from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3280\">#3280</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/472951eba8f6e35be845fd1b91625a1b5488294b\"><code>472951e</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3277\">#3277</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/764dab0dcfb9033d75442d7a359645c9f94648c6\"><code>764dab0</code></a>\nIgnore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3279\">#3279</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/19d08115ce56da8d4da2838ecdd9c5882cb2b365\"><code>19d0811</code></a>\nHarden GitHub Actions workflows and Dependabot config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3276\">#3276</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/01f46378120fe2c6312074ed7e997e3b5f7d8c20\"><code>01f4637</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump idna from 3.10 to 3.15 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3274\">#3274</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/b8fa5140d2ef9f22483d777e936ab4c2df897179\"><code>b8fa514</code></a>\ndocs: fix typos in TestClient docs and test_requests comment (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3266\">#3266</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/e935b6b5d4616c2317bbdadfb4cf07a8e7637955\"><code>e935b6b</code></a>\nfix uvicorn domain (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3269\">#3269</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/96af9521a7e46bc0d00b5227186f03b70b6d242f\"><code>96af952</code></a>\nAdd 7-day cooldown for dependency resolution via uv exclude-newer (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3265\">#3265</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/61e385bd6dc438a90493c50f65ed232430f873fb\"><code>61e385b</code></a>\nAdd zizmor GitHub Actions security analysis workflow (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3264\">#3264</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-05T03:04:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/997121b8f2ee0c49260de07444003c0045724106","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/997121b8f2ee0c49260de07444003c0045724106","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/997121b8f2ee0c49260de07444003c0045724106/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5ff807cc773bc983ee3e696672b685e3e3e54596","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5ff807cc773bc983ee3e696672b685e3e3e54596","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5ff807cc773bc983ee3e696672b685e3e3e54596"}]},{"sha":"5ff807cc773bc983ee3e696672b685e3e3e54596","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDVmZjgwN2NjNzczYmM5ODNlZTNlNjk2NjcyYjY4NWUzZTNlNTQ1OTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-04T22:33:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T22:33:53Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump starlette from 0.52.1 to 1.0.1 in /libs/evals (#3768)\n\nBumps [starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette) from 0.52.1 to\n1.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/releases\">starlette's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 1.0.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3279\">Kludex/starlette#3279</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here! 🎉</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a>,\nand <a href=\"https://github.com/uSpike\"><code>@​uSpike</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years! ❤️</p>\n<p>Read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0\">https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0rc1</h2>\n<p>We're ready! 🚀</p>\n<p>The first release candidate for Starlette 1.0 is here! After years on\nZeroVer, we're finally making the jump.</p>\n<p>This release removes all deprecated features marked for 1.0.0, along\nwith some last-minute bug fixes.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years!</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/blob/main/docs/release-notes.md\">starlette's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.0.1 (May 21, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3279\">#3279</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0 (March 22, 2026)</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here!</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.\nThank you to everyone who tested the release candidate and reported\nissues.</p>\n<p>You can read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Track session access and modification in\n<code>SessionMiddleware</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3166\">#3166</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Handle websocket denial responses in <code>StreamingResponse</code>\nand <code>FileResponse</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3189\">#3189</a>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>bytearray</code> for field accumulation in\n<code>FormParser</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3179\">#3179</a>.</li>\n<li>Move <code>parser.finalize()</code> inside try/except in\n<code>MultiPartParser.parse()</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3153\">#3153</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0rc1 (February 23, 2026)</h2>\n<p>We're ready! I'm thrilled to announce the first release candidate for\nStarlette 1.0.</p>\n<p>Starlette was created in June 2018 by Tom Christie, and has been on\nZeroVer for years. Today, it's downloaded\nalmost <a href=\"https://pypistats.org/packages/starlette\">10 million\ntimes a day</a>, serves as the foundation for FastAPI,\nand has inspired many other frameworks. In the age of AI, Starlette\ncontinues to play an important role as a\ndependency of the Python MCP SDK.</p>\n<p>This release focuses on removing deprecated features that were marked\nfor removal in 1.0.0, along with some\nlast minute bug fixes. It's a release candidate, so we can gather\nfeedback from the community before the final\n1.0.0 release soon.</p>\n<p>A huge thank you to all the contributors who have helped make\nStarlette what it is today.\nIn particular, I'd like to recognize:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\">Kim Christie</a> - The\noriginal creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, and MkDocs, and the\ncurrent maintainer of HTTPX. Kim's work helped lay the foundation for\nthe modern async Python ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/adriangb\">Adrian Garcia Badaracco</a> -\nOne of the smartest people I know, whom I have the pleasure of working\nwith at Pydantic.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/graingert\">Thomas Grainger</a> - My\nasync teacher, always ready to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/agronholm\">Alex Grönholm</a> - Another\nasync mentor, always prompt to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\">Florimond Manca</a> -\nAlways present in the early days of both Starlette and Uvicorn, and\nhelped a lot in the ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\">Amin Alaee</a> - Contributed\na lot with file-related PRs.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\">Sebastián Ramírez</a> -\nMaintains FastAPI upstream, and always in contact to help with upstream\nissues.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\">Alex Oleshkevich</a> -\nHelped a lot on templates and many discussions.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/48f8e331b23ca692f4713ac1f370bff1b5cd034c\"><code>48f8e33</code></a>\nVersion 1.0.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3281\">#3281</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/f078832be1aa27ab0e7ec3153479a347749e967a\"><code>f078832</code></a>\nRemove Hugging Face sponsor block from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3280\">#3280</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/472951eba8f6e35be845fd1b91625a1b5488294b\"><code>472951e</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3277\">#3277</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/764dab0dcfb9033d75442d7a359645c9f94648c6\"><code>764dab0</code></a>\nIgnore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3279\">#3279</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/19d08115ce56da8d4da2838ecdd9c5882cb2b365\"><code>19d0811</code></a>\nHarden GitHub Actions workflows and Dependabot config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3276\">#3276</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/01f46378120fe2c6312074ed7e997e3b5f7d8c20\"><code>01f4637</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump idna from 3.10 to 3.15 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3274\">#3274</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/b8fa5140d2ef9f22483d777e936ab4c2df897179\"><code>b8fa514</code></a>\ndocs: fix typos in TestClient docs and test_requests comment (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3266\">#3266</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/e935b6b5d4616c2317bbdadfb4cf07a8e7637955\"><code>e935b6b</code></a>\nfix uvicorn domain (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3269\">#3269</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/96af9521a7e46bc0d00b5227186f03b70b6d242f\"><code>96af952</code></a>\nAdd 7-day cooldown for dependency resolution via uv exclude-newer (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3265\">#3265</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/61e385bd6dc438a90493c50f65ed232430f873fb\"><code>61e385b</code></a>\nAdd zizmor GitHub Actions security analysis workflow (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3264\">#3264</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=starlette&package-manager=uv&previous-version=0.52.1&new-version=1.0.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"96b60d55406dca8dac0dcb10a0f3fa0381d9a654","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/96b60d55406dca8dac0dcb10a0f3fa0381d9a654"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5ff807cc773bc983ee3e696672b685e3e3e54596","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIf1RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA//MQAAsGdHYa6YlEW6bpSsxfN5Rw\n4Zm4+rWYac+gfShUQKH1NUGe5IZ8t9RgyVWjXsvmbUxeevJopAcayax3h9swEqVL\nkD7czgBXzz7grRMQIxHzZjVotESCWEnNh0UKOexIN+RuH/3+VSmKmznmiuyafwrm\n7JnvsQ/Bn38GaurnyqxxBjfO3grIzKeuMmHSRYbFGxgDwu4ByG1x7P78RcVqGtBa\nH3xYhhXT84aTVDCSnA+meKQwV3B+q14riSQbtxdTVLwpc/XVQgNmHmvv//TokdXz\nfgqjbl0ZdHe1lJWecL4SLj/jW363dqXhd7LUgCwcwDXtXp7wyfQYUJvz5TSzSvB4\ngRD1dVnjxqoBqY1kDCIUP2q8gfSoR0veA33t+fWMfYbegELNHBzvAQP2RgJk3eDF\njgZsmCK9Y+dbfGD8M6ukS+a0oHQn9FI6hjYUL5tU5BiT9vqKjadBVASdTEeO4iZr\nH2zq1wVrVmZLcpWloZuMPtwzgyVHNGJ5bJyR4IKSbmFWeoc9HajmW1hBLNDwC5MP\n9yS6X+zCxmPEBUAcdQ7W3TXbXUyA7xtiI2RkjjvBA7zyO9pfMoj7ZNV/LaJH1ZSs\nZ+K4BZk2lN34Wcy/5EEWKhjL+x/l3gBKyq0xpTou9FAwLxc7vlm33I1lVI6gD+IO\n0TwBi9AazLPWz0SkhAos\n=9TLm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 96b60d55406dca8dac0dcb10a0f3fa0381d9a654\nparent 460ce551b1095d4b74478f7f23a160d09d4ab668\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1780612433 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780612433 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump starlette from 0.52.1 to 1.0.1 in /libs/evals (#3768)\n\nBumps [starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette) from 0.52.1 to\n1.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/releases\">starlette's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 1.0.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3279\">Kludex/starlette#3279</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here! 🎉</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a>,\nand <a href=\"https://github.com/uSpike\"><code>@​uSpike</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years! ❤️</p>\n<p>Read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0\">https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0rc1</h2>\n<p>We're ready! 🚀</p>\n<p>The first release candidate for Starlette 1.0 is here! After years on\nZeroVer, we're finally making the jump.</p>\n<p>This release removes all deprecated features marked for 1.0.0, along\nwith some last-minute bug fixes.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years!</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/blob/main/docs/release-notes.md\">starlette's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.0.1 (May 21, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3279\">#3279</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0 (March 22, 2026)</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here!</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.\nThank you to everyone who tested the release candidate and reported\nissues.</p>\n<p>You can read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Track session access and modification in\n<code>SessionMiddleware</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3166\">#3166</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Handle websocket denial responses in <code>StreamingResponse</code>\nand <code>FileResponse</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3189\">#3189</a>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>bytearray</code> for field accumulation in\n<code>FormParser</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3179\">#3179</a>.</li>\n<li>Move <code>parser.finalize()</code> inside try/except in\n<code>MultiPartParser.parse()</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3153\">#3153</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0rc1 (February 23, 2026)</h2>\n<p>We're ready! I'm thrilled to announce the first release candidate for\nStarlette 1.0.</p>\n<p>Starlette was created in June 2018 by Tom Christie, and has been on\nZeroVer for years. Today, it's downloaded\nalmost <a href=\"https://pypistats.org/packages/starlette\">10 million\ntimes a day</a>, serves as the foundation for FastAPI,\nand has inspired many other frameworks. In the age of AI, Starlette\ncontinues to play an important role as a\ndependency of the Python MCP SDK.</p>\n<p>This release focuses on removing deprecated features that were marked\nfor removal in 1.0.0, along with some\nlast minute bug fixes. It's a release candidate, so we can gather\nfeedback from the community before the final\n1.0.0 release soon.</p>\n<p>A huge thank you to all the contributors who have helped make\nStarlette what it is today.\nIn particular, I'd like to recognize:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\">Kim Christie</a> - The\noriginal creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, and MkDocs, and the\ncurrent maintainer of HTTPX. Kim's work helped lay the foundation for\nthe modern async Python ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/adriangb\">Adrian Garcia Badaracco</a> -\nOne of the smartest people I know, whom I have the pleasure of working\nwith at Pydantic.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/graingert\">Thomas Grainger</a> - My\nasync teacher, always ready to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/agronholm\">Alex Grönholm</a> - Another\nasync mentor, always prompt to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\">Florimond Manca</a> -\nAlways present in the early days of both Starlette and Uvicorn, and\nhelped a lot in the ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\">Amin Alaee</a> - Contributed\na lot with file-related PRs.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\">Sebastián Ramírez</a> -\nMaintains FastAPI upstream, and always in contact to help with upstream\nissues.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\">Alex Oleshkevich</a> -\nHelped a lot on templates and many discussions.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/48f8e331b23ca692f4713ac1f370bff1b5cd034c\"><code>48f8e33</code></a>\nVersion 1.0.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3281\">#3281</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/f078832be1aa27ab0e7ec3153479a347749e967a\"><code>f078832</code></a>\nRemove Hugging Face sponsor block from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3280\">#3280</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/472951eba8f6e35be845fd1b91625a1b5488294b\"><code>472951e</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3277\">#3277</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/764dab0dcfb9033d75442d7a359645c9f94648c6\"><code>764dab0</code></a>\nIgnore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3279\">#3279</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/19d08115ce56da8d4da2838ecdd9c5882cb2b365\"><code>19d0811</code></a>\nHarden GitHub Actions workflows and Dependabot config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3276\">#3276</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/01f46378120fe2c6312074ed7e997e3b5f7d8c20\"><code>01f4637</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump idna from 3.10 to 3.15 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3274\">#3274</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/b8fa5140d2ef9f22483d777e936ab4c2df897179\"><code>b8fa514</code></a>\ndocs: fix typos in TestClient docs and test_requests comment (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3266\">#3266</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/e935b6b5d4616c2317bbdadfb4cf07a8e7637955\"><code>e935b6b</code></a>\nfix uvicorn domain (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3269\">#3269</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/96af9521a7e46bc0d00b5227186f03b70b6d242f\"><code>96af952</code></a>\nAdd 7-day cooldown for dependency resolution via uv exclude-newer (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3265\">#3265</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/61e385bd6dc438a90493c50f65ed232430f873fb\"><code>61e385b</code></a>\nAdd zizmor GitHub Actions security analysis workflow (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3264\">#3264</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=starlette&package-manager=uv&previous-version=0.52.1&new-version=1.0.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-04T22:33:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5ff807cc773bc983ee3e696672b685e3e3e54596","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5ff807cc773bc983ee3e696672b685e3e3e54596","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5ff807cc773bc983ee3e696672b685e3e3e54596/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"460ce551b1095d4b74478f7f23a160d09d4ab668","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/460ce551b1095d4b74478f7f23a160d09d4ab668","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/460ce551b1095d4b74478f7f23a160d09d4ab668"}]},{"sha":"460ce551b1095d4b74478f7f23a160d09d4ab668","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQ2MGNlNTUxYjEwOTVkNGI3NDQ3OGY3ZjIzYTE2MGQwOWQ0YWI2Njg","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-04T19:21:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T19:21:00Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump starlette from 0.50.0 to 1.0.1 in /examples/deep_research (#3764)\n\nBumps [starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette) from 0.50.0 to\n1.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/releases\">starlette's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 1.0.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3279\">Kludex/starlette#3279</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here! 🎉</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a>,\nand <a href=\"https://github.com/uSpike\"><code>@​uSpike</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years! ❤️</p>\n<p>Read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0\">https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0rc1</h2>\n<p>We're ready! 🚀</p>\n<p>The first release candidate for Starlette 1.0 is here! After years on\nZeroVer, we're finally making the jump.</p>\n<p>This release removes all deprecated features marked for 1.0.0, along\nwith some last-minute bug fixes.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years!</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 0.52.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Only use <code>typing_extensions</code> in older Python versions by\n<a href=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3109\">Kludex/starlette#3109</a></li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/blob/main/docs/release-notes.md\">starlette's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.0.1 (May 21, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3279\">#3279</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0 (March 22, 2026)</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here!</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.\nThank you to everyone who tested the release candidate and reported\nissues.</p>\n<p>You can read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Track session access and modification in\n<code>SessionMiddleware</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3166\">#3166</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Handle websocket denial responses in <code>StreamingResponse</code>\nand <code>FileResponse</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3189\">#3189</a>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>bytearray</code> for field accumulation in\n<code>FormParser</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3179\">#3179</a>.</li>\n<li>Move <code>parser.finalize()</code> inside try/except in\n<code>MultiPartParser.parse()</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3153\">#3153</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0rc1 (February 23, 2026)</h2>\n<p>We're ready! I'm thrilled to announce the first release candidate for\nStarlette 1.0.</p>\n<p>Starlette was created in June 2018 by Tom Christie, and has been on\nZeroVer for years. Today, it's downloaded\nalmost <a href=\"https://pypistats.org/packages/starlette\">10 million\ntimes a day</a>, serves as the foundation for FastAPI,\nand has inspired many other frameworks. In the age of AI, Starlette\ncontinues to play an important role as a\ndependency of the Python MCP SDK.</p>\n<p>This release focuses on removing deprecated features that were marked\nfor removal in 1.0.0, along with some\nlast minute bug fixes. It's a release candidate, so we can gather\nfeedback from the community before the final\n1.0.0 release soon.</p>\n<p>A huge thank you to all the contributors who have helped make\nStarlette what it is today.\nIn particular, I'd like to recognize:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\">Kim Christie</a> - The\noriginal creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, and MkDocs, and the\ncurrent maintainer of HTTPX. Kim's work helped lay the foundation for\nthe modern async Python ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/adriangb\">Adrian Garcia Badaracco</a> -\nOne of the smartest people I know, whom I have the pleasure of working\nwith at Pydantic.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/graingert\">Thomas Grainger</a> - My\nasync teacher, always ready to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/agronholm\">Alex Grönholm</a> - Another\nasync mentor, always prompt to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\">Florimond Manca</a> -\nAlways present in the early days of both Starlette and Uvicorn, and\nhelped a lot in the ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\">Amin Alaee</a> - Contributed\na lot with file-related PRs.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\">Sebastián Ramírez</a> -\nMaintains FastAPI upstream, and always in contact to help with upstream\nissues.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\">Alex Oleshkevich</a> -\nHelped a lot on templates and many discussions.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/48f8e331b23ca692f4713ac1f370bff1b5cd034c\"><code>48f8e33</code></a>\nVersion 1.0.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3281\">#3281</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/f078832be1aa27ab0e7ec3153479a347749e967a\"><code>f078832</code></a>\nRemove Hugging Face sponsor block from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3280\">#3280</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/472951eba8f6e35be845fd1b91625a1b5488294b\"><code>472951e</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3277\">#3277</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/764dab0dcfb9033d75442d7a359645c9f94648c6\"><code>764dab0</code></a>\nIgnore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3279\">#3279</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/19d08115ce56da8d4da2838ecdd9c5882cb2b365\"><code>19d0811</code></a>\nHarden GitHub Actions workflows and Dependabot config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3276\">#3276</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/01f46378120fe2c6312074ed7e997e3b5f7d8c20\"><code>01f4637</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump idna from 3.10 to 3.15 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3274\">#3274</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/b8fa5140d2ef9f22483d777e936ab4c2df897179\"><code>b8fa514</code></a>\ndocs: fix typos in TestClient docs and test_requests comment (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3266\">#3266</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/e935b6b5d4616c2317bbdadfb4cf07a8e7637955\"><code>e935b6b</code></a>\nfix uvicorn domain (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3269\">#3269</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/96af9521a7e46bc0d00b5227186f03b70b6d242f\"><code>96af952</code></a>\nAdd 7-day cooldown for dependency resolution via uv exclude-newer (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3265\">#3265</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/61e385bd6dc438a90493c50f65ed232430f873fb\"><code>61e385b</code></a>\nAdd zizmor GitHub Actions security analysis workflow (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3264\">#3264</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.50.0...1.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=starlette&package-manager=uv&previous-version=0.50.0&new-version=1.0.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a1b432d63b70bad23ef18733ffe4cae92dbf485a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a1b432d63b70bad23ef18733ffe4cae92dbf485a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/460ce551b1095d4b74478f7f23a160d09d4ab668","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIdAcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfNgQAGhrnh2UhqvPNo3aU8fAtYW1\nQJ3IV2Z+Se61ElCT2zvO5AP0Medrq+WWUeTNyDZA6n98bVX6QcJFcXvcsDNCzxfP\nbC0riJSbUjtmA5BdKoxLx5IssL5PD2GtEeHe0dK1eYipmSV70jdyeTPYwlf/CiX6\n5qxu4W/jo/NEpFZEMt+kfpCYGIKO8tQBn4OWXh6MlMpWZrAA4FdYabE5el0u7CBp\nt0O8P2j4kEuhJMLw79Td45Dzj9FIwYPDc/bisIrnLCO8bXAyPXBz9dWdMuo7PVG5\nACNIjDP1yr3zdDzo89NReLGQMvnXD0Wz7wGvYhE1d13GgB/yDBlJmqIRnSvdSDPd\nUftLBFDOHA2IW//wQjbMhOdxOlCpreeuQ71Bsf++7b965SWdAP6QOij/bPgBBYiR\nji0t0ba+QK/rJa1odY/RV8p+Px41rOHEFa34unp7NQsM+cW9ImVfyRv3aN/LiSfF\nfM5Islp1JVnIbjaLvc5+cnhwxB+o1KlgvEHxuCJMO4UcFYnYz6LtdgKwXqYhtgDN\nv27WrvBdK2fnFA3R+PTlWaMVmQ+LBkqXLgphq8bisK9tlq/hAKJL7+Zph3s4ytWz\njqsU3Aq9NNj++5H+SfFMXi+8fpKcsOU926BEyfOqjk4ktQgFpTcCfexoFBIrZt6d\nZNbOH/y4ZC03/4ehEyYt\n=9BR9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a1b432d63b70bad23ef18733ffe4cae92dbf485a\nparent e0f4e919a20916e78b5965378adc9aae014d0cb7\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1780600860 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780600860 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump starlette from 0.50.0 to 1.0.1 in /examples/deep_research (#3764)\n\nBumps [starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette) from 0.50.0 to\n1.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/releases\">starlette's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 1.0.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3279\">Kludex/starlette#3279</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.0...1.0.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here! 🎉</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a>,\nand <a href=\"https://github.com/uSpike\"><code>@​uSpike</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years! ❤️</p>\n<p>Read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100-march-22-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0\">https://github.com/encode/starlette/compare/1.0.0rc1...1.0.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.0.0rc1</h2>\n<p>We're ready! 🚀</p>\n<p>The first release candidate for Starlette 1.0 is here! After years on\nZeroVer, we're finally making the jump.</p>\n<p>This release removes all deprecated features marked for 1.0.0, along\nwith some last-minute bug fixes.</p>\n<p>A special thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\"><code>@​lovelydinosaur</code></a>,\nthe creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, HTTPX and MkDocs, whose work helped\nto lay the foundation for the modern async Python ecosystem. 🙏</p>\n<p>Thank you to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/adriangb\"><code>@​adriangb</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/agronholm\"><code>@​agronholm</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\"><code>@​florimondmanca</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\"><code>@​aminalaee</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\"><code>@​alex-oleshkevich</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/abersheeran\"><code>@​abersheeran</code></a> for\nhelping make Starlette what it is today. And to all my sponsors -\nespecially <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/huggingface\"><code>@​huggingface</code></a>,\nand <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/elevenlabs\"><code>@​elevenlabs</code></a> -\nthank you for your support!</p>\n<p>Thank you to all <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/encode/starlette/graphs/contributors\">290+\ncontributors</a> who have shaped Starlette over the years!</p>\n<p>Check out the full release notes at <a\nhref=\"https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026\">https://www.starlette.io/release-notes/#100rc1-february-23-2026</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/0.52.1...1.0.0rc1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 0.52.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Only use <code>typing_extensions</code> in older Python versions by\n<a href=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3109\">Kludex/starlette#3109</a></li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/blob/main/docs/release-notes.md\">starlette's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.0.1 (May 21, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3279\">#3279</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0 (March 22, 2026)</h2>\n<p>Starlette 1.0 is here!</p>\n<p>After nearly eight years since its creation, Starlette has reached\nits first stable release.\nThank you to everyone who tested the release candidate and reported\nissues.</p>\n<p>You can read more on the <a\nhref=\"https://marcelotryle.com/blog/2026/03/22/starlette-10-is-here/\">blog\npost</a>.</p>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Track session access and modification in\n<code>SessionMiddleware</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3166\">#3166</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Handle websocket denial responses in <code>StreamingResponse</code>\nand <code>FileResponse</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3189\">#3189</a>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>bytearray</code> for field accumulation in\n<code>FormParser</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3179\">#3179</a>.</li>\n<li>Move <code>parser.finalize()</code> inside try/except in\n<code>MultiPartParser.parse()</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3153\">#3153</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.0.0rc1 (February 23, 2026)</h2>\n<p>We're ready! I'm thrilled to announce the first release candidate for\nStarlette 1.0.</p>\n<p>Starlette was created in June 2018 by Tom Christie, and has been on\nZeroVer for years. Today, it's downloaded\nalmost <a href=\"https://pypistats.org/packages/starlette\">10 million\ntimes a day</a>, serves as the foundation for FastAPI,\nand has inspired many other frameworks. In the age of AI, Starlette\ncontinues to play an important role as a\ndependency of the Python MCP SDK.</p>\n<p>This release focuses on removing deprecated features that were marked\nfor removal in 1.0.0, along with some\nlast minute bug fixes. It's a release candidate, so we can gather\nfeedback from the community before the final\n1.0.0 release soon.</p>\n<p>A huge thank you to all the contributors who have helped make\nStarlette what it is today.\nIn particular, I'd like to recognize:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/lovelydinosaur\">Kim Christie</a> - The\noriginal creator of Starlette, Uvicorn, and MkDocs, and the\ncurrent maintainer of HTTPX. Kim's work helped lay the foundation for\nthe modern async Python ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/adriangb\">Adrian Garcia Badaracco</a> -\nOne of the smartest people I know, whom I have the pleasure of working\nwith at Pydantic.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/graingert\">Thomas Grainger</a> - My\nasync teacher, always ready to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/agronholm\">Alex Grönholm</a> - Another\nasync mentor, always prompt to help with questions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/florimondmanca\">Florimond Manca</a> -\nAlways present in the early days of both Starlette and Uvicorn, and\nhelped a lot in the ecosystem.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/aminalaee\">Amin Alaee</a> - Contributed\na lot with file-related PRs.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\">Sebastián Ramírez</a> -\nMaintains FastAPI upstream, and always in contact to help with upstream\nissues.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/alex-oleshkevich\">Alex Oleshkevich</a> -\nHelped a lot on templates and many discussions.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/48f8e331b23ca692f4713ac1f370bff1b5cd034c\"><code>48f8e33</code></a>\nVersion 1.0.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3281\">#3281</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/f078832be1aa27ab0e7ec3153479a347749e967a\"><code>f078832</code></a>\nRemove Hugging Face sponsor block from docs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3280\">#3280</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/472951eba8f6e35be845fd1b91625a1b5488294b\"><code>472951e</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump the github-actions group with 2 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3277\">#3277</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/764dab0dcfb9033d75442d7a359645c9f94648c6\"><code>764dab0</code></a>\nIgnore malformed <code>Host</code> header when constructing\n<code>request.url</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3279\">#3279</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/19d08115ce56da8d4da2838ecdd9c5882cb2b365\"><code>19d0811</code></a>\nHarden GitHub Actions workflows and Dependabot config (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3276\">#3276</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/01f46378120fe2c6312074ed7e997e3b5f7d8c20\"><code>01f4637</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump idna from 3.10 to 3.15 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3274\">#3274</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/b8fa5140d2ef9f22483d777e936ab4c2df897179\"><code>b8fa514</code></a>\ndocs: fix typos in TestClient docs and test_requests comment (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3266\">#3266</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/e935b6b5d4616c2317bbdadfb4cf07a8e7637955\"><code>e935b6b</code></a>\nfix uvicorn domain (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3269\">#3269</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/96af9521a7e46bc0d00b5227186f03b70b6d242f\"><code>96af952</code></a>\nAdd 7-day cooldown for dependency resolution via uv exclude-newer (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3265\">#3265</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/61e385bd6dc438a90493c50f65ed232430f873fb\"><code>61e385b</code></a>\nAdd zizmor GitHub Actions security analysis workflow (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3264\">#3264</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https