b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE2NjNjYWQ4ODU4YTc4YTVkMDYzYWYwYzUxYmI3ODliZmIxYWJhMmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"open-swe[bot]","email":"215916821+open-swe[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-03T15:23:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T15:23:10Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): pass through summarization factory prompt knobs (#3559)\n\nCloses #2622\n\n---\n\nAdds keyword-only controls for summarization prompt, trim limit, token\ncounter, and compact-tool system prompt while preserving model-aware\ntrigger/keep defaults. Brings to parity with class init.\n\n_Opened collaboratively by Mason Daugherty and open-swe._\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <61371264+mdrxy@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"5ae41b875b5ae0b7a628b88bb87b4b6c85c97a0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5ae41b875b5ae0b7a628b88bb87b4b6c85c97a0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a663cad8858a78a5d063af0c51bb789bfb1aba2b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIEbeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAF1EQAEHc0ZbU34jwnWbLvTG4cqsL\ntfK2TV2lQF34q4XNoAtH+1QmyoR1mUt46SORav1vYVsJ8BHEK0rAVpDLUu4Unahb\n6TP2EqSDaZZzpAajomO/ov3XzIuc728Iwcrdh8bwtu5nyVDLwNj9rjjRdVpP46h1\n1F83R9hzHp1PdSeI0G/xK7huAy4oWmGIMMFhSi64JW0FCGX0/lCJJxj1ai6NGjiB\nwF+jvpKM+t7jFhOki+XJUkvNS0mqtaKCQPirv5/LBSJxZziFu2s8kSjXaVZb/hMJ\nUqQD4HFrO+hRPD6VikQ6Cj3tCOSwUTiyjEQ6bBTTI00c05AcYRlHq1STUaaQTom4\nt+9ASPJG3qTkQ5kz30XJdfxo1jUB6h2vVt3pV3npIBaj8hrRZC6T7gapF60l6UXs\nn20xohC8okI5DgkJLdRNK2E8dRbp5VgmE1u0UM5Dlo6fF/F2t7bPtDkvPmDgBwBU\nNkaZm2uwp2YpokK9jhqH6JY6RVd6Bd2aD8hd7/QQUd+2Jz9g0heoBzCaO1viPAjW\nwO25fibX1/e9ReyJ8OPglPasSCPAX5QnUT9cPvv2pS8mOPM/NV/zBmwKz87GPAEF\ntleYyCes/F14HdpHj7i0TigPTCE9pO5anYmwzftt0JGYrzVUZh0i9p/+eXVglqxz\n18oxGk/dqyA6vde2+liC\n=TGLl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5ae41b875b5ae0b7a628b88bb87b4b6c85c97a0e\nparent 2c2cec87476f06e32c7b09cedd2c44e0c713f147\nauthor open-swe[bot] <215916821+open-swe[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1780500190 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780500190 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): pass through summarization factory prompt knobs (#3559)\n\nCloses #2622\n\n---\n\nAdds keyword-only controls for summarization prompt, trim limit, token\ncounter, and compact-tool system prompt while preserving model-aware\ntrigger/keep defaults. Brings to parity with class init.\n\n_Opened collaboratively by Mason Daugherty and open-swe._\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <61371264+mdrxy@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-03T15:23:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a663cad8858a78a5d063af0c51bb789bfb1aba2b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a663cad8858a78a5d063af0c51bb789bfb1aba2b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a663cad8858a78a5d063af0c51bb789bfb1aba2b/comments","author":{"login":"open-swe[bot]","id":215916821,"node_id":"BOT_kgDODN6hFQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1395372?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/open-swe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2c2cec87476f06e32c7b09cedd2c44e0c713f147","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2c2cec87476f06e32c7b09cedd2c44e0c713f147","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2c2cec87476f06e32c7b09cedd2c44e0c713f147"}]},{"sha":"2c2cec87476f06e32c7b09cedd2c44e0c713f147","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJjMmNlYzg3NDc2ZjA2ZTMyYzdiMDljZWRkMmM0NGUwYzcxM2YxNDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ninaad R. Rao","email":"35262832+NinaadRao@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-03T15:08:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T15:08:18Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): guard empty binary reads with empty-content warning (#3675)\n\nFixes #3664\n\n---\n\nEmpty binary file reads now return the same `\"System reminder: File\nexists but has empty contents\"` warning that empty text reads already\nproduce, instead of silently emitting a degenerate `{\"type\": \"file\",\n\"base64\": \"\", ...}` content block with `status=\"success\"`.\n\nPreviously the `check_empty_content` guard only ran on the text branch\nof `_handle_read_result`, so empty binary reads fell through to a\ndegenerate content block. The fix lifts the guard above the\nencoding/type routing into a single check, so empty files return the\nwarning uniformly whether the extension is a known binary type (e.g.\n`.pdf`), unmapped (e.g. `.docx`), or text.\n\n## Social handles (optional)\nLinkedIn: https://linkedin.com/in/ninaadrao\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"058bdfaaaa06c9fd970818efa39104f6b8126596","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/058bdfaaaa06c9fd970818efa39104f6b8126596"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2c2cec87476f06e32c7b09cedd2c44e0c713f147","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIENiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt6EQAAs1k7j92fzykCQPbZ13lOQP\nSFBMZp9R+X5/Z3MKUl/dv4x/DbzivihS1AD9nnylIln1gTHKdFqb2ptDVdVOVv7v\n2Es5VJL/p9M9OpPfDsqTaYo5OkLOruzal8qj6PO2KdvGdjT27N3son+N0q12gRN7\nyL/lKy1sU6jmecfoemj/SbD26lqsmB6Aubc59Cp8VzuiLUFn7czqvfJ3o6wAf4xs\nUthiHPwA3mcYOANgsLqVKpaA80njOxNj14W6cSrsdtIc9Qe8GXUADnLGrWX3cZwV\nFOtwNtOVkrOy6G1mfltde+1/4Xk01xS6yeHJ9HhVVbhlBwyF8lNGZ53nnYHqINz/\n2kCUu1fkGwGKopVVGX8VFNXwlF1CtG45io3yyviRVJSDCUbV5PjOG1nZuJgVpI3q\n9e3Ba76cRMINX1P8+SgtZ/Y9BrhQzwX6ou0TZXTiCd0h6SmNOUs1CSXcVQ2nMswq\ncQrSbOavRZv/GnpPDbYhk9YQRHPgh7ZwnLDMsEScmYfQdDaXMODQVdNudQw6gWlj\nSgquJjmAio/ZiKTm57JS3YGuAYSYf7T4DmX+UfFfpXVCH858mqU1l6tUnFnl4cOW\ntgD/lQk3JeCkt3et5zpq4dkGYzQVl44nK78bPaQn8+utchTFquLOruO97ApCSQtO\nkGhgJsveovqQQlBbs6aX\n=aEIL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 058bdfaaaa06c9fd970818efa39104f6b8126596\nparent d9e4976826ae2281e90e06facb5a70a785703029\nauthor Ninaad R. Rao <35262832+NinaadRao@users.noreply.github.com> 1780499298 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780499298 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): guard empty binary reads with empty-content warning (#3675)\n\nFixes #3664\n\n---\n\nEmpty binary file reads now return the same `\"System reminder: File\nexists but has empty contents\"` warning that empty text reads already\nproduce, instead of silently emitting a degenerate `{\"type\": \"file\",\n\"base64\": \"\", ...}` content block with `status=\"success\"`.\n\nPreviously the `check_empty_content` guard only ran on the text branch\nof `_handle_read_result`, so empty binary reads fell through to a\ndegenerate content block. The fix lifts the guard above the\nencoding/type routing into a single check, so empty files return the\nwarning uniformly whether the extension is a known binary type (e.g.\n`.pdf`), unmapped (e.g. `.docx`), or text.\n\n## Social handles (optional)\nLinkedIn: https://linkedin.com/in/ninaadrao\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-03T15:08:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2c2cec87476f06e32c7b09cedd2c44e0c713f147","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2c2cec87476f06e32c7b09cedd2c44e0c713f147","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2c2cec87476f06e32c7b09cedd2c44e0c713f147/comments","author":{"login":"NinaadRao","id":35262832,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjYyODMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35262832?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao","html_url":"https://github.com/NinaadRao","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d9e4976826ae2281e90e06facb5a70a785703029","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d9e4976826ae2281e90e06facb5a70a785703029","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d9e4976826ae2281e90e06facb5a70a785703029"}]},{"sha":"d9e4976826ae2281e90e06facb5a70a785703029","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQ5ZTQ5NzY4MjZhZTIyODFlOTBlMDZmYWNiNWE3MGE3ODU3MDMwMjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Devin Lai","email":"161107414+devin-lai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-03T14:59:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T14:59:16Z"},"message":"fix(code): add terminal progress preference (#3728)\n\nFixes #3683\n\n---\n\nAdds a `terminal_progress` UI config preference so users can disable\n`OSC 9;4` taskbar progress without turning off every terminal escape.\nThe preference defaults to enabled and falls back to the existing\nbehavior when config is missing or malformed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"c193ca883816526baa5ee53cf092a78fdbbbaf22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c193ca883816526baa5ee53cf092a78fdbbbaf22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d9e4976826ae2281e90e06facb5a70a785703029","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIEFECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt0kQAFz6CaY4LpPENLf66tXYKh4u\nycTQDCps46D+QtKfcB/aPw1vktNx7EHKFaYX8T7zfm2JgFOs/tGmTC0x8pgyMH1S\n49hOTQS2sb+8z1ZtE1HwNwpkgws9gEKnM4nby6BO7NL0XbPOxLjbGhHHAtizo8o1\n6lUGQZdY4fa1r96lmbshk622yYM6eJLmAxMXCPYKu7aXNax7HgN7UJNF+F2b+BAo\nN1wl4CPGqFX3lhE2wH7Ga2ENTIYaBUk9QQ7xy4/38NUZ6P+ac6EDC34WbjOAuY2I\ntqv0BKlWm02JCmZUKnPDG+W9pgBrqu0QFVDqN39k1R5s6wV/JgO00w6eNeSm6o3E\nwCtGRmG2yGCLsghUfTZBXoeS8gOP3QfGj89IAOhduaUbbrv4760Uvx0mBoQNE+1H\n4wO6PMy/LpJ51XomzK4kDu+uztpD/0tI1sEKSHW4UovVn+Xc2ne0B0lXy9ETUWyj\njRj/h2vDviQvyaNBKzTKYkVdcMKZCUa7c9jF8UBASmaLGyvW0hwGy89CYaVpo6nN\nK6BxTlLuBHB5OyLK+M4LuICdT+uCW+LnuIFH7DvXafs+ATrT75i/vxEVIvygk931\nY1Qt94khRphzZ2AnMZL77tGWTN3AR2sKafDX4GItV/eSDY3uV9oX2m2qr1KP4H8P\ndl+S7EUna8EdBSBNsBed\n=xC7U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c193ca883816526baa5ee53cf092a78fdbbbaf22\nparent a090162ea9fd950c54fac874b8a165ca770fd2dc\nauthor Devin Lai <161107414+devin-lai@users.noreply.github.com> 1780498756 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780498756 -0400\n\nfix(code): add terminal progress preference (#3728)\n\nFixes #3683\n\n---\n\nAdds a `terminal_progress` UI config preference so users can disable\n`OSC 9;4` taskbar progress without turning off every terminal escape.\nThe preference defaults to enabled and falls back to the existing\nbehavior when config is missing or malformed.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-03T14:59:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d9e4976826ae2281e90e06facb5a70a785703029","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d9e4976826ae2281e90e06facb5a70a785703029","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d9e4976826ae2281e90e06facb5a70a785703029/comments","author":{"login":"devin-lai","id":161107414,"node_id":"U_kgDOCZpN1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161107414?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/devin-lai","html_url":"https://github.com/devin-lai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devin-lai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devin-lai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devin-lai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devin-lai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devin-lai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devin-lai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devin-lai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devin-lai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devin-lai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a090162ea9fd950c54fac874b8a165ca770fd2dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a090162ea9fd950c54fac874b8a165ca770fd2dc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a090162ea9fd950c54fac874b8a165ca770fd2dc"}]},{"sha":"a090162ea9fd950c54fac874b8a165ca770fd2dc","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGEwOTAxNjJlYTlmZDk1MGM1NGZhYzg3NGI4YTE2NWNhNzcwZmQyZGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-03T14:58:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T14:58:58Z"},"message":"feat(sdk): add interrupt mode to filesystem permissions (#3505)\n\n## Example\n\n```python\nfrom deepagents import create_deep_agent\nfrom deepagents.middleware.filesystem import FilesystemPermission\n\nagent = create_deep_agent(\n    model=\"anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-5\",\n    permissions=[\n        # Pause for human approval on any write under /secrets/**\n        FilesystemPermission(\n            operations=[\"write\", \"edit\"],\n            paths=[\"/secrets/**\"],\n            mode=\"interrupt\",\n        ),\n    ],\n)\n```\n\nWhen the agent calls a filesystem tool whose access matches an\ninterrupt-mode rule, the run pauses for approval via\n`HumanInTheLoopMiddleware` instead of erroring (`mode=\"deny\"`) or\nrunning silently (`mode=\"allow\"`). HITL is auto-installed whenever any\nrule uses `mode=\"interrupt\"`.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Adds `mode=\"interrupt\"` to `FilesystemPermission` — matching tool\ncalls pause for human approval via `HumanInTheLoopMiddleware` instead of\nerroring out or running silently.\n- `create_deep_agent` auto-installs HITL when any interrupt-mode rule is\npresent and merges generated `interrupt_on` entries with the caller's\n`interrupt_on` (caller wins per tool name). Wired at all three sites:\nmain agent, general-purpose subagent, and declarative subagents.\n- Uses the `when` predicate on `InterruptOnConfig`\n(langchain-ai/langchain#37579), so interrupts fire per matching\npath/subtree rather than per tool name. The gate is **scope-aware** per\ntool, so it fires precisely without leaking protected paths.\n- The interrupt offers the approver the full decision set — `approve` /\n`edit` / `reject` / `respond` — matching langchain's default for\nuser-supplied `interrupt_on` tools.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- `deepagents/middleware/filesystem.py`\n  - `FilesystemPermission.mode: Literal[\"allow\", \"deny\", \"interrupt\"]`.\n- `_check_fs_permission` returns the matched rule's mode (first-match\nprecedence — list a `deny` before an `interrupt` if you want deny to\nwin).\n- Result-filtering helpers (`_filter_paths_by_permission`,\n`_filter_file_infos_by_permission`,\n`_filter_grep_matches_by_permission`) drop only `deny` matches;\ninterrupt-mode paths remain in `ls`/`glob`/`grep` output because the\nHITL gate fires **before** execution (the predicate), so an approved\nbulk listing still returns its results.\n- `deepagents/middleware/_fs_interrupt.py` (new) — the HITL glue, kept\nout of `FilesystemMiddleware` since only graph assembly needs it.\n`_FS_TOOL_PATH_ARGS` tags each tool with a `ToolScope`, and\n`_build_interrupt_on_from_permissions(rules)` returns a `{tool_name:\nInterruptOnConfig}` map with a scope-aware `when` predicate:\n- **exact** (`read_file` / `write_file` / `edit_file`) — fires iff the\ncall's literal path matches an interrupt-mode rule.\n- **bulk** (`ls` / `glob` / `grep`) — fires iff the call's search\nsubtree could intersect an interrupt-mode rule. A pathless call\n(`grep(path=None)`) and current-directory aliases (`.`, `\"\"`, `./`) fire\nunconditionally because they can't be localized; `glob`'s `pattern` is\nalso gated, since an absolute pattern (or `..` traversal) redirects the\nsearch root independently of `path`.\n- `deepagents/backends/utils.py` — generic path helpers `_glob_anchor`\n(longest wildcard-free prefix of a glob) and `_paths_overlap`\n(component-aware subtree intersection), alongside `validate_path` /\n`to_posix_path`.\n- `deepagents/graph.py` — merges fs-derived configs with `interrupt_on`\nand conditionally adds `HumanInTheLoopMiddleware` for the main agent, GP\nsubagent, and declarative subagents.\n\n## Security hardening (from review)\n\nCorridor flagged, and this PR closes, three HITL-bypass shapes for bulk\ntools — each with a regression test:\n\n- **Pathless `grep`** (`grep(path=None)`) — the predicate now fires\nunconditionally when the call can't be localized.\n- **Current-directory aliases** (`.` / `\"\"` / `./`, which\n`validate_path` normalizes to `/.`) — collapsed to `/` so the\nroot-overlaps-everything branch fires.\n- **Absolute / `..` glob `pattern`** (`glob(pattern=\"/secrets/**\",\npath=\"/workspace\")`) — Python's `glob` ignores the working directory for\nabsolute patterns, so the predicate now gates `pattern` in addition to\n`path`.\n\n## Dependency\n\nThis needs the `when` predicate / `interrupt_mode` on\n`HumanInTheLoopMiddleware`, which shipped in **langchain 1.3.3**. No git\noverride or branch pin — the dependency uses the released package:\n\n```toml\n\"langchain>=1.3.3,<2.0.0\",\n```\n\n(The earlier `[tool.uv.sources]` override that pinned `langchain` to the\n`sr/hitl-refactor` branch has been removed now that\nlangchain-ai/langchain#37579 is merged and released.)\n\nThe smoke-test snapshots track langchain's released tool descriptions\n(e.g. the `write_todos` description).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `make test` — 1727 passed, 90 skipped, 4 xfailed\n- [x] `make lint` — clean (ruff + ty)\n- [x] Unit tests in `tests/unit_tests/test_permissions.py` cover:\n  - The `\"interrupt\"` literal on the dataclass.\n- `_check_fs_permission` returns `\"interrupt\"` on match and\n`deny`-before-`interrupt` precedence.\n- `_filter_paths_by_permission` keeps interrupt paths (only deny is\nfiltered).\n- `_build_interrupt_on_from_permissions` registers only the tools whose\nop could be triggered.\n- The scope-aware `when` predicate: **exact** behavior, **bulk** subtree\noverlap, `_glob_anchor` / `_paths_overlap` edge cases (root, equal,\nancestor, descendant, prefix lookalike, disjoint), and all three bypass\nregressions above (pathless, current-dir aliases, absolute/`..` glob\npatterns).","tree":{"sha":"87042ee1f10d301757763b97963d1f550c322f8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/87042ee1f10d301757763b97963d1f550c322f8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a090162ea9fd950c54fac874b8a165ca770fd2dc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIEEyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARsAQACP9SnvuxjRPSgAu0IEB9kNa\nZXpwXITqYavQQ5+G7a4nvOsSu81S6XA2eX1CNKr7l3chNpS1dCPWAu95fJ9cIU3c\nVOziTA1PaC/FLHmPhgXMgMU5eu9rpgjfeF0TeFaCr2/2s+Rn6fi2fHXkuVuZ/HH1\nhBTlA/+ZQ4qqG+rgU3KnscPt3+2syVbRCBwbGzU8MgZ+24pMAPPcC7mZ7XNmW2UL\nhvfFKCKuEuf0yCBLqtuH1d07hT15q+v+vEoXVQsUHR00hT3xv35Kv2N/hTN+Ag7y\n4xbYgn21fTvOVLJNhwH8s8nzk5HkprkzOKZEMK1p3XiEQQHmUgN8vCtr8anzzIjQ\nzc9RtQ3DIRaDkejf32wr2PD5/Ck2TJMshugf72VeE9CGplNTMy3uyCKq2oscKvjX\nIGK023zppqkeVUP7s4hFoNr3ioxBg1PXKvsqu22shfEpi26mHvs1zwlilOQWRFqB\npmcnsoS9dqMKga3Ti7QsEZgv1a2a3aFsUPs+prxNVeb5TXzJKGIq/QGqjXqzJkRv\n7XBX9DAlDdPTiOlY66G3cgv3qJuzrTh/ez6BK1ERS8uV+7CHUkLiSgBrv8TLMK+2\nEwFSMvTN/4EmDt8BnYxKyBXUcGy8yNcc3XUqa5b/ixyaYG3IJ+Qb+HIFqj1BR/IM\nRx0lskGEAmBKRyd88u7F\n=UPcS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 87042ee1f10d301757763b97963d1f550c322f8a\nparent e052e089934661b96ae3f65974742de7fd2c6d6f\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1780498738 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780498738 -0400\n\nfeat(sdk): add interrupt mode to filesystem permissions (#3505)\n\n## Example\n\n```python\nfrom deepagents import create_deep_agent\nfrom deepagents.middleware.filesystem import FilesystemPermission\n\nagent = create_deep_agent(\n    model=\"anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-5\",\n    permissions=[\n        # Pause for human approval on any write under /secrets/**\n        FilesystemPermission(\n            operations=[\"write\", \"edit\"],\n            paths=[\"/secrets/**\"],\n            mode=\"interrupt\",\n        ),\n    ],\n)\n```\n\nWhen the agent calls a filesystem tool whose access matches an\ninterrupt-mode rule, the run pauses for approval via\n`HumanInTheLoopMiddleware` instead of erroring (`mode=\"deny\"`) or\nrunning silently (`mode=\"allow\"`). HITL is auto-installed whenever any\nrule uses `mode=\"interrupt\"`.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Adds `mode=\"interrupt\"` to `FilesystemPermission` — matching tool\ncalls pause for human approval via `HumanInTheLoopMiddleware` instead of\nerroring out or running silently.\n- `create_deep_agent` auto-installs HITL when any interrupt-mode rule is\npresent and merges generated `interrupt_on` entries with the caller's\n`interrupt_on` (caller wins per tool name). Wired at all three sites:\nmain agent, general-purpose subagent, and declarative subagents.\n- Uses the `when` predicate on `InterruptOnConfig`\n(langchain-ai/langchain#37579), so interrupts fire per matching\npath/subtree rather than per tool name. The gate is **scope-aware** per\ntool, so it fires precisely without leaking protected paths.\n- The interrupt offers the approver the full decision set — `approve` /\n`edit` / `reject` / `respond` — matching langchain's default for\nuser-supplied `interrupt_on` tools.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- `deepagents/middleware/filesystem.py`\n  - `FilesystemPermission.mode: Literal[\"allow\", \"deny\", \"interrupt\"]`.\n- `_check_fs_permission` returns the matched rule's mode (first-match\nprecedence — list a `deny` before an `interrupt` if you want deny to\nwin).\n- Result-filtering helpers (`_filter_paths_by_permission`,\n`_filter_file_infos_by_permission`,\n`_filter_grep_matches_by_permission`) drop only `deny` matches;\ninterrupt-mode paths remain in `ls`/`glob`/`grep` output because the\nHITL gate fires **before** execution (the predicate), so an approved\nbulk listing still returns its results.\n- `deepagents/middleware/_fs_interrupt.py` (new) — the HITL glue, kept\nout of `FilesystemMiddleware` since only graph assembly needs it.\n`_FS_TOOL_PATH_ARGS` tags each tool with a `ToolScope`, and\n`_build_interrupt_on_from_permissions(rules)` returns a `{tool_name:\nInterruptOnConfig}` map with a scope-aware `when` predicate:\n- **exact** (`read_file` / `write_file` / `edit_file`) — fires iff the\ncall's literal path matches an interrupt-mode rule.\n- **bulk** (`ls` / `glob` / `grep`) — fires iff the call's search\nsubtree could intersect an interrupt-mode rule. A pathless call\n(`grep(path=None)`) and current-directory aliases (`.`, `\"\"`, `./`) fire\nunconditionally because they can't be localized; `glob`'s `pattern` is\nalso gated, since an absolute pattern (or `..` traversal) redirects the\nsearch root independently of `path`.\n- `deepagents/backends/utils.py` — generic path helpers `_glob_anchor`\n(longest wildcard-free prefix of a glob) and `_paths_overlap`\n(component-aware subtree intersection), alongside `validate_path` /\n`to_posix_path`.\n- `deepagents/graph.py` — merges fs-derived configs with `interrupt_on`\nand conditionally adds `HumanInTheLoopMiddleware` for the main agent, GP\nsubagent, and declarative subagents.\n\n## Security hardening (from review)\n\nCorridor flagged, and this PR closes, three HITL-bypass shapes for bulk\ntools — each with a regression test:\n\n- **Pathless `grep`** (`grep(path=None)`) — the predicate now fires\nunconditionally when the call can't be localized.\n- **Current-directory aliases** (`.` / `\"\"` / `./`, which\n`validate_path` normalizes to `/.`) — collapsed to `/` so the\nroot-overlaps-everything branch fires.\n- **Absolute / `..` glob `pattern`** (`glob(pattern=\"/secrets/**\",\npath=\"/workspace\")`) — Python's `glob` ignores the working directory for\nabsolute patterns, so the predicate now gates `pattern` in addition to\n`path`.\n\n## Dependency\n\nThis needs the `when` predicate / `interrupt_mode` on\n`HumanInTheLoopMiddleware`, which shipped in **langchain 1.3.3**. No git\noverride or branch pin — the dependency uses the released package:\n\n```toml\n\"langchain>=1.3.3,<2.0.0\",\n```\n\n(The earlier `[tool.uv.sources]` override that pinned `langchain` to the\n`sr/hitl-refactor` branch has been removed now that\nlangchain-ai/langchain#37579 is merged and released.)\n\nThe smoke-test snapshots track langchain's released tool descriptions\n(e.g. the `write_todos` description).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `make test` — 1727 passed, 90 skipped, 4 xfailed\n- [x] `make lint` — clean (ruff + ty)\n- [x] Unit tests in `tests/unit_tests/test_permissions.py` cover:\n  - The `\"interrupt\"` literal on the dataclass.\n- `_check_fs_permission` returns `\"interrupt\"` on match and\n`deny`-before-`interrupt` precedence.\n- `_filter_paths_by_permission` keeps interrupt paths (only deny is\nfiltered).\n- `_build_interrupt_on_from_permissions` registers only the tools whose\nop could be triggered.\n- The scope-aware `when` predicate: **exact** behavior, **bulk** subtree\noverlap, `_glob_anchor` / `_paths_overlap` edge cases (root, equal,\nancestor, descendant, prefix lookalike, disjoint), and all three bypass\nregressions above (pathless, current-dir aliases, absolute/`..` glob\npatterns).","verified_at":"2026-06-03T14:58:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a090162ea9fd950c54fac874b8a165ca770fd2dc","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a090162ea9fd950c54fac874b8a165ca770fd2dc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a090162ea9fd950c54fac874b8a165ca770fd2dc/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e052e089934661b96ae3f65974742de7fd2c6d6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e052e089934661b96ae3f65974742de7fd2c6d6f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e052e089934661b96ae3f65974742de7fd2c6d6f"}]},{"sha":"e052e089934661b96ae3f65974742de7fd2c6d6f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGUwNTJlMDg5OTM0NjYxYjk2YWUzZjY1OTc0NzQyZGU3ZmQyYzZkNmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-02T22:43:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:43:11Z"},"message":"docs(code): fix env var name in instructions (#3725)","tree":{"sha":"75ca0362a0b1b1b6d70af46ca4ff904edd815d0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/75ca0362a0b1b1b6d70af46ca4ff904edd815d0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e052e089934661b96ae3f65974742de7fd2c6d6f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH1x/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9I4QAH0oVW3QyZwxWYHMhpH+oEsD\nuaSv+ilHfXl/9zntjOTS4xq4j+ng+zaSyJ6KRTLtDIQXSdlBzBjqN4bgxUHJEBKW\nhwJHTUfgXZn7OzaZdqY0OicrX7SfJCNKCSbUhkzwTKmiY5nzWE+OEpHnUWSaAtZd\nxN7+JN0iZA/821+EMMK2squ8mb/GnAOdx2IZBTJNhNg9kzYrijnm8vHgDd2DK/D8\nP+utcwGRFCDXQiGHnIpQUg0KeBaFzv9WXcZZ57TUU7oo4A822g4F7o/K+oQfXurm\n4UOiQT49vaZjhk6EYjTg20CPlnv6v2QLJeldYLMFJNHhSqPgKks3TzrLYTCTwLZW\nSMZbtTzypvQtcsaLliRw3mL1OLNG50nqPW4Fo+b341ws2QfOKU04Mflho0hGQuWt\nIRha8xN/Ov7tSqbMKhL6TFiNGZB5353BR7VxEehZBqwR9Tw822qzfsFtzi53YN0r\nu8ytDbyZcWUPLhkR9lvXCh15aaauBPcHrFr3zWuspDMmH/4XEZEpFcKgZdxgN6ff\nUJKaAmctm3j+NVMlrB1y8lD8RIc8capvOc5J/bGw5oIu7dZecTgztiPq0YNcg0SU\nqTa+xVWfON/PFfEXrFSITKHoWRKHjEjdk9Fly56mqkpey2euckIkfNOzeqB4Rsw/\nNRxpxhsia3QGfF2kbeVw\n=v46o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 75ca0362a0b1b1b6d70af46ca4ff904edd815d0f\nparent a5107ab6888cac6349c858fd44c6c21c4fe6fe57\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1780440191 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780440191 -0400\n\ndocs(code): fix env var name in instructions (#3725)","verified_at":"2026-06-02T22:43:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e052e089934661b96ae3f65974742de7fd2c6d6f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e052e089934661b96ae3f65974742de7fd2c6d6f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e052e089934661b96ae3f65974742de7fd2c6d6f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a5107ab6888cac6349c858fd44c6c21c4fe6fe57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a5107ab6888cac6349c858fd44c6c21c4fe6fe57","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a5107ab6888cac6349c858fd44c6c21c4fe6fe57"}]},{"sha":"a5107ab6888cac6349c858fd44c6c21c4fe6fe57","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE1MTA3YWI2ODg4Y2FjNjM0OWM4NThmZDQ0YzZjMjFjNGZlNmZlNTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:39:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:39:30Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.8 (#3686)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.8](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.7...deepagents-code==0.1.8)\n(2026-06-02)\n\n### Features\n\n* List valid extras when `/install` has no argument\n([#3695](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3695))\n([c7d529c](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c7d529ca0fc478dec9060ea04bcc8589f9b1cd3a))\n* Add MCP error detail modal\n([#3687](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3687))\n([4ae4754](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4ae475453ce0df6d6b057b7e163396aa27d55143))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Allow recovery commands when startup fails\n([#3706](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3706))\n([727d022](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/727d022cd1526836c3d1de997c1f036e870881f7))\n* Preserve extras during install\n([#3707](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3707))\n([e636ce9](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e636ce9e979fd1c30335ec340acdabbd0a5ae79e))\n* Normalize empty file list tool output\n([#3697](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3697))\n([b67aead](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b67aead2b86e04aaee8f2dbfba7b263e3e23597d))\n* Point MCP re-enable guidance at `Ctrl+R`\n([#3688](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3688))\n([15ca302](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/15ca3029f18fa38c1592859febc2a6d0469bff2d))\n* Preserve MCP token refresh when metadata discovery fails\n([#3685](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3685))\n([afafeeb](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/afafeeb471c4008d4eb4263ec478cf868833fe0b))\n* Reduce OAuth login modal noise\n([#3693](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3693))\n([0e8a780](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0e8a780e2dfea2e22ac44545a16279dbe30eb8ee))\n* Repair MCP OAuth login redirect and stale client registration\n([#3692](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3692))\n([f741293](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f741293524f7d47eb8a16a3cd4def336c3c3c13f))\n* Search all models from `/model` filter\n([#3690](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3690))\n([5fcb877](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5fcb877d094c4504f671bb7aeb52efa7bf3a5b48))\n* Serialize `QueuedUserMessage` as user input\n([#3708](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3708))\n([307d598](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/307d59826da9b1ddcbcdab8dccef6d18ecf16d10))\n* Serialize cold SDK imports\n([#3712](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3712))\n([fb2adc0](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fb2adc0585e978b12646602ba922e252abf41f81))\n* Pluralize singular MCP login splash text\n([#3689](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3689))\n([492b0fc](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/492b0fc9209e13cd7004a255ef67b31b7e78e95e))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"29a96d05bf5f8cead19246352cb762ea9fd82e2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/29a96d05bf5f8cead19246352cb762ea9fd82e2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a5107ab6888cac6349c858fd44c6c21c4fe6fe57","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH1uiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4FMQAFy2uHFU/6S7selcIyhDl+1/\nPMMq+jwmCm0SOlZ6CvPAyPXtzDh0u0FEQnpyvMklIzDosr4qL2PQ1Fgh6BUQMVZt\n6uBTczb+8IHPeXGC2kvUBQfLRbVrYdarCSeIBBdDDWvqnOmCxeoKZtlUd6tU6rKx\nqGQunqgoQ9SVmvbyEgYtPmhVnOT/t0pw3fWLkpmGC2qwPtJUh6KD0p41WbTU9IYq\nkNZYFHDE6MT/1eLl2BVQ+3rTxUBxYShepppSvc41IiOOMZQNGC6D0pVgD6t6TcUA\nlp3nsNF1kFoxLGxn90x21Zl+xtQfGHUtNQoDlLd8Oovx24FJ8Q9lId1wad/Tv1QL\nkkEULCYoCI1pGaR2MpOkvcgpobl5Add9jSjjU72w9fusfhqtYW+oV0GOAJU55Zve\np2p7vtWlbNhlL61LG/I1v/uOx1zt6LkRko18NGiHd+tPTt/Ql/mqiv0ZlYLGikKw\na7mRA7dA/pbh0fD2tLu2FCaRHS2zW6zzkUmxkeNU+sgXpM/UMOfBC8RfT6asC4pi\n24PcPFv8+KwlgYBSO49MwIOzA1kdh0q26W05dKAm2cOAFdNwdxJoOOLxjM+A72mN\nwHkCAooT5otZBoz+AcXccN8LMq5HDXY88igR7nX3bUqfSNPYomSePyx7LtmHDHOm\nD38GpZNDlj63Lh5F0d2h\n=Bnuo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 29a96d05bf5f8cead19246352cb762ea9fd82e2a\nparent 7d33459cbdf2e0fa69e9b40a81b6b8f7038904ee\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1780439970 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780439970 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.8 (#3686)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.8](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.7...deepagents-code==0.1.8)\n(2026-06-02)\n\n### Features\n\n* List valid extras when `/install` has no argument\n([#3695](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3695))\n([c7d529c](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c7d529ca0fc478dec9060ea04bcc8589f9b1cd3a))\n* Add MCP error detail modal\n([#3687](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3687))\n([4ae4754](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4ae475453ce0df6d6b057b7e163396aa27d55143))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Allow recovery commands when startup fails\n([#3706](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3706))\n([727d022](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/727d022cd1526836c3d1de997c1f036e870881f7))\n* Preserve extras during install\n([#3707](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3707))\n([e636ce9](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e636ce9e979fd1c30335ec340acdabbd0a5ae79e))\n* Normalize empty file list tool output\n([#3697](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3697))\n([b67aead](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b67aead2b86e04aaee8f2dbfba7b263e3e23597d))\n* Point MCP re-enable guidance at `Ctrl+R`\n([#3688](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3688))\n([15ca302](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/15ca3029f18fa38c1592859febc2a6d0469bff2d))\n* Preserve MCP token refresh when metadata discovery fails\n([#3685](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3685))\n([afafeeb](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/afafeeb471c4008d4eb4263ec478cf868833fe0b))\n* Reduce OAuth login modal noise\n([#3693](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3693))\n([0e8a780](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0e8a780e2dfea2e22ac44545a16279dbe30eb8ee))\n* Repair MCP OAuth login redirect and stale client registration\n([#3692](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3692))\n([f741293](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f741293524f7d47eb8a16a3cd4def336c3c3c13f))\n* Search all models from `/model` filter\n([#3690](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3690))\n([5fcb877](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5fcb877d094c4504f671bb7aeb52efa7bf3a5b48))\n* Serialize `QueuedUserMessage` as user input\n([#3708](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3708))\n([307d598](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/307d59826da9b1ddcbcdab8dccef6d18ecf16d10))\n* Serialize cold SDK imports\n([#3712](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3712))\n([fb2adc0](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fb2adc0585e978b12646602ba922e252abf41f81))\n* Pluralize singular MCP login splash text\n([#3689](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3689))\n([492b0fc](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/492b0fc9209e13cd7004a255ef67b31b7e78e95e))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-02T22:39:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a5107ab6888cac6349c858fd44c6c21c4fe6fe57","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a5107ab6888cac6349c858fd44c6c21c4fe6fe57","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a5107ab6888cac6349c858fd44c6c21c4fe6fe57/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7d33459cbdf2e0fa69e9b40a81b6b8f7038904ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d33459cbdf2e0fa69e9b40a81b6b8f7038904ee","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7d33459cbdf2e0fa69e9b40a81b6b8f7038904ee"}]},{"sha":"7d33459cbdf2e0fa69e9b40a81b6b8f7038904ee","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdkMzM0NTljYmRmMmUwZmE2OWU5YjQwYTgxYjZiOGY3MDM4OTA0ZWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"bonpiedlaroute","email":"noel.tchidjo@hotmail.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:30:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:30:05Z"},"message":"style(code): allow disabling cursor blink (#3553)\n\nCloses #3503\n\n---\n\nLets users disable the chat input cursor blink by setting\n`[ui].cursor_blink = false` in `~/.deepagents/config.toml`. The value is\nread at startup and applied to the chat input.\n\nThis is config-file only for now.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"c571ee78b9448ee7d97dd7e4898cbb48897f5292","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c571ee78b9448ee7d97dd7e4898cbb48897f5292"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7d33459cbdf2e0fa69e9b40a81b6b8f7038904ee","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH1ltCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANU0QAFOxVNXelODu1Uua6pfx0t71\n3EBTwzoRBzwQKcqNIbrnGIewz0u97ll9ujY/AXdyp/PSTcyVs7+mSqVW2pfF2/Et\n6O8EJWs5GzXsR7LazHkUhtBb01bX1AOa3hOS/NZLNog29VLeWCtnHln74f6Br7qZ\nIJVvq3AkEh6NihbWxqpP7gHG9sZqNZNCItzpxLjp2iQvR91/y6+LoDqe+z8dt8RN\nDfaSNLqF+Csb7G5/mIPic9V3Jn9Jx1U92Azb2YKTZ1UmfGrXNdAjcDU5wPLoNcrf\ngW8xhXbWToN98RuhTL+47ekdWc9/79BZZnXmTrzH9i0lhJAA4Uc2DD+sup2/1waG\nvcsRX+Jd+htHsB44E7eoM88f00oPauvy99bjj2POh2YLKZPgye6LIoToNQut3DiO\ncxml7FO1soVjzqKDDSf3IV+DVEd9p3EZYOpEMRheURmX7bagirSEafhtwbTsHeqT\nq7se2mRPDIHka8BA7F/zWOBvuqLg02e7zsJyJIBEo9ksRTK+MIUtW6r7xfpSm35H\n8YHlFHs/HdLJAvBEuggu2+M7dxwOwB0b5yeLVJvLjqb+L9F08VGTPGwRiOmv2z0K\nxWlU2iZmhfjR4uA47CaNHNZV13y9Bn/58qr6iZlAV2VK7dDd7Y9UJyE7m6taetFZ\ngtdaY+ISpM+7Bo0lq4Tc\n=wP3m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c571ee78b9448ee7d97dd7e4898cbb48897f5292\nparent 665a18e7fe7f291319af6780328384cc658af899\nauthor bonpiedlaroute <noel.tchidjo@hotmail.com> 1780439405 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780439405 -0400\n\nstyle(code): allow disabling cursor blink (#3553)\n\nCloses #3503\n\n---\n\nLets users disable the chat input cursor blink by setting\n`[ui].cursor_blink = false` in `~/.deepagents/config.toml`. The value is\nread at startup and applied to the chat input.\n\nThis is config-file only for now.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-02T22:30:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d33459cbdf2e0fa69e9b40a81b6b8f7038904ee","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7d33459cbdf2e0fa69e9b40a81b6b8f7038904ee","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7d33459cbdf2e0fa69e9b40a81b6b8f7038904ee/comments","author":{"login":"bonpiedlaroute","id":17798880,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Nzk4ODgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17798880?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonpiedlaroute","html_url":"https://github.com/bonpiedlaroute","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonpiedlaroute/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonpiedlaroute/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonpiedlaroute/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonpiedlaroute/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonpiedlaroute/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonpiedlaroute/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonpiedlaroute/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonpiedlaroute/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonpiedlaroute/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"665a18e7fe7f291319af6780328384cc658af899","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/665a18e7fe7f291319af6780328384cc658af899","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/665a18e7fe7f291319af6780328384cc658af899"}]},{"sha":"665a18e7fe7f291319af6780328384cc658af899","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDY2NWExOGU3ZmU3ZjI5MTMxOWFmNjc4MDMyODM4NGNjNjU4YWY4OTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-02T22:18:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:18:47Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): timeout python grep fallback (#1937)\n\nStopgap whilst waiting for #1935\n\n---\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Behavior change to the `grep` tool.** This PR alters grep semantics\nin two ways:\n>\n> 1. **The Python fallback can no longer hang indefinitely.** Previously\nonly the ripgrep path enforced a 30s timeout; the pure-Python fallback\n(used when `rg` is not on `PATH`) walked the tree unbounded. It now\naborts after `DEFAULT_GREP_TIMEOUT` (30s) and returns the matches\ncollected so far plus a partial-error message.\n> 2. **Partial matches are now surfaced instead of discarded.**\nPreviously any backend error caused the tool to return only the error\nstring with `status=\"error\"`, throwing away any matches already found.\nThe tool now returns those partial matches alongside the error\n(`status=\"error\"`, content includes a `Partial matches:` section). The\nclean, fully-successful path is unchanged (`status=\"success\"`, identical\ncontent).\n\n\n`FilesystemBackend._python_search` had no timeout — on large repos, if\nripgrep timed out or wasn't installed, the Python fallback would walk\nthe entire file tree via `rglob(\"*\")` indefinitely, blocking the calling\nthread forever. This was observed in production: a subagent's grep tool\ncall hung permanently, stalling an entire ACP session.","tree":{"sha":"e02305f10f8bceab5338dd2ce902be0a5a261ae5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e02305f10f8bceab5338dd2ce902be0a5a261ae5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/665a18e7fe7f291319af6780328384cc658af899","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH1bHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqeMQACm3IJlnKxRS1IEqtl8SLnwC\nn34/oQRSIswdoS1PwTK0GxzQj1ciwnFIaRjZs0Lsp9hZEHbZmSmlOLLG7FxXUOpK\nB/U/BxhRmVM3gzMKhKA2x3tV3TAyBJwXM9R+vuuGb/3+hJ2841k6gugByb7yPkv2\nrb/wNS8vt4eKqAZNrUGrswY2OxMIYBW7jgIMS8z5bwVXHJor1d6rke6rHtKUQFRX\nzeYGIy8GZvj0HkU+ggCYXY5kYeN8tDWGbLcIdjx0pYq8rEFJEzfbncmskMv/mZ6W\nH2iwhi8uNXsMQgRJCsDpbMfn9I2MGQl9tsup8ZThooJGvgz368zIRa8ZdvLnBrdc\n7SZKKLdEdve4NbvZudFKrm7pP7ZjxouCwkIeLCUUEzbnGtKbRDbY+vvB0Is1HnV1\nYzdnMpNiHV5En3Apc3DYQ0EPQyK7aFfaQ4/7CGh9o5231dE73ewdcvDhCbynjM6Y\nEmNi0NsDjApTYZp4sG+r6h6nIQQZEpLSG4NSbgXNxkHm/kYAKQsNAUQtcscBYbOT\n3Uq9BIemnbMk1ynr9ANxzW0R+FuC0bqSfI2k2x9/GK64iUErNTQuvo67Gz20eRtr\nJ5xLUdjoMFghY1YDOD+sg5fpq9Yq4qcwtMPj0q4koXtRyFtgoh7Onb3sjub3/BUg\nmPn4Nl7ODVF6M+IdV+nq\n=Im8S\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e02305f10f8bceab5338dd2ce902be0a5a261ae5\nparent 4c28760abbbe43117f2118793f11ff9d4f71761e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1780438727 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780438727 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): timeout python grep fallback (#1937)\n\nStopgap whilst waiting for #1935\n\n---\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Behavior change to the `grep` tool.** This PR alters grep semantics\nin two ways:\n>\n> 1. **The Python fallback can no longer hang indefinitely.** Previously\nonly the ripgrep path enforced a 30s timeout; the pure-Python fallback\n(used when `rg` is not on `PATH`) walked the tree unbounded. It now\naborts after `DEFAULT_GREP_TIMEOUT` (30s) and returns the matches\ncollected so far plus a partial-error message.\n> 2. **Partial matches are now surfaced instead of discarded.**\nPreviously any backend error caused the tool to return only the error\nstring with `status=\"error\"`, throwing away any matches already found.\nThe tool now returns those partial matches alongside the error\n(`status=\"error\"`, content includes a `Partial matches:` section). The\nclean, fully-successful path is unchanged (`status=\"success\"`, identical\ncontent).\n\n\n`FilesystemBackend._python_search` had no timeout — on large repos, if\nripgrep timed out or wasn't installed, the Python fallback would walk\nthe entire file tree via `rglob(\"*\")` indefinitely, blocking the calling\nthread forever. This was observed in production: a subagent's grep tool\ncall hung permanently, stalling an entire ACP session.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T22:18:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/665a18e7fe7f291319af6780328384cc658af899","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/665a18e7fe7f291319af6780328384cc658af899","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/665a18e7fe7f291319af6780328384cc658af899/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4c28760abbbe43117f2118793f11ff9d4f71761e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c28760abbbe43117f2118793f11ff9d4f71761e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4c28760abbbe43117f2118793f11ff9d4f71761e"}]},{"sha":"4c28760abbbe43117f2118793f11ff9d4f71761e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRjMjg3NjBhYmJiZTQzMTE3ZjIxMTg3OTNmMTFmZjlkNGY3MTc2MWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mohammad Mohtashim","email":"45242107+keenborder786@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:00:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T22:00:07Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): surface missing path errors in `FilesystemBackend.ls` (#3574)\n\nCloses #3573\n\n---\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Behavior change for direct backend callers.** Code calling\n`FilesystemBackend.ls()` / `als()` directly (not through\n`FilesystemMiddleware`) now receives `entries=None` instead of\n`entries=[]` on **every** failure path — missing path, not-a-directory,\nand resolver errors (e.g. symlink loops). This realigns `ls` with the\nlong-documented `LsResult` contract (`entries` is `None` on failure),\nand the middleware was already null-safe (`ls_result.entries or []`), so\nthe tool surface is unaffected. But a direct caller that assumed\n`entries` was always a list will now hit `None` on these paths. Treat\nthis as a **contract correction**, not a purely additive change.\n\n## Behavior\n\n`FilesystemBackend.ls(path)` now tells callers *why* a listing is empty\ninstead of collapsing every case into `entries=[]`.\n\n| You call `ls` on… | Returns |\n|---|---|\n| A missing path | `error=\"Path '<path>': path_not_found\"`,\n`entries=None` |\n| A file (not a directory) | `error=\"Path '<path>': not_a_directory\"`,\n`entries=None` |\n| A path that errors while resolving (e.g. symlink loop) |\n`error=\"Cannot list '<path>': <reason>\"`, `entries=None` *(was\n`entries=[]`)* |\n| An empty directory | `error=None`, `entries=[]` *(unchanged)* |\n| A populated directory | `error=None`, `entries=[...]` *(unchanged)* |\n\nSo an agent can finally distinguish \"that path isn't there\" from \"that\ndirectory exists but is empty.\"\n\n## Why\n\nPreviously the success-like cases above returned `error=None,\nentries=[]`. A missing path looked identical to an empty directory, so\nan agent calling the `ls` tool would conclude a directory exists and is\nempty when really the path was wrong or gone — a silent failure that\nsends the agent down the wrong branch.\n\nThis also brings the local backend in line with the sandbox backends,\nwhich already surface `path_not_found` / `not_a_directory` errors. Agent\nreasoning shouldn't change based on which backend is wired in.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Only `FilesystemBackend.ls()` changed; `LsResult.error` already\nexisted and `FilesystemMiddleware` already checks it before formatting\noutput, so no middleware changes were needed.\n- `ls()` now upholds a single failure contract: **every** error path\nreturns `entries=None` (the `LsResult` docstring's documented \"`None` on\nfailure\"). This includes the pre-existing `OSError`/`RuntimeError`\nresolver-failure path, which previously returned `entries=[]` alongside\nits error.\n- Async `als()` inherits the fix via `BackendProtocol.als()`.\n- Tests updated in the composite and filesystem backend suites (sync +\nasync) to assert the new `error` / `entries=None` contract, including\nthe symlink-loop resolver-failure path.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"c65cfce6231f8b56bd2317c644676e4830cf14a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c65cfce6231f8b56bd2317c644676e4830cf14a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4c28760abbbe43117f2118793f11ff9d4f71761e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH1JoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm/wQADh5bLmBXEtkbn5WI+27C6Vf\nizTUqAzeY0zjUvLHNgMbYbNh+GdP9qkHoN2jENZnehrkHEIW//1QhE8MUqcbHBVK\nyJhK2vr9HKqvgXO2XZU4/jmt3JV6n+Tx9dr7aJbmbNZRn0MOnlQ3l5NigCat0ruQ\nJkUOt2LrAp0Vi4mJJWLcSeJ3wRbXRumXIo0z4ONG9xqM6lxk4lXZEBPPhSr7SMSO\nJv5PLQiGRb8tnO/yXHoKP5v7wloTon26wTMTg84nukY6ablFuqEBZ4XNHP5ZBBdG\ncNrjcMOP6mr3pHtqPuHffr4vA2ePf8r/4aQXv9DFEpsrjF/Xqai72JNrsIWAEjO/\n8kt2LbTfb7r4A7zAG0/6V8pwXWJqZ+iFDgPgFccJ/0lPaSfqV1qYHEL628wH6hnf\nKzLIFNaB4t4SUZS5pxJGjwRYYJL/AOwFFG7DiDCIYqlioOafA7DpiVd3jkhcvpD6\nSzEfqDEcE9axMgR5K+P3VyKCgF5TBZqXEA5f/aPS0Ezw+8eKS9rYO/47bvRh0uvy\nuiu6MPfP4P3DHnXB8/e9gBFb9uAJSAx7ISbooGPnES0tP0HgR2HPgkbNUAzwhTim\nmHquOMD+ZpowZUB9iw3vS5ou4lPmyeYWr4lW2J4zu5hMrMqWp3CZLhGIJiXqwwwP\nqumBaFseal1t+s3k9aLK\n=ioME\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c65cfce6231f8b56bd2317c644676e4830cf14a8\nparent 3822192a5255706f3ba50d63c67c347c0e02de99\nauthor Mohammad Mohtashim <45242107+keenborder786@users.noreply.github.com> 1780437607 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780437607 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): surface missing path errors in `FilesystemBackend.ls` (#3574)\n\nCloses #3573\n\n---\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Behavior change for direct backend callers.** Code calling\n`FilesystemBackend.ls()` / `als()` directly (not through\n`FilesystemMiddleware`) now receives `entries=None` instead of\n`entries=[]` on **every** failure path — missing path, not-a-directory,\nand resolver errors (e.g. symlink loops). This realigns `ls` with the\nlong-documented `LsResult` contract (`entries` is `None` on failure),\nand the middleware was already null-safe (`ls_result.entries or []`), so\nthe tool surface is unaffected. But a direct caller that assumed\n`entries` was always a list will now hit `None` on these paths. Treat\nthis as a **contract correction**, not a purely additive change.\n\n## Behavior\n\n`FilesystemBackend.ls(path)` now tells callers *why* a listing is empty\ninstead of collapsing every case into `entries=[]`.\n\n| You call `ls` on… | Returns |\n|---|---|\n| A missing path | `error=\"Path '<path>': path_not_found\"`,\n`entries=None` |\n| A file (not a directory) | `error=\"Path '<path>': not_a_directory\"`,\n`entries=None` |\n| A path that errors while resolving (e.g. symlink loop) |\n`error=\"Cannot list '<path>': <reason>\"`, `entries=None` *(was\n`entries=[]`)* |\n| An empty directory | `error=None`, `entries=[]` *(unchanged)* |\n| A populated directory | `error=None`, `entries=[...]` *(unchanged)* |\n\nSo an agent can finally distinguish \"that path isn't there\" from \"that\ndirectory exists but is empty.\"\n\n## Why\n\nPreviously the success-like cases above returned `error=None,\nentries=[]`. A missing path looked identical to an empty directory, so\nan agent calling the `ls` tool would conclude a directory exists and is\nempty when really the path was wrong or gone — a silent failure that\nsends the agent down the wrong branch.\n\nThis also brings the local backend in line with the sandbox backends,\nwhich already surface `path_not_found` / `not_a_directory` errors. Agent\nreasoning shouldn't change based on which backend is wired in.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Only `FilesystemBackend.ls()` changed; `LsResult.error` already\nexisted and `FilesystemMiddleware` already checks it before formatting\noutput, so no middleware changes were needed.\n- `ls()` now upholds a single failure contract: **every** error path\nreturns `entries=None` (the `LsResult` docstring's documented \"`None` on\nfailure\"). This includes the pre-existing `OSError`/`RuntimeError`\nresolver-failure path, which previously returned `entries=[]` alongside\nits error.\n- Async `als()` inherits the fix via `BackendProtocol.als()`.\n- Tests updated in the composite and filesystem backend suites (sync +\nasync) to assert the new `error` / `entries=None` contract, including\nthe symlink-loop resolver-failure path.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-02T22:00:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c28760abbbe43117f2118793f11ff9d4f71761e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4c28760abbbe43117f2118793f11ff9d4f71761e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c28760abbbe43117f2118793f11ff9d4f71761e/comments","author":{"login":"keenborder786","id":45242107,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MjQyMTA3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45242107?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keenborder786","html_url":"https://github.com/keenborder786","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keenborder786/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keenborder786/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keenborder786/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keenborder786/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keenborder786/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keenborder786/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keenborder786/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keenborder786/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keenborder786/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3822192a5255706f3ba50d63c67c347c0e02de99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3822192a5255706f3ba50d63c67c347c0e02de99","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3822192a5255706f3ba50d63c67c347c0e02de99"}]},{"sha":"3822192a5255706f3ba50d63c67c347c0e02de99","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM4MjIxOTJhNTI1NTcwNmYzYmE1MGQ2M2M2N2MzNDdjMGUwMmRlOTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-02T21:59:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T21:59:51Z"},"message":"feat(ci): block lockfile-only release fan-out (#3724)\n\nAdds a pull-request gate for release-please fan-out caused by\nregenerated package lockfiles. The check catches bump-worthy PRs that\nwould accidentally create release PRs for managed packages whose only\nchange is `uv.lock`, while still allowing intentional lockfile-only\nreleases through an explicit bypass label.","tree":{"sha":"2435f325b606b6db927f81e79d2acee7cc5c50c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2435f325b606b6db927f81e79d2acee7cc5c50c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3822192a5255706f3ba50d63c67c347c0e02de99","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH1JXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAy8AQAKlhoGutng453a1uK6Vj6i97\npLIQKqlHF2LOZrfk39IMvJN4+DnKen4pnQHHICfCQCeSeFO/IPUt5fT8THJkN5xB\nQvSRwP7pCQCHkLw56mb5+7pDgLirV1wPcoVYPepVyU8g0EvfsSa26x1omediPw1l\n2uPdfVeTziwSgbouELhIuoqZ6YjhSdq82yI+B+ixUedurZ2wRBIbPTLYGdeESpV0\nzGnOKEIKOhgjGcSiYb20sN7xqSlxnEPvj58dfshTpIaHBJs6TxzUQ0kQxo70y+Cs\neVMbsvBaeiRcNixBIQhEJjShIXjV00MwSQ83pfnIlMPwMkJ5g/NFK4Y0FL14w7Rx\nUIPzapqYIyFiRbDPPdNa0/CvC5tyHhAP1+ceD16bIWRnbjhS3qUBtLKh/lQD8TCZ\nl+IvcjXb3aPsSzIYvg6v0P/kEWuKtuzDDYVosZqPUnzxGO/7XUarbxpyTViSVYLH\nvh2dWHCGziUgnvX7oXGs7NJqhQRvEz5EGGEInBMPVxcAEZVyu814O1kcUdnmyieV\n8fnCNiDe7S98R6rBvOAXQOiEUEPYm0siSv6ewIwilmrRuxkwspMyB/ey01/Qib4i\naDRdVy8Ws2qeCbxLAi4lu5Wj5189AvGnIdfVmdA+PLVBZMbajIBpDLU585uZrh4N\niKmUx0vIOXh3YmLXDxCZ\n=Q5JA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2435f325b606b6db927f81e79d2acee7cc5c50c8\nparent ece8e752059f493254753194bcf59befe54b3556\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1780437591 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780437591 -0400\n\nfeat(ci): block lockfile-only release fan-out (#3724)\n\nAdds a pull-request gate for release-please fan-out caused by\nregenerated package lockfiles. The check catches bump-worthy PRs that\nwould accidentally create release PRs for managed packages whose only\nchange is `uv.lock`, while still allowing intentional lockfile-only\nreleases through an explicit bypass label.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T21:59:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3822192a5255706f3ba50d63c67c347c0e02de99","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3822192a5255706f3ba50d63c67c347c0e02de99","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3822192a5255706f3ba50d63c67c347c0e02de99/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ece8e752059f493254753194bcf59befe54b3556","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ece8e752059f493254753194bcf59befe54b3556","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ece8e752059f493254753194bcf59befe54b3556"}]},{"sha":"ece8e752059f493254753194bcf59befe54b3556","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGVjZThlNzUyMDU5ZjQ5MzI1NDc1MzE5NGJjZjU5YmVmZTU0YjM1NTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-02T21:13:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T21:13:52Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): align `glob` path default with `grep` (#3666)\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **TL;DR:** Omitting `path` in `glob` now searches each backend's own\ndefault root (e.g. `FilesystemBackend`'s `cwd`) instead of forcing a\nliteral `\"/\"`, matching how `grep` already behaves. Explicit `path=\"/\"`\nis unchanged.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Custom backends:** `BackendProtocol.glob`/`aglob` now declare `path:\nstr | None = None`, and the tool layer passes `None` (not `\"/\"`) when\nthe caller omits `path`. Built-in backends are updated to treat `None`\nas their default root. A custom `BackendProtocol` subclass that assumed\n`path` is always a string must add a guard such as `path = path or \"/\"`\nat the top of its `glob`/`aglob` to avoid an `AttributeError` on\nunscoped calls.\n\n---\n\n`glob` and `grep` are paired filesystem search tools. Previously their\nschemas disagreed on the default search root: `glob.path` defaulted to\n`\"/\"` while `grep.path` defaulted to `null`. This makes omitted\n`glob.path` flow through as `None`, so each backend resolves its own\ndefault root instead of being handed a literal `\"/\"`.\n\n**Behavior with an omitted `path`:**\n\n- **`FilesystemBackend`** searches its configured `root_dir` / `cwd` —\nthe agent's working directory, *not* the real OS root. Both an omitted\n`path` and an explicit `path=\"/\"` resolve to `cwd`.\n- **`StateBackend`**, **`StoreBackend`**, **sandbox**, **context hub**,\n**Harbor**, and **composite** backends search their respective default\nroot.\n- Error messages for an omitted `path` now display `<default>` rather\nthan a misleading `'/'`.\n\n**Behavior with an explicit `path`:**\n\n- `path=\"/\"` remains fully supported and behaves exactly as before, so\nexisting callers are unaffected.\n- Any other explicit `path` is resolved relative to the backend as it\nalways has been.\n\n**Schema change:**\n\n- Generated tool schemas now expose `glob.path` as nullable with default\n`null`, matching `grep.path`. Unscoped `glob()` calls keep the same\nruntime behavior.\n\nThis is source-compatible for normal callers. The one compatibility risk\nis code that introspects the Python signature or generated tool schema\nand expects `glob.path.default == \"/\"` or a non-nullable `path` — those\nwill now see `None` / a nullable field.","tree":{"sha":"3537cb075a352ca69377e815f8fc823d07f79865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3537cb075a352ca69377e815f8fc823d07f79865"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ece8e752059f493254753194bcf59befe54b3556","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH0eQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhKIQAJJKLmNSq6QWRzLAwjYNmjqP\n5BnZMuTwYU7GuqS+6aJjNhzSZsF+EaxjdekbGutK6GXHgrHwNXskWJ1c0hpFYbWh\nX+iWYjsHsvZudGDc5pIIx+GL9QAOisrG/nrqcwk7iNWfimFLJTrzsC65MHfib7EN\nH2vIMi+8ssHwg3U/lBfrHqPL30yrQ4vJeQbCEV8WV+8Qh/dRhhGWwCzEhJmvZQQD\nlDvD+bGuXuJ46MRM5O3Dqcx9W7uFZdNgDaoGCMlkF+rvSXOveBkaSGeeVhdk3Jma\ndsci70aqumJgJRnH//PVXAIldBDT1hUAFKrUkQ67cjEJfWnBKZ5FQPl2NOtHktWA\n3uNjVutzO2r1euM4z/YH3eTU0YJxO3+ExEtGSW0KejCD+d2Rt2YneBITgj1OaTGd\nDgBOeDDnyksMoY9x0DnxAqw2SGnCZA8LULmDVZPZ2+tvNqk1U9GOppcE6CxPTGzD\n2OiKNPQKdY4Ux3EpSmI5tc1ZsHtDKes1ADegxbcUJygKydUZYpmqyP4G2UNvjm4R\nwm1nKKTwBP8Tl/0Z2h4ojO9Q1Q/UWIa2R5JqAMvLMiDkRWfrvqXICRww1rbn3O/a\nqkJ1xaQFHIZfRTt19qhZnG96qIjwbDUP9rGgXdPZqC4DYKb9jeMGd3poE38Hol7+\nFuJB8jP8PzdEe2LW6w82\n=qxuW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3537cb075a352ca69377e815f8fc823d07f79865\nparent fd5c154372cc2d9dc9ceea16d091cd351d3fe158\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1780434832 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780434832 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): align `glob` path default with `grep` (#3666)\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **TL;DR:** Omitting `path` in `glob` now searches each backend's own\ndefault root (e.g. `FilesystemBackend`'s `cwd`) instead of forcing a\nliteral `\"/\"`, matching how `grep` already behaves. Explicit `path=\"/\"`\nis unchanged.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Custom backends:** `BackendProtocol.glob`/`aglob` now declare `path:\nstr | None = None`, and the tool layer passes `None` (not `\"/\"`) when\nthe caller omits `path`. Built-in backends are updated to treat `None`\nas their default root. A custom `BackendProtocol` subclass that assumed\n`path` is always a string must add a guard such as `path = path or \"/\"`\nat the top of its `glob`/`aglob` to avoid an `AttributeError` on\nunscoped calls.\n\n---\n\n`glob` and `grep` are paired filesystem search tools. Previously their\nschemas disagreed on the default search root: `glob.path` defaulted to\n`\"/\"` while `grep.path` defaulted to `null`. This makes omitted\n`glob.path` flow through as `None`, so each backend resolves its own\ndefault root instead of being handed a literal `\"/\"`.\n\n**Behavior with an omitted `path`:**\n\n- **`FilesystemBackend`** searches its configured `root_dir` / `cwd` —\nthe agent's working directory, *not* the real OS root. Both an omitted\n`path` and an explicit `path=\"/\"` resolve to `cwd`.\n- **`StateBackend`**, **`StoreBackend`**, **sandbox**, **context hub**,\n**Harbor**, and **composite** backends search their respective default\nroot.\n- Error messages for an omitted `path` now display `<default>` rather\nthan a misleading `'/'`.\n\n**Behavior with an explicit `path`:**\n\n- `path=\"/\"` remains fully supported and behaves exactly as before, so\nexisting callers are unaffected.\n- Any other explicit `path` is resolved relative to the backend as it\nalways has been.\n\n**Schema change:**\n\n- Generated tool schemas now expose `glob.path` as nullable with default\n`null`, matching `grep.path`. Unscoped `glob()` calls keep the same\nruntime behavior.\n\nThis is source-compatible for normal callers. The one compatibility risk\nis code that introspects the Python signature or generated tool schema\nand expects `glob.path.default == \"/\"` or a non-nullable `path` — those\nwill now see `None` / a nullable field.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T21:13:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ece8e752059f493254753194bcf59befe54b3556","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ece8e752059f493254753194bcf59befe54b3556","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ece8e752059f493254753194bcf59befe54b3556/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fd5c154372cc2d9dc9ceea16d091cd351d3fe158","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fd5c154372cc2d9dc9ceea16d091cd351d3fe158","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fd5c154372cc2d9dc9ceea16d091cd351d3fe158"}]},{"sha":"fd5c154372cc2d9dc9ceea16d091cd351d3fe158","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZkNWMxNTQzNzJjYzJkOWRjOWNlZWExNmQwOTFjZDM1MWQzZmUxNTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-02T20:59:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-02T20:59:18Z"},"message":"docs(code,sdk): explain tool-error propagation in the tool-call path (#3665)\n\nCode comments documenting *why* a `ToolException` raised by a tool\naborts the whole agent turn rather than coming back as a recoverable\nresult. The behavior is non-obvious: langgraph's `ToolNode` default\nhandler re-raises everything except argument-validation errors, and\n`create_agent` doesn't expose a knob to change it — so the path from\n\"MCP server returns an error\" to \"turn dies\" spans three layers with no\nbreadcrumbs. These notes mark each layer so the next reader (or agent)\ndoesn't have to re-derive it.","tree":{"sha":"43c843012f4b741c16d7736978a3dbb58362a868","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/43c843012f4b741c16d7736978a3dbb58362a868"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/fd5c154372cc2d9dc9ceea16d091cd351d3fe158","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqH0QmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQEIQAJIsPl/eYrgQO+S4RWXkc8T8\ncgiaXqzd+Sc54218qosFZh5mEdBYhCPHhO0OK8dECGbgOeaGk66mdND2Wcg5hyIn\nyPymkkbUFxNK1qgp4LfR07SIE0WyLrnRmAg5XQn8y7MPfvGrjEetxLtvKv2ffav5\nIsP4Dbq6N07EVRFP6c8P4LJcgWsvbT/LPrmsu0WvEc5kYvpFlX3MzNt3MKWVFWIy\n6aXMFUBYG5MvkHVI9P8XKXDekYrPp4doW0y/3UMAejda1BHhXK2ot8pawMRIC7dl\niYcHTcfXuApB/GPi1VnJD47WsW0uOhuMXXEfGpIXdqL+OVUxaFGETbovUqk9/QtT\n1FtiPfrnuaMRqOB8Wgw+Ijc+cTOiII5fxpNu2Yq8vOBoPoxI9OYMt71wS1Gl2PWK\nql6HocuyD0ua+/p2Q+fFTniaoGTVHwpkxEKGZCEWvK8qsPdQGtp4iBObRvmfJkmt\nyn+7iwJMiOzark39cicWDyoHVgXHGVDriDLZpo0qNRKpGYmvdlggnyNDrq441DKq\nY3RjVqyAFr2wuWfhz/TqzU6VHZzNUiBDzsleevB0odIO1QnEVkmx+IbUcg++rjNI\nCcbOPaYxXIWOAHP9ZTg0zh7hYDKEoZsaSPSOWL5zFu8VI2mOqEGmGXiidvlxiZ6y\niXKSct3cORZ2mLE+Y0fI\n=SGR8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 43c843012f4b741c16d7736978a3dbb58362a868\nparent 983841cca3d083f58eb16aa3cc36b8ae7d218650\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1780433958 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780433958 -0400\n\ndocs(code,sdk): explain tool-error propagation in the tool-call path (#3665)\n\nCode comments documenting *why* a `ToolException` raised by a tool\naborts the whole agent turn rather than coming back as a recoverable\nresult. The behavior is non-obvious: langgraph's `ToolNode` default\nhandler re-raises everything except argument-validation errors, and\n`create_agent` doesn't expose a knob to change it — so the path from\n\"MCP server returns an error\" to \"turn dies\" spans three layers with no\nbreadcrumbs. These notes mark each layer so the next reader (or agent)\ndoesn't have to re-derive it.","verified_at":"2026-06-02T20:59:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fd5c154372cc2d9dc9ceea16d091cd351d3fe158","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fd5c154372cc2d9dc9ceea16d091cd351d3fe158","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fd5c154372cc2d9dc9ceea16d091cd351d3fe158/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"